E["item:battleworn-axe"] = {t="item",n="Battleworn Axe",z="redridge",s="In Redridge, Battleworn Axe blades mark the Blackrock orcs invading the mountains. Marshal Marris accepts the recovered weapons in Lakeshire as proof of the threat to its people.",h="In Redridge, Battleworn Axe blades mark the Blackrock orcs invading the mountains.",sec={{t="Trophy of an Invader",b="Blackrock reavers carry these heavy, nicked axes as they push south from the Burning Steppes into Redridge. Marshal Marris and Lakeshire's hard-pressed town watch collect the blades to confirm another marauding orc has fallen and to show how well armed the advancing warband is.",sp=0},{t="The Threat in the Hills",b="Blackrock invaders have fortified Stonewatch Keep and taken footholds in southeastern Redridge, trapping townspeople in Lakeshire. Taking their battleworn weapons reduces the arms available to the warband and clears roads for Alliance travel.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is a Battleworn Axe?",a="Blackrock orcs in the Redridge Mountains carry Battleworn Axes, rugged weapons worn by hard use. Recovered blades prove that invaders have been slain.",al={"battleworn axe info","what are these axes","blackrock axe"},it="identity"},{q="Who wants these axes in Lakeshire?",a="Marshal Marris, who commands Lakeshire's town guard, wants the axes as proof that the Blackrock threat is being pushed back from town lands.",al={"who takes battleworn axes","battleworn axe quest giver","marshal marris axes"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where do these axes come from?",a="Blackrock orcs throughout Redridge carry these axes, especially near Stonewatch Keep to the north and in orc encampments to the southeast.",al={"where do battleworn axes drop","battleworn axe farm","which orcs have them"},it="origin"},{q="Why are the orcs in Redridge in the first place?",a="The Blackrock clan marched south through the mountain passes from the Burning Steppes, captured Stonewatch Keep, and marauded across northern and eastern Redridge to pin down Lakeshire.",al={"why are blackrock orcs in redridge","stonewatch invasion","blackrock menace reason"},it="conflict"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, each axe brought to Lakeshire marks one fewer invader threatening Redridge's exposed citizens while Stormwind's core forces are elsewhere.",["profession:Blacksmithing"]="As a blacksmith, you can see the resilient, heavy forging typical of Blackrock weapons in these crude iron blades, despite their jagged edges and chips."},kw={"battleworn axe","blackrock","lakeshire","marris","orc","redridge","stonewatch","weapon"},rel={"quest:20","npc:marshal-marris","subzone:lakeshire","subzone:stonewatch","zone:redridge","zone:burningsteppes","quest:19"},src={"Battleworn Axe","Blackrock Menace"}}
E["item:bottle-of-moonshine"] = {t="item",n="Bottle of Moonshine",z="redridge",s="In Darkshire, a bottle of moonshine is sought for Lakeshire’s tavern. Barkeep Daniels needs one while Blackrock orc incursions keep regular supplies from reaching town.",h="In Darkshire, a bottle of moonshine is sought for Lakeshire’s tavern.",sec={{t="A Spirited Relief",b="Blackrock orcs have cut off Lakeshire’s regular supply caravans. Barkeep Daniels seeks regional drinks to restock the tavern for the guards and townsfolk. One is brewed and sold at the Scarlet Raven Tavern in Darkshire, where locals favor strong drinks.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find a Bottle of Moonshine?",a="Find a Bottle of Moonshine at the Scarlet Raven Tavern in Darkshire, within Duskwood.",al={"where to buy moonshine","darkshire moonshine location","bottle of moonshine vendor"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who wants this bottle?",a="Barkeep Daniels, Lakeshire’s innkeeper in the Redridge Mountains, wants the bottle and other regional drinks for his cellar during the orc siege.",al={"who needs moonshine","moonshine quest turn in","barkeep daniels moonshine"},it="target"},{q="Why is Lakeshire running out of liquor?",a="Blackrock orcs have swarmed the Redridge Mountains, raiding roads and severing trade routes. Regular shipments have failed to arrive, leaving Lakeshire’s tavern shelves nearly empty.",al={"why dry times","lakeshire supply shortage","redridge alcohol shortage"},it="history"},{q="What is a Bottle of Moonshine?",a="It is a potent spirit sold down in Duskwood at the Scarlet Raven Tavern in Darkshire. While illicit or harsh liquor might seem out of place in a sleepy lakeside retreat, tough times call for strong drink.",al={"what is moonshine","bottle of moonshine info","what is the bottle of moonshine"},it="identity",add="1eb07341"},{q="Where does this Bottle of Moonshine come from?",a="This particular liquor comes from the shadowed town of Darkshire in Duskwood, stocked by the Scarlet Raven Tavern. With local supply lines strained across the kingdom, publicans look wherever they can to keep their shelves stocked.",al={"who makes the moonshine","where is moonshine made","moonshine origin"},it="origin",add="5d3a7e66"},{q="Why is a Bottle of Moonshine wanted in Lakeshire?",a="Barkeep Daniels needs it to keep the tavern running in Lakeshire. Between the Blackrock orc invasion and disrupted trade routes, the town's liquor supplies have nearly run dry. Daniels sends travelers across human lands to gather strong drink—including this moonshine from Darkshire—to satisfy his stressed patrons.",al={"why does lakeshire want moonshine","why buy moonshine","who needs moonshine"},it="why_wanted",add="08a7d809"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="The trip from Darkshire to Lakeshire shows how fragile the supply lines between Stormwind’s scattered settlements are during the crisis."},kw={"barkeep daniels","bottle of moonshine","darkshire","dry times","duskwood","lakeshire","moonshine","scarlet raven tavern"},rel={"quest:116","npc:barkeep-daniels","subzone:scarlet-raven-tavern","subzone:darkshire","subzone:lakeshire","item:cask-of-merlot","item:skin-of-sweet-rum","zone:duskwood"},src={"Bottle of Moonshine","Dry Times"}}
E["item:cask-of-merlot"] = {t="item",n="Cask of Merlot",z="redridge",s="In Stormwind, Cask of Merlot supplies Lakeshire while Blackrock orcs cut its trade routes.",h="In Stormwind, Cask of Merlot supplies Lakeshire while Blackrock orcs cut its trade routes.",sec={{t="A Taste of the Capital",b="Harvested and fermented in the heart of the kingdom, the merlot comes from the Galina Winery's cellars. The winery lies along the canals bordering Stormwind's Trade District, where winemaker Roberto Pupellyverbos tends its vintages for the capital's refined tastes. Unlike Duskwood moonshine or Elwynn spirits, this wine reflects the craft of human vintners working within the city's walls.",sp=0},{t="Restocking Lakeshire",b="When the Blackrock clan invaded the Redridge Mountains, supply routes failed and Lakeshire lost its usual merchant shipments. With locals parched and terrified, Barkeep Daniels sends willing couriers across the kingdom to refill his tavern's cellars. The cask gives defenders and refugees by Lake Everstill a gentle drink to wash down their rations.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find a Cask of Merlot?",a="Roberto Pupellyverbos sells the Cask of Merlot inside the Galina Winery, along the canals at the edge of Stormwind City's Trade District.",al={"cask of merlot location","where to buy merlot","who sells cask of merlot","stormwind wine vendor"},gp=true},{q="Why does Barkeep Daniels need this wine?",a="The Blackrock orc invasion of Redridge has cut off Lakeshire's regular shipments, and Barkeep Daniels is nearly out of alcohol. He sends adventurers across southern Azeroth to secure regional specialties and keep his patrons satisfied.",al={"dry times quest merlot","why does daniels want wine","lakeshire merlot purpose"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What other drinks are collected alongside the Merlot?",a="Daniels also asks for a skin of Sweet Rum from Goldshire, a bottle of Moonshine from Darkshire, and a keg of Thunderbrew Lager from Grimbooze Thunderbrew in the hills of Westfall.",al={"dry times drinks","daniels booze list","other alcohols dry times"},gp=true},{q="Is the Galina Winery in danger?",a="The Galina Winery is safe behind Stormwind City's stone ramparts. Bandits and orc raids trouble outlying lands such as Westfall and Redridge, while trade and winemaking continue in the capital's canal district.",al={"galina winery lore","winery in stormwind"},it="danger"},{q="What is the Cask of Merlot?",a="It is a substantial container of fine red wine produced and sold in Stormwind City. While ordinary citizens enjoy it as a staple vintage, distant settlements caught in turmoil prize such bulk spirits to keep their weary taverns stocked and local spirits high.",al={"what is cask of merlot","cask of merlot item","merlot cask what is it"},it="identity",add="e882dee4"},{q="Where does the Cask of Merlot come from, and who made it?",a="The cask comes from the Galina Winery, nestled along the canals bordering the Trade District in Stormwind City. It is prepared and sold by Roberto Pupellyverbos, who supplies city patrons and traveling merchants with the winery's sought-after vintages.",al={"cask of merlot origin","who makes the merlot","where is cask of merlot from"},it="origin",add="33c97a45"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, fetching the cask shows the contrast between Stormwind's secure canal district and Redridge's embattled towns under siege."},kw={"barkeep daniels","cask of merlot","dry times","galina winery","lakeshire","merlot","roberto pupellyverbos","stormwind"},rel={"quest:116","npc:barkeep-daniels","subzone:canals-stormwind-city","subzone:trade-district","zone:stormwind","subzone:lakeshire","item:bottle-of-moonshine","item:skin-of-sweet-rum"},src={"Cask of Merlot","Dry Times"}}
E["item:daffodil-bouquet"] = {t="item",n="Daffodil Bouquet",z="redridge",s="In Lakeshire, Guard Parker sends a bouquet to thank Darcy for packing his lunch. Martie Jainrose gathers the flowers, and their choice stirs gossip between the two women.",h="In Lakeshire, Guard Parker sends a bouquet to thank Darcy for packing his lunch.",sec={{t="A Tangled Token",b="Guard Parker wants to thank Darcy at the Lakeshire inn for packing his daily lunch. He asks the town herbalist, Martie Jainrose, to prepare a bouquet of daffodils. Martie says they are her favorite flowers. Darcy recognizes them as Martie’s signature bloom and suspects jealousy. Half-joking, she wonders whether Martie poisoned the stems out of spite.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Daffodil Bouquet used for?",a="Guard Parker sends the bouquet to Darcy at the Lakeshire inn to thank her for packing and sending his lunch while he is on duty.",al={"daffodil bouquet purpose","what do i do with daffodil bouquet","who gets the daffodils"},it="purpose"},{q="Who prepared this bouquet?",a="Martie Jainrose, Lakeshire’s herbalist, gathers and binds the bouquet on request. She chooses daffodils because they are her favorite flowers.",al={"who made the bouquet","daffodil bouquet source","where did the flowers come from"},it="origin"},{q="Why does Darcy react suspiciously to the flowers?",a="Darcy recognizes the daffodils as Martie’s favorite flowers, not a choice made especially for her. She calls Martie a jealous rival and jokes that the flowers might be tainted out of spite, but accepts the gesture.",al={"why is darcy mad","darcy poisoned flowers","darcy and martie rivalry"},sp=1,it="conflict"},{q="Are the daffodils actually poisoned?",a="No. Darcy’s suspicion is theatrical jealousy between the two women in Lakeshire. The flowers are harmless.",al={"is the bouquet poisoned","did martie poison the daffodils"},sp=1,it="danger"},{q="What is the Daffodil Bouquet?",a="The Daffodil Bouquet is a bundle of fresh yellow blossoms gathered in Redridge Mountains. Chosen specifically as an arrangement of Martie Jainrose's favorite flowers, it serves as a token of gratitude meant to be delivered to Darcy at the Lakeshire inn in return for a meal.",al={"what is daffodil bouquet","daffodil bouquet lore","daffodils item"},it="identity",add="d233835e"},{q="Why does Darcy want the Daffodil Bouquet?",a="Darcy did not request flowers specifically, but Guard Parker wanted to return the favor after she sent him a hot lunch out at the Three Corners guard post. He sends you to fetch a bouquet to brighten her day, though she eagerly accepts them to put in water before realizing which herbalist prepared them.",al={"why deliver daffodil bouquet","why does darcy want flowers","who wants daffodil bouquet"},it="why_wanted",add="c8a417a4"}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="As an herbalist in Lakeshire, you may recognize the bouquet as Martie Jainrose’s handiwork. She gathers wild flowers for her trade."},kw={"daffodil bouquet","daffodils","darcy","guard parker","lakeshire","martie jainrose","redridge"},rel={"quest:131","quest:130","quest:129","zone:redridge","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Daffodil Bouquet","Delivering Daffodils"}}
E["item:faded-shadowhide-pendant"] = {t="item",n="Faded Shadowhide Pendant",z="redridge",s="A voice now comes from the Faded Shadowhide Pendant, found in the Redridge Mountains. The Shadowhide gnolls wore it to receive orders from Morganth, and the delayed message is a spell cast by Theocritus.",h="A voice now comes from the Faded Shadowhide Pendant, found in the Redridge Mountains.",sec={{t="A Broken Network",b="The Shadowhide gnolls of the Redridge Mountains follow Morganth and coordinate their movements through enchanted pendants. From his sanctuary at Tower Azora, High Mage Theocritus studied the talismans and devised a spell to breach their magical link. His broadcast took weeks to appear. This faded pendant proves the gnolls’ communication can be intercepted, giving Theocritus a way to disrupt Morganth’s reach.",sp=0},{t="The Mage's Ambition",b="Theocritus wants to study the pendant and learn how its enchantment endured his intrusion. He hopes to refine his sorcery until he can send disabling attacks through matching amulets worn across Redridge. The pendant must be brought to Tower Azora in Elwynn Forest so he can begin his work against Morganth’s hold over the region’s gnolls.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Faded Shadowhide Pendant?",a="The Faded Shadowhide Pendant was worn by Shadowhide gnolls in the Redridge Mountains to receive orders from Morganth. High Mage Theocritus’s broadcast spell has altered this pendant.",al={"shadowhide pendant","what is this pendant","theocritus pendant"},it="identity"},{q="Why does a voice speak from the pendant?",a="The voice is an echo of a spell High Mage Theocritus cast weeks ago. After months of study, he found a way to breach the pendants’ communication link, and the message shows his spell reached the gnolls’ network.",al={"who is talking","disembodied voice","theocritus voice"},it="power"},{q="Who is Theocritus?",a="Theocritus is the High Mage at Tower Azora in eastern Elwynn Forest. He studies dark threats across the border in Redridge, especially the rogue sorcerer Morganth.",al={"theocritus lore","high mage theocritus","tower azora mage"}},{q="Who is Morganth?",a="Morganth is a sinister rogue magic-user in Redridge. He commands the local Shadowhide gnolls through enchanted pendants.",al={"morganth identity","who is morganth","gnoll master"}},{q="What does Theocritus plan to do with the pendant?",a="Theocritus plans to study the pendant’s enchantment in his laboratory. He hopes to send disabling attacks through the network and incapacitate any gnoll wearing a matching pendant.",al={"why does theocritus want it","pendant purpose","weaponizing pendants"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where does the Faded Shadowhide Pendant come from, and who made it?",a="The pendant originates with the Shadowhide gnolls of Redridge and their dark master, the rogue mage Morganth. Morganth crafted or enchanted these baubles as mystical conduits to relay his commands directly to the gnoll packs under his sway.",al={"who made faded shadowhide pendant","where did the shadowhide pendant come from","origin of faded shadowhide pendant"},it="origin",add="6c0e263d"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a Mage, you can see how magical interception can reach even crude or dark enchantments. A disciplined wizard can decode and hijack them.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you help Tower Azora weaken the Shadowhide gnolls threatening Elwynn Forest and Lakeshire."},kw={"elwynn","gnolls","morganth","pendant","redridge","shadowhide","theocritus","tower azora"},rel={"quest:178","npc:theocritus","quest:94","quest:248","quest:249","item:shadowhide-pendant","zone:redridge","zone:elwynn"},src={"Faded Shadowhide Pendant","Theocritus' Retrieval"}}
E["item:fangore-s-paw"] = {t="item",n="Fangore's Paw",z="redridge",s="In the Redridge Mountains, Lieutenant Fangore leads the Shadowhide gnolls against Lakeshire. His severed paw proves his death to Magistrate Solomon, whose bounty seeks to end the threat Fangore poses to the besieged town.",h="In the Redridge Mountains, Lieutenant Fangore leads the Shadowhide gnolls against Lakeshire.",sec={{t="Trophy of a Fallen Chieftain",b="Lieutenant Fangore is a primary field commander among the Shadowhide gnolls encroaching across the Redridge Mountains. He serves the renegade mage Morganth and directs attacks on trade roads, outlying farms, and the defenses around Lake Everstill. Gnoll raiders leave no uniforms, official seals, or banners to confirm their dead, so the township authorities rely on physical proof. Magistrate Solomon demanded Fangore's paw to prove he had been executed, giving Lakeshire some relief amid the dangers closing around the town.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who does this paw belong to?",a="The paw belongs to Lieutenant Fangore, a notorious leader among the Shadowhide gnolls in the Redridge Mountains. He organizes raids and leads forces under the direction of the dark wizard Morganth.",al={"who is fangore","whose paw is this","fangore identity"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Magistrate Solomon want the paw?",a="Magistrate Solomon posted a wanted mandate condemning Fangore as a vile enemy of Stormwind. He requires the severed paw as indisputable physical proof that the Shadowhide lieutenant has been slain.",al={"why collect fangore paw","solomon bounty proof","magistrate proof"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who is Lieutenant Fangore working for?",a="Fangore serves Morganth, a rogue practitioner of dark magic who threatens Lakeshire from his tower in the eastern mountains and directs gnoll activity against the kingdom.",al={"fangore master","who leads fangore","morganth connection"},it="ties"},{q="Where is Lieutenant Fangore found?",a="Lieutenant Fangore operates in the wilderness of the Redridge Mountains among the hostile Shadowhide gnoll encampments.",al={"fangore location","where is fangore","find fangore"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Where does Fangore's Paw come from?",a="The paw is taken directly from the corpse of Lieutenant Fangore, a notorious leader of the Shadowhide gnolls inhabiting the Redridge Mountains. It is not a crafted relic or weapon, but rather a severed physical trophy claimed in battle to verify that the dangerous gnoll commander has been eliminated.",al={"fangore paw origin","where did fangore paw come from","who made fangores paw"},it="origin",add="62ed4317"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance hero, bringing Fangore down and returning his paw gives relief to Lakeshire, a beleaguered town that receives scarce military support from Stormwind."},kw={"fangore","gnoll","lakeshire","morganth","paw","redridge","shadowhide","solomon"},rel={"quest:180","npc:magistrate-solomon","zone:redridge","subzone:lakeshire","topic:gnoll","quest:249","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Fangore's Paw","Wanted: Lieutenant Fangore (quest)"}}
E["item:head-of-gath-ilzogg"] = {t="item",n="Head of Gath'Ilzogg",z="redridge",s="Claiming Gath'Ilzogg's severed head proves the Blackrock warlord has been slain. His fall breaks the leadership behind the siege of Stonewatch Keep and brings desperate relief to Lakeshire.",h="Claiming Gath'Ilzogg's severed head proves the Blackrock warlord has been slain.",sec={{t="A Bountied Warlord",b="Gath'Ilzogg led the Blackrock assault that took Stonewatch Keep, drove out its defenders, and left the valley under constant raids. Lakeshire stood near ruin, while Stormwind sent almost no military help. Magistrate Solomon offered a bounty on the warlord. Gath'Ilzogg fell in the keep's fortified upper levels, and claiming his head breaks the local Blackrock leadership. For Lakeshire, it is the first step toward reclaiming the keep for the kingdom.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who was Gath'Ilzogg?",a="Gath'Ilzogg was a powerful Blackrock orc warlord who led the conquest of Stonewatch Keep and directed raids against settlements in Redridge Mountains, bringing Lakeshire close to collapse.",al={"who is gath'ilzogg","gathilzogg lore","stonewatch boss"},it="identity"},{q="Where is the head taken once collected?",a="The head goes to Magistrate Solomon at Lakeshire's town hall, as proof that the bounty on the town's wanted board has been fulfilled.",al={"who wants the head","turn in gath'ilzogg head","magistrate solomon bounty"},it="target"},{q="What does Gath'Ilzogg's death mean for Lakeshire?",a="Gath'Ilzogg's death deprives the Blackrock invaders of their chief tactician in Redridge. Many Blackrock orcs remain entrenched across Stonewatch, but the break in their command gives the local defense a chance to hold the region.",al={"does lakeshire get saved","significance of killing gath'ilzogg"},it="history"},{q="Where was Gath'Ilzogg found?",a="Gath'Ilzogg occupied the high reaches of Stonewatch Keep, deep within the captured fortification with his personal bodyguards and lieutenants.",al={"where is gathilzogg","stonewatch keep location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the Head of Gath'Ilzogg?",a="It is the severed head of Gath'Ilzogg, the Blackrock orc warlord who directed the assault on Stonewatch Keep and organized raids threatening Lakeshire. Severing it provides irrefutable physical proof that the brutal leader orchestrating the Blackrock campaign in Redridge has finally been eliminated.",al={"what is head of gath'ilzogg","gathilzogg head","head of gath ilzogg"},it="item",add="0b5a65b1"},{q="Where does the Head of Gath'Ilzogg come from?",a="The head is taken directly from Gath'Ilzogg after he is slain within the heights of Stonewatch Keep. Holed up in the fortress he conquered, the warlord plotted further aggression against the people of Redridge until an adventurer braved his stronghold and claimed it as a trophy.",al={"where did head of gath'ilzogg come from","who took gath'ilzogg head","gath ilzogg head origin"},it="origin",add="ca6d6fe9"},{q="Why does Magistrate Solomon want the Head of Gath'Ilzogg?",a="Magistrate Solomon posted a severe bounty demanding physical proof of the warlord's death. Gath'Ilzogg was responsible for butchering innocent humans and overrunning Stonewatch Keep. Seeing his head delivered assures Lakeshire's leadership that the immediate threat has broken, offering vindication and the hope of reclaiming the keep.",al={"why does solomon want gath'ilzogg head","why bring head of gath ilzogg","bounty on gath'ilzogg head"},it="why_wanted",add="a1bebb0c"}},ang={["race:Human"]="For Stormwind's people, bringing down Gath'Ilzogg avenges the slaughter of innocent settlers and the humiliating fall of Stonewatch Keep.",["faction:Alliance"]="With the capital distracted by internal squabbles, Alliance volunteers must defend Redridge and strike down Blackrock leaders themselves."},kw={"blackrock","gath'ilzogg","lakeshire","magistrate solomon","redridge","stonewatch","stonewatch keep"},rel={"npc:gath-ilzogg","quest:169","subzone:stonewatch-keep","subzone:stonewatch","npc:magistrate-solomon","subzone:lakeshire","topic:blackrock-clan","zone:redridge"},src={"Head of Gath'Ilzogg","Wanted: Gath'Ilzogg (quest)"}}
E["item:iron-pike"] = {t="item",n="Iron Pike",z="redridge",s="In Lakeshire, Iron Pike supplies are needed to repair the Everstill Bridge. The shipment from Stormwind was seized by Redridge gnolls, leaving the town short of iron.",h="In Lakeshire, Iron Pike supplies are needed to repair the Everstill Bridge.",sec={{t="Stolen Caravan Cargo",b="Lakeshire spent its metal reserves forging armor, blades, and ammunition after recent attacks by the Blackrock orcs. Builders requested more iron from Stormwind City, but Redridge gnolls hijacked the caravan on the road. They carried crates of iron pikes and rivets north into the hills, stopping repairs on the Everstill Bridge.",sp=0},{t="Rebuilding the Span",b="Foreman Oslow oversees the bridge's reconstruction and needs the stolen hardware back. Without the heavy pikes to reinforce its stone and timber frame, the bridge leaves Lakeshire partly cut off from the northern road and open to further incursions.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why are the gnolls carrying construction pikes?",a="The gnolls ambushed a supply caravan traveling from Stormwind to Lakeshire, then scattered into the Redridge hills with crates of stolen construction supplies, including iron pikes and rivets.",al={"why do gnolls have iron pikes","where did gnolls get iron pikes"},it="origin"},{q="Who needs these iron pikes in Lakeshire?",a="Foreman Oslow needs the pikes to rebuild the Everstill Bridge across Lake Everstill. Lakeshire has no spare iron after melting its reserves into weapons and armor during recent orc attacks.",al={"who wants iron pikes","foreman oslow iron pikes"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where can these iron pikes be recovered?",a="Redridge gnolls hold the pikes in their camps in the hills and ridges north of Lakeshire.",al={"where to find iron pikes","iron pike location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why couldn't Lakeshire just forge their own iron pikes?",a="Lakeshire used its local iron supply fighting the Blackrock orcs, melting the metal into swords, bullets, and protective gear. The town had to ask Stormwind for new iron for construction.",al={"why did lakeshire order iron","lakeshire iron shortage"},it="history"},{q="What is an Iron Pike?",a="An Iron Pike is a heavy iron construction stake meant to reinforce masonry and stonework. Foreman Oslow and his crew need these sturdy structural spikes to repair and stabilize Lakeshire's ruined Everstill Bridge.",al={"what is iron pike","what are iron pikes","iron pike redridge"},it="identity",add="c6b2b586"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, recovering the stolen supplies helps secure Lakeshire's crossings and fortify Stormwind's eastern border against Blackrock aggression.",["profession:Blacksmithing"]="As a blacksmith, you can see how war strained local smiths: all their raw iron had to go toward weapons."},kw={"everstill bridge","foreman oslow","iron pike","iron rivet","lakeshire","redridge gnolls","redridge mountains"},rel={"quest:89","npc:foreman-oslow","subzone:lakeshire","item:iron-rivet","topic:gnoll","zone:redridge","quest:124","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Iron Pike","The Everstill Bridge"}}
E["item:iron-rivet"] = {t="item",n="Iron Rivet",z="redridge",s="Iron Rivet shipments from Stormwind now lie in gnoll camps north of Lake Everstill. Foreman Oslow needs them to mend Lakeshire's damaged bridge.",h="Iron Rivet shipments from Stormwind now lie in gnoll camps north of Lake Everstill.",sec={{t="Stolen Caravan Cargo",b="Lakeshire's iron stores went into weapons and armor when Blackrock orcs attacked. After the assaults eased, Foreman Oslow asked Stormwind for supplies to mend the damaged Everstill Bridge. Redridge gnolls ambushed the caravan before it reached town. They dragged its wagons and pack beasts into the hills north of Lake Everstill, scattering iron rivets and pikes among their camps.",sp=0},{t="Mending the Bridge",b="The Everstill Bridge needs heavy iron rivets to hold its stone and timber framework together under the weight of carts and travelers. Foreman Oslow cannot safely carry out repairs without them. The bridge links Lakeshire to the western valleys, and its repair will help secure the town's perimeter against further incursions.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What are Iron Rivets used for?",a="Foreman Oslow needs the iron rivets to repair the damaged Everstill Bridge in Lakeshire. Its original iron was melted down during the fighting with the Blackrock orcs.",al={"iron rivet purpose","why need iron rivets","what are iron rivets for"},it="purpose"},{q="Why do the gnolls have these rivets?",a="Redridge gnolls ambushed a supply caravan from Stormwind and took its construction cargo. The rivets and iron pikes are now in their camps north of Lakeshire.",al={"why gnolls have rivets","how gnolls got iron rivets","who stole the rivets"},it="ties"},{q="Why was Lakeshire short on iron to begin with?",a="Lakeshire's defenders melted down the town's stored iron to make swords, bullets, and armor during the orc invasion.",al={"lakeshire iron shortage","why no iron in lakeshire"},it="history"},{q="Who is looking for these rivets?",a="Foreman Oslow, who oversees the Everstill Bridge's restoration, is looking for the rivets.",al={"who wants iron rivets","who takes iron rivets"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What is an Iron Rivet?",a="An Iron Rivet is a sturdy metal fastener forged for heavy construction work in the kingdom. Stormwind sent a shipment of these rivets toward Lakeshire to aid in rebuilding the town's ruined infrastructure, particularly the vital Everstill Bridge.",al={"iron rivet what is it","what are iron rivets","iron rivet description"},it="identity",add="0d91405a",nx={6}},{q="Where do these Iron Rivets come from, and who made them?",a="These rivets were dispatched from Stormwind as part of a relief caravan carrying raw materials and construction goods to Redridge. Before reaching Lakeshire, the caravan was ambushed and looted by Redridge gnolls, scattering the iron supplies across their hillside encampments.",al={"where do iron rivets come from","who made iron rivets","iron rivet origin"},it="origin",add="a8a8e120"}},ang={["profession:Blacksmithing"]="These heavy fasteners were forged in Stormwind for major building work, including stone and timber bridges.",["faction:Alliance"]="Recovering the stolen supplies helps Lakeshire repair its infrastructure and curb the gnoll threat to the town."},kw={"everstill bridge","foreman oslow","iron pike","iron rivet","lakeshire","redridge gnolls","redridge mountains"},rel={"quest:89","npc:foreman-oslow","item:iron-pike","subzone:lakeshire","zone:redridge","topic:gnoll","quest:124","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Iron Rivet","The Everstill Bridge"}}
E["item:nida-s-necklace"] = {t="item",n="Hilary's Necklace",z="redridge",s="In Lakeshire, Hilary searches for the necklace she lost in Lake Everstill. Her father gave it to her when she was young, and it slipped beneath the water while she and the other children fished by the docks.",h="In Lakeshire, Hilary searches for the necklace she lost in Lake Everstill.",sec={{t="Lost in the Depths",b="Hilary lost her necklace while fishing with her friend Shawn along the Lakeshire shore. Her father had given it to her, and she treasures the gift. Fierce beasts and aggressive murlocs live in the lake's depths, so local children stay on the docks. The necklace remains beneath the water, buried in the lakebed silt.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who does this necklace belong to?",a="The necklace belongs to Hilary, a young girl who lives in Lakeshire in the Redridge Mountains. Her father gave it to her.",al={"who owns the necklace","nida necklace owner","whose necklace is this","hilary necklace owner"},it="identity"},{q="How did the necklace end up in Lake Everstill?",a="Hilary was fishing by the water with Shawn when the necklace slipped off and sank into Lake Everstill.",al={"how did it get in the lake","why is necklace in water","how was necklace lost"}},{q="Why didn't the children dive in to get it back?",a="Their parents forbid the children to swim in Lake Everstill. Dangerous predators and aggressive murlocs live in its deep waters and threaten the townspeople.",al={"why didn't nida swim for it","why can't shawn get the necklace","why didn't hilary swim for it"}},{q="Who is Effsee?",a="Effsee is Hilary's pet cat. The cat stays by her side in Lakeshire and welcomes the necklace's return with its young owner.",al={"who is the kitty","nida cat","hilary cat"}},{q="Where did Hilary get her necklace?",a="The necklace was a gift from Hilary's father. While it holds little historical or magical renown, it is a treasured family keepsake given to a young girl living in Lakeshire.",al={"who made hilarys necklace","where did hilarys necklace come from","who gave hilary the necklace"},it="origin",add="a22bd4db"},{q="Why is Hilary's Necklace being sought after?",a="Hilary lost the necklace while fishing along the docks of Lake Everstill. Because her parents forbid the children from diving into the monster-infested waters, her friend Shawn asks passing adventurers to brave the lake depths and retrieve the cherished keepsake for her.",al={"why find hilarys necklace","who wants hilarys necklace","why does hilary want her necklace back"},it="why_wanted",add="14f3017c"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Lakeshire's defenders face threats from the surrounding area. Traveling Alliance adventurers can help local children recover lost keepsakes."},kw={"effsee","glinting mud","hilary","lake everstill","lakeshire","nida","nida's necklace","redridge","shawn"},rel={"quest:3741","subzone:lakeshire","zone:redridge"},src={"Nida's Necklace","Nida's Necklace (quest)"}}
E["item:oslow-s-toolbox"] = {t="item",n="Oslow's Toolbox",z="redridge",s="Foreman Oslow needs tools for Lakeshire's defenses, but they lie beneath Lake Everstill. Sent from Goldshire, the chest went down when Blackrock orcs struck its boat with a catapult.",h="Foreman Oslow needs tools for Lakeshire's defenses, but they lie beneath Lake Everstill.",sec={{t="A Fateful Crossing",b="Foreman Oslow needs construction tools to keep Lakeshire's defenses and buildings in repair. Blackrock orcs besiege the Redridge Mountains, and the bridge into town lies destroyed. The tools came from Goldshire, so the shipment crossed Lake Everstill in a rowboat. Blackrock forces struck the vessel with a catapult, sending the boat and Oslow's heavy chest into the depths among the murlocs.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is Oslow's Toolbox at the bottom of the lake?",a="The tools were being carried from Goldshire to Lakeshire. With the bridge destroyed, the shipment crossed Lake Everstill by boat. Blackrock orcs struck the rowboat with a catapult, sinking it and sending the toolbox to the lakebed.",al={"why is the toolbox in the water","how did oslow lose his tools","sunken toolbox lore"},it="history"},{q="Who owns this toolbox?",a="Foreman Oslow owns the toolbox and oversees construction and repairs in Lakeshire. Without proper equipment, keeping the town's fortifications in repair against ongoing attacks is nearly impossible.",al={"who is oslow","oslow owner","foreman oslow tools"},it="identity"},{q="Where in Lake Everstill did the tools sink?",a="The tools rest in a sunken chest near the rowboat's wreckage in Lake Everstill. The chest lies among underwater boulders south of a prominent murloc encampment on the shore.",al={"toolbox location","where is sunken chest","where did the boat sink"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What threats guard the sunken chest?",a="Hostile murlocs and predatory aquatic beasts infest the waters around the wreckage. Dangerous Lake Threshers prowl the deeper parts of the lake.",al={"dangers near toolbox","lake everstill enemies","what is guarding oslows tools"},it="threat",gp=true},{q="Why does Foreman Oslow need his toolbox retrieved?",a="Lakeshire is under heavy siege, leaving the town cut off and desperately short on essential supplies. As the town's foreman, Oslow needs his equipment to maintain and repair Lakeshire's structures and defenses. Because the delivery wagon from Goldshire could not cross the destroyed bridge, losing the replacement tools in the lake stalled critical construction work, making their recovery vital to the town's survival.",al={"why Oslow wants toolbox","why does Oslow need tools","why retrieve oslows toolbox"},it="why_wanted",add="543d5407"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Lakeshire stands nearly isolated under Blackrock siege. Recovering Oslow's supplies is crucial to keeping the town's defenses in repair."},kw={"foreman oslow","lake everstill","lakeshire","oslow","redridge","sunken chest","the lost tools","toolbox"},rel={"npc:foreman-oslow","quest:125","subzone:lake-everstill","subzone:lakeshire","zone:redridge","subzone:goldshire","topic:murloc"},src={"Oslow's Toolbox","The Lost Tools"}}
E["item:parker-s-lunch"] = {t="item",n="Parker's Lunch",z="redridge",s="Darcy packs Parker's Lunch in Lakeshire for Guard Parker's patrol. The meal offers a glimpse of the bonds and modest comforts among Redridge's defenders.",h="Darcy packs Parker's Lunch in Lakeshire for Guard Parker's patrol.",sec={{t="A Meal for the Road",b="Darcy, a waitress at the Lakeshire inn, packs a meal for Guard Parker. He patrols the exposed road south toward Duskwood while Redridge faces attacks from gnolls and Blackrock orcs. The garrison is stretched thin and cut off from Stormwind's aid, leaving guards to keep long, lonely watches. Darcy's small gesture keeps Parker fed and begins a bashful courtship between the two townspeople.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who prepared Parker's Lunch?",a="Darcy, a waitress at the Lakeshire inn, prepares Parker's Lunch for Guard Parker, who is out on patrol. A traveler carries it to him.",al={"who made parker's lunch","who gave me parker's lunch","darcy redridge lunch"},it="origin"},{q="Where can Guard Parker be found?",a="Guard Parker patrols the main dirt road southwest from Lakeshire toward the Duskwood border. He marches back and forth, watching for roaming gnolls.",al={"guard parker location","where is guard parker","find guard parker"},it="target",gp=true},{q="What does Guard Parker do after receiving his lunch?",a="Parker is touched by Darcy's thoughtfulness and seeks a way to return her kindness. He arranges to send her fresh daffodils from the herbalist.",al={"parker lunch follow up","darcy and parker","parker reaction to lunch"},sp=1},{q="Why doesn't Darcy deliver the lunch herself?",a="Gnolls and Blackrock invaders threaten the roads outside Lakeshire. Darcy is an ordinary towns-person, while Parker has the training and armor to patrol them.",al={"why cant darcy bring it","why deliver lunch redridge"},it="why_me"},{q="What is Parker's Lunch?",a="Parker's Lunch is a packaged meal prepared by Darcy, an innkeeper's assistant in Lakeshire. She packed it specifically to sustain Guard Parker, who spends long, grueling hours patrolling the treacherous roads south of town toward Duskwood.",al={"what is parkers lunch","parker lunch item"},it="identity",add="2351e721"},{q="Why does Guard Parker need his lunch delivered?",a="Guard Parker is stationed far outside the relative safety of Lakeshire, keeping watch against roving gnolls and Blackrock orcs along the border road. Unable to abandon his post to return to the inn, he depends on the kindness of townsfolk like Darcy—and passing travelers—to keep him fed on duty.",al={"why deliver parkers lunch","why does parker want lunch","why does guard parker need lunch"},it="why_wanted",add="b73a829b"}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="For frontier guards, a warm packed meal can be a comfort through long hours in the wilderness among hostile beasts.",["faction:Alliance"]="With reinforcements from the capital slow to arrive, townspeople and the few remaining guards support one another to keep Lakeshire functioning."},kw={"a free lunch","darcy","guard parker","lakeshire","parker's lunch","redridge"},rel={"quest:129","quest:130","quest:131","subzone:lakeshire","zone:redridge","subzone:darkshire","topic:stormwind-guard","topic:gnoll"},src={"Parker's Lunch","A Free Lunch"}}
E["item:pendant-of-shadow"] = {t="item",n="Pendant of Shadow",z="redridge",s="At the Tower of Ilgalar, Morganth carries the Pendant of Shadow as he pursues the Scythe of Elune. Theocritus wants the talisman brought to the Tower of Azora as proof Morganth has been slain.",h="At the Tower of Ilgalar, Morganth carries the Pendant of Shadow as he pursues the Scythe of Elune.",sec={{t="Token of a Dark Warlock",b="Morganth, a rogue warlock, holds the Pendant of Shadow at the Tower of Ilgalar. He sought the mysteries of the Scythe of Elune, an ancient relic of immense and volatile power. Theocritus feared the havoc Morganth might unleash upon the Redridge Mountains and the kingdom of Stormwind. The mage sent adventurers to infiltrate Ilgalar, end Morganth's plotting, and take the talisman as proof of his demise.",sp=1,bt={"q94.4"}}},faq={{q="Where do I find the Pendant of Shadow?",a="Morganth carries the pendant at the top of the Tower of Ilgalar in northeastern Redridge Mountains.",al={"pendant of shadow location","where is pendant of shadow","how to get pendant of shadow"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who wants the Pendant of Shadow?",a="Theocritus wants the talisman brought to him at the Tower of Azora in eastern Elwynn Forest.",al={"who takes pendant of shadow","turn in pendant of shadow","theocritus pendant"},it="for_you"},{q="Why does Theocritus need this pendant?",a="Theocritus needs the pendant as proof Morganth has been slain and his pursuit of the dangerous Scythe of Elune has ended.",al={"why theocritus wants it","purpose of pendant of shadow"},sp=1,it="why_wanted",bt={"q94.4"}},{q="What threat did Morganth pose with the pendant?",a="Morganth sought the Scythe of Elune. Theocritus feared the warlock would unleash catastrophic power across Redridge and the surrounding kingdom if he secured the artifact.",al={"what was morganth doing","morganth lore"},sp=1,it="threat",bt={"q94.4"}},{q="What is the Pendant of Shadow?",a="The Pendant of Shadow is a dark talisman worn by the rogue warlock Morganth atop the Tower of Ilgalar in the Redridge Mountains. Tied directly to Morganth's sinister ambitions and dark arts, the pendant serves as proof of his defeat for the wizard Theocritus, who fears the havoc Morganth could unleash upon Stormwind if left unchecked.",al={"what is pendant of shadow","pendant of shadow lore","pendant of shadow info"},it="identity",add="d0e37f9a"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, recovering the talisman for Theocritus shows the responsibility mages bear to stop reckless rogue spellcasters who threaten the realm.",["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, Morganth shows the peril of drawing the Tower of Azora's scrutiny while pursuing volatile, forbidden artifacts like the Scythe of Elune."},kw={"morganth","pendant of shadow","redridge","scythe of elune","theocritus","tower of azora","tower of ilgalar"},rel={"quest:249","subzone:tower-of-ilgalar","npc:theocritus","subzone:tower-of-azora","zone:redridge","quest:1043","topic:warlock","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Pendant of Shadow","Morganth (quest)"}}
E["item:shadowhide-pendant"] = {t="item",n="Shadowhide Pendant",z="redridge",s="In Redridge, Shadowhide Pendant charms pass among gnolls working with Morganth. Lakeshire accepts ten as proof that its law has been enforced.",h="In Redridge, Shadowhide Pendant charms pass among gnolls working with Morganth.",sec={{t="Tokens of Defiance",b="Shadowhide Pendant charms pass among the Shadowhide warriors, brutes, and spellcasters. Deep in Redridge's hills, the clan has gathered under Lieutenant Fangore and fallen under the sway of Morganth, a rogue wielder of the Arcane. To Lakeshire's townspeople, the crude charms mark an organized threat harassing settlements for an enemy of the Crown.",sp=0},{t="Lakeshire's Justice",b="Stormwind law, upheld by Magistrate Solomon, sets death as the sentence for actively aiding a known criminal of the realm. Royal reinforcements are too few, so Bailiff Conacher at Lakeshire Town Hall relies on adventurers to keep the peace. Ten Shadowhide Pendants prove that gnolls obeying Morganth's orders have faced frontier justice.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is a Shadowhide Pendant?",a="A Shadowhide Pendant is a crude charm worn by members of the Shadowhide gnoll clan in the Redridge Mountains. The local magistrate accepts them as evidence that invading gnolls have been slain in defense of the township.",al={"what are shadowhide pendants","shadowhide pendant lore","redridge pendant"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Bailiff Conacher want these pendants?",a="Bailiff Conacher collects the pendants as proof that Solomon's Law has been enforced. The Shadowhide clan collaborates with renegade wizard Morganth to terrorize the local populace, so the town treats every affiliated gnoll as an enemy subject to capital punishment.",al={"why collect pendants","bailiff conacher bounty","conacher quest"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who carries these pendants?",a="Standard footpads, brutes, and rabid gnolls carry the pendants, as do figures such as Rohh the Silent and Lieutenant Fangore in the Redridge wilderness.",al={"who drops pendants","which gnolls have pendants","shadowhide pendant source"},it="target"},{q="What is the relationship between the Shadowhide clan and Morganth?",a="Morganth, a rogue practitioner of the Arcane in the eastern foothills, uses his sinister powers to bend the Shadowhide gnolls to his will. He deploys them as foot soldiers to terrorize Lakeshire and enforce his schemes.",al={"gnolls and morganth","why are gnolls working with morganth","shadowhide morganth"},it="ties"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As a loyal Alliance adventurer, you may be called on to uphold kingdom law. Frontier settlements like Lakeshire receive scant aid from Stormwind's garrison, so local magistrates rely on you.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you face aggressive, physically imposing Shadowhide gnolls. Their ranks test frontline defenders protecting the roads into Lakeshire."},kw={"bailiff conacher","gnoll","lakeshire","lieutenant fangore","morganth","pendant","redridge","shadowhide","solomon's law"},rel={"quest:91","npc:bailiff-conacher","quest:249","subzone:lakeshire-town-hall","subzone:lakeshire","zone:redridge","topic:gnoll","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Shadowhide Pendant","Solomon's Law"}}
E["item:skin-of-sweet-rum"] = {t="item",n="Skin of Sweet Rum",z="redridge",s="At the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire, Skin of Sweet Rum is bound for Lakeshire, where war has thinned the tavern's stores.",h="At the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire, Skin of Sweet Rum is bound for Lakeshire, where war has thinned the...",sec={{t="A Rare Comfort for Lakeshire",b="Lakeshire's tavern supplies are running low as the Blackrock orc invasion cuts off the roads into the Redridge Mountains. Barkeep Daniels needs drink for the town guards and refugees, so he sends travelers to gather regional specialties. Among them is a waterskin of sweet rum from the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find a Skin of Sweet Rum?",a="You can buy a Skin of Sweet Rum from the innkeeper or barkeep at the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire, in Elwynn Forest.",al={"sweet rum location","where buy sweet rum","who sells sweet rum"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who wants this rum?",a="Barkeep Daniels, who keeps the tavern in Lakeshire, wants a skin of Sweet Rum and other regional brews to refill his shelves during Dry Times.",al={"who needs sweet rum","sweet rum turn in","sweet rum quest"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why is Lakeshire running out of liquor?",a="The Blackrock orc invasion has cut trade routes into Redridge, leaving merchant wagons unable to travel safely and Lakeshire's liquor stocks nearly empty.",al={"why are they out of booze","why lakeshire dry","dry times reason"},it="motive"},{q="What other spirits are needed alongside the rum?",a="Barkeep Daniels also needs a keg of Thunderbrew Lager from Westfall, a cask of Merlot from Stormwind City, and a bottle of Moonshine from Darkshire.",al={"dry times drinks","daniels drinks list","other booze needed"},gp=true},{q="What is a Skin of Sweet Rum?",a="A Skin of Sweet Rum is a leather waterskin filled with sugary liquor sold out of Goldshire in Elwynn Forest. It is one of several regional specialty spirits prized across the human kingdoms of southern Azeroth.",al={"what is sweet rum","skin of sweet rum info","sweet rum"},it="identity",add="efbd5e13"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, gathering the rum shows the strain the Blackrock orc invasion puts on the small settlements defending Stormwind's eastern borders."},kw={"barkeep daniels","dry times","goldshire","lakeshire","lion's pride inn","skin of sweet rum","sweet rum"},rel={"quest:116","npc:barkeep-daniels","subzone:goldshire","subzone:lakeshire","item:bottle-of-moonshine","item:cask-of-merlot","zone:redridge","zone:elwynn"},src={"Skin of Sweet Rum","Dry Times"}}
E["item:solomon-s-plea-to-darkshire"] = {t="item",n="Solomon's Plea to Darkshire",z="redridge",s="Magistrate Solomon asks Darkshire for aid as Lakeshire faces mounting threats. His urgent letter to Lord Ello Ebonlocke requests the Night Watch to help defend Redridge.",h="Magistrate Solomon asks Darkshire for aid as Lakeshire faces mounting threats.",sec={{t="A Desperate Call for Aid",b="Lakeshire faces attacks from Blackrock orcs, gnolls, and murlocs, with few reinforcements arriving from Stormwind. Magistrate Solomon sends a formal plea to Mayor Ello Ebonlocke in Darkshire, asking him to send Night Watch militia north into Redridge. With central military support failing across southern Azeroth, human settlements must seek help from one another to survive.",sp=0},{t="Darkshire's Grim Plight",b="Darkshire is already struggling to hold its borders against undead, ravenous beasts, and the darkness gripping Duskwood. The Night Watch is stretched thin, leaving the town unable to spare defenders for Redridge when Solomon’s plea arrives.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is Solomon's Plea to Darkshire?",a="Solomon’s Plea to Darkshire is Magistrate Solomon’s urgent letter to Lord Ello Ebonlocke, Darkshire’s mayor. It asks the Night Watch to help defend Redridge against Blackrock orcs and gnolls.",al={"solomons letter to darkshire","what is solomons plea","lakeshire letter to duskwood"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Lakeshire asking Darkshire for military help instead of Stormwind?",a="Stormwind has sent few garrison troops to its outlying territories amid political inertia and internal strife. Left to face growing attacks alone, Magistrate Solomon seeks help from neighboring human towns.",al={"why ask darkshire","why not stormwind","why does solomon need night watch"},it="conflict"},{q="Who is Lord Ello Ebonlocke?",a="Lord Ello Ebonlocke is Darkshire’s mayor and chief civic leader in Duskwood. He oversees the town and coordinates the Night Watch, its civilian defense force against the dangers in the woods.",al={"who is ebonlocke","mayor of darkshire","lord ello"},it="target"},{q="Can Darkshire actually spare the Night Watch to help Lakeshire?",a="No. Duskwood faces undead, feral worgen, and dark magic, and the Night Watch can barely hold Darkshire’s perimeter. It cannot spare fighters to travel to Redridge.",al={"does darkshire help","will the night watch come","did ebonlocke send guards"},sp=1},{q="Where does Solomon's Plea to Darkshire come from, and who made it?",a="The letter was penned directly by Magistrate Solomon, the town leader of Lakeshire in Redridge. With Blackrock orcs pressing hard against his town and Stormwind unable to provide royal reinforcements, Solomon wrote the urgent appeal himself from Lakeshire's town hall in hopes of securing aid from neighboring settlements.",al={"who wrote solomon's plea","origin solomon's plea to darkshire","who made solomon plea"},it="origin",add="a3b7e1d6"},{q="Why does Lord Ello Ebonlocke want Solomon's Plea to Darkshire?",a="Lord Ello Ebonlocke needs the letter because it formally details Lakeshire's desperate defense and Magistrate Solomon's direct request for military assistance. As Darkshire's mayor and commander of the Night Watch, Ebonlocke relies on official dispatches like this to understand the threats facing their Alliance neighbors and evaluate whether his town can spare guards.",al={"why deliver solomon's plea","why does ebonlocke need the letter","purpose of solomon's plea to darkshire"},it="why_wanted",add="5061acb5"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, Solomon’s plea shows how southern settlements must seek one another’s help while Stormwind gives little support.",["race:Human"]="As a human traveler, you carry a dispatch that speaks to the danger facing Redridge and Duskwood."},kw={"darkshire","duskwood","lakeshire","lord ello ebonlocke","magistrate solomon","messenger to darkshire","night watch","redridge","solomon's plea"},rel={"quest:145","npc:magistrate-solomon","npc:lord-ello-ebonlocke","subzone:lakeshire","subzone:darkshire","topic:night-watch","quest:56","zone:duskwood"},src={"Solomon's Plea to Darkshire","Messenger to Darkshire"}}
E["item:solomon-s-plea-to-westfall"] = {t="item",n="Solomon's Plea to Westfall",z="redridge",s="In Lakeshire, Magistrate Solomon sends an urgent appeal to Westfall for help against Blackrock orcs and gnolls. He asks Gryan Stoutmantle to send the People's Militia while Stormwind's royal army fails to answer.",h="In Lakeshire, Magistrate Solomon sends an urgent appeal to Westfall for help against Blackrock orcs and...",sec={{t="A Desperate Call for Aid",b="Blackrock orcs and hostile gnolls threaten Redridge, and Magistrate Solomon is isolated in Lakeshire. Stormwind's royal army has not arrived in force to defend the region's borders. With no time to wait for support from the capital, Solomon writes to seek help beyond the regular army. Word has reached him of a volunteer defense force forming in Elwynn to the west, so he appeals to the People's Militia.",sp=0},{t="Reaching Across the Border",b="Solomon addresses his message to Gryan Stoutmantle, a veteran warrior organizing Westfall's frontier defense. He hopes Stoutmantle can spare fighters for Lakeshire until Stormwind sends regular reserves. An adventurer carries the document. With Stormwind's outlying territories poorly coordinated, local magistrates must arrange mutual aid on their own.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Solomon's Plea to Westfall?",a="Magistrate Solomon of Lakeshire writes to Gryan Stoutmantle, asking the People's Militia in Westfall to send reinforcements for Redridge's defense.",al={"what is solomon's plea","solomon plea to westfall letter","lakeshire westfall letter"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Magistrate Solomon asking Westfall for help instead of Stormwind?",a="Stormwind's royal troops have not arrived in force as Lakeshire's danger grows. With no time to wait for the Crown, Solomon seeks help from a nearby fighting force.",al={"why ask westfall","why not ask stormwind","why send plea to westfall"},it="motive"},{q="Who is Gryan Stoutmantle?",a="Gryan Stoutmantle leads the People's Militia, a volunteer defense league of local farmers and settlers protecting Westfall from the Defias Brotherhood.",al={"who is stoutmantle","gryan stoutmantle role"},it="target"},{q="What threats are pushing Solomon to send this letter?",a="Blackrock orcs are invading, and gnolls raid throughout the Redridge Mountains, straining Lakeshire's town guard.",al={"why is lakeshire in danger","what threatens redridge"},it="threat"},{q="Where does Solomon's Plea to Westfall come from, and who made it?",a="The letter is penned directly by Magistrate Solomon in Lakeshire, the beleaguered town in Redridge Mountains. Desperate after the Stormwind Army fails to send promised reinforcements to defend his people, Solomon wrote this urgent message himself to beseech nearby allies for aid.",al={"who wrote solomon's plea to westfall","where does solomon's plea come from","creator of solomon's plea"},it="origin",add="7804da1c"},{q="Why does Gryan Stoutmantle want Solomon's Plea to Westfall?",a="Gryan Stoutmantle leads the People's Militia in Westfall, and this dispatch informs him of Lakeshire's dire plight. Solomon hopes the militia can spare fighters to bolster Redridge's dwindling defenses while the township awaits word and troops from King Anduin's court in Stormwind.",al={"why deliver solomon's plea","why does stoutmantle want the plea","what is the letter for"},it="why_wanted",add="6d6e291d"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, Solomon's appeal shows how outlying towns turn to local volunteers when royal troops do not arrive.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you can see how strained rural settlements have become, with the missing king and political neglect leaving frontier lands vulnerable."},kw={"gryan stoutmantle","lakeshire","magistrate solomon","people's militia","redridge","solomon's plea","stormwind army","westfall"},rel={"quest:143","npc:magistrate-solomon","npc:gryan-stoutmantle","subzone:lakeshire","zone:westfall","zone:redridge","quest:12","topic:stormwind-army"},src={"Solomon's Plea to Westfall","Messenger to Westfall"}}
E["item:spotted-sunfish"] = {t="item",n="Spotted Sunfish",z="redridge",s="At Lake Everstill, Spotted Sunfish draw fishers and hungry murlocs alike. The fish bring trade to Lakeshire, though murlocs make the shallows dangerous.",h="At Lake Everstill, Spotted Sunfish draw fishers and hungry murlocs alike.",sec={{t="A Prized Catch",b="Spotted Sunfish bring trade to the Lakeshire piers. Dockmaster Baren buys them from the lake's steady catch, supplying food and commerce to a town under strain. Aggressive murloc tribes prowl the shallows and disrupt fishing. They gather sunfish at their camps, where travelers can take the fish by force.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where are Spotted Sunfish found?",a="Spotted Sunfish live in Lake Everstill in the Redridge Mountains. Anglers catch them in the lake, and murlocs gather them at camps along the shoreline.",al={"where to get spotted sunfish","spotted sunfish location","lake everstill fish"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who buys or needs Spotted Sunfish?",a="Dockmaster Baren buys Spotted Sunfish at the Lakeshire docks. He trades in the fish and pays for fresh stock.",al={"who wants spotted sunfish","dockmaster baren fish","selling fish quest"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why do the murlocs carry these fish?",a="Murlocs along Lake Everstill gather sunfish to feed their growing tribes. They keep their catches at camps along the shallows.",al={"murloc spotted sunfish","why murlocs drop fish"}},{q="Can you obtain them without fishing?",a="Yes. Travelers without a fishing rod can defeat the hostile murlocs along Lake Everstill's shores and take the fish they have gathered.",al={"get sunfish without fishing rod","no fishing rod sunfish"},gp=true},{q="What is a Spotted Sunfish?",a="The Spotted Sunfish is a prized freshwater fish native to Lake Everstill in the Redridge Mountains. Renowned across the region for its taste and commercial value, it thrives in the lake's deep waters and serves as a staple commodity for Lakeshire's fishermen as well as a primary food source for local murlocs.",al={"what is spotted sunfish","spotted sunfish info","spotted sunfish lore"},it="identity",add="723094c5"},{q="Where does Spotted Sunfish come from?",a="Spotted Sunfish originate naturally within the cool waters of Lake Everstill in the Redridge Mountains. Rather than being crafted or cultivated, they are wild fish harvested directly from the lake, caught either by angling along the docks and shores or reclaimed from the clutches of local murloc poachers.",al={"spotted sunfish origin","where do spotted sunfish come from","spotted sunfish source"},it="origin",add="1a933976"}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="As a cook, you can use Spotted Sunfish, a native freshwater fish and a fixture on tavern tables in Redridge."},kw={"dockmaster baren","lake everstill","lakeshire","murloc","redridge mountains","selling fish","spotted sunfish"},rel={"quest:127","subzone:lake-everstill","subzone:lakeshire","zone:redridge","quest:150","topic:murloc"},src={"Spotted Sunfish","Selling Fish"}}
E["item:tharil-zun-s-head"] = {t="item",n="Tharil'zun's Head",z="redridge",s="Tharil'zun's Head reaches Lakeshire as proof that the commander terrorizing the Redridge approaches is dead. He led the Blackrock Outrunners occupying Stonewatch.",h="Tharil'zun's Head reaches Lakeshire as proof that the commander terrorizing the Redridge approaches is dead.",sec={{t="Trophy of Stonewatch",b="Blackrock orcs at Stonewatch Keep have pressed Lakeshire hard, raiding farms and ambushing travelers on the roads. Tharil'zun directed the Blackrock Outrunners at the head of these attacks. Lakeshire's garrison cannot risk acting on rumors or partial victories, so Marshal Marris demands proof that Tharil'zun is dead. His severed head shows that the Outrunners' coordinated ambushes from the keep have suffered a major blow.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who was Tharil'zun?",a="Tharil'zun was a crafty, vicious Blackrock orc commander at Stonewatch Keep. He led the Blackrock Outrunners, who ran relentless ambushes with the Renegades between Lakeshire and the keep.",al={"tharil'zun lore","who is tharilzun","tharil'zun leader"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Marshal Marris want his head?",a="Stormwind withholds major military aid from Redridge, leaving Marshal Marris and the Lakeshire guard to rely on mercenaries to pick off key threats. Marris requires absolute proof of Tharil'zun's death to know the Outrunners' leadership is truly shattered.",al={"why tharil'zun head","marris head proof","marris bounty"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where is Tharil'zun found?",a="Tharil'zun holds Stonewatch Keep in Redridge Mountains' eastern hills, surrounded by Blackrock orcs and gnolls.",al={"tharil'zun location","where is tharil'zun","find tharil'zun"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Does taking Tharil'zun's head end the Blackrock threat?",a="No. Tharil'zun's death disrupts the Outrunners' ambushes, but the Blackrock clan keeps a massive entrenched force in Stonewatch Keep and across the Redridge Mountains.",al={"are orcs gone","did we save redridge","after tharil'zun"},it="threat"},{q="What is Tharil'zun's Head?",a="This severed head is the physical proof that Tharil'zun, the commander directing Blackrock orc ambushes around Stonewatch Keep, has been slain. Carried back to Lakeshire, it shows the beleaguered town guard that one of the Blackrock clan's most dangerous field leaders in the Redridge Mountains will terrorize the roads no longer.",al={"tharil'zun head item","tharilzuns head lore"},it="item",add="a015b31b"},{q="Where does Tharil'zun's Head come from?",a="It is taken directly from the corpse of Tharil'zun, a prominent Blackrock orc leader operating out of the ruins of Stonewatch Keep. After he falls in battle to you or Lakeshire's defenders, the head is claimed as an undeniable trophy and grim verification of his demise.",al={"who took tharil'zun's head","tharilzun head origin","where did tharil'zuns head come from"},it="origin",add="f673cecf"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Each Blackrock chieftain slain eases the pressure on Lakeshire, a beleaguered town fighting for survival without official reinforcements from Stormwind."},kw={"blackrock outrunners","lakeshire","marshal marris","stonewatch","stonewatch keep","tharil'zun","tharil'zun's head"},rel={"quest:19","npc:marshal-marris","subzone:stonewatch-keep","subzone:stonewatch","quest:20","zone:redridge"},src={"Tharil'zun's Head","Tharil'zun (quest)"}}
E["item:the-state-of-lakeshire"] = {t="item",n="The State of Lakeshire",z="redridge",s="In Lakeshire, Magistrate Solomon's report calls for help before the town falls. It urges General Marcus Jonathan in Stormwind to send royal army reinforcements against the crisis in Redridge.",h="In Lakeshire, Magistrate Solomon's report calls for help before the town falls.",sec={{t="A Cry for Aid",b="Magistrate Solomon writes of the attacks threatening Lakeshire. Blackrock orcs and gnolls press the town, whose defenders cannot hold the borders indefinitely. Couriers carry his dispatch west along the road to Elwynn Forest. Solomon asks the Stormwind Army to intervene and protect the kingdom's eastern reach.",sp=0},{t="Bureaucracy and Deadlock",b="General Marcus Jonathan receives Solomon's report at Stormwind's gates. He respects the magistrate's standing and understands the danger, but cannot move the army on his own. Deployments need the crown's consent, so Lakeshire's plea must wait for a council with the young King and regent Bolvar Fordragon.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is The State of Lakeshire?",a="The State of Lakeshire is Magistrate Solomon's official dispatch about the military danger facing Lakeshire, asking Stormwind for troop reinforcements.",al={"state of lakeshire document","what is this report","solomon's message"},it="identity"},{q="Who is supposed to receive this dispatch?",a="General Marcus Jonathan is meant to receive the dispatch. He commands the Stormwind city guard and royal forces and is stationed at Stormwind's gates.",al={"who gets the report","who to deliver to","marcus jonathan report"},it="target"},{q="Why does Lakeshire need royal reinforcements?",a="Lakeshire needs royal reinforcements because Blackrock orcs, Shadowhide gnolls, and local murlocs keep besieging the settlement, overwhelming its town guard.",al={"why is lakeshire in danger","what threatens redridge"},it="motive"},{q="Does General Marcus Jonathan send help immediately?",a="No. General Marcus Jonathan agrees the crisis is severe, but he needs the King's formal approval to deploy the army. The request must first go through royal review.",al={"does stormwind help","does jonathan send troops"},it="next_step"},{q="Where does The State of Lakeshire come from, and who made it?",a="Magistrate Solomon, the civic leader and judge of Lakeshire, drafted this critical report. Facing relentless pressure from hostile forces surrounding the town, Solomon penned the dispatch himself to formally detail Redridge's perilous situation and petition the high command of Stormwind for immediate military aid.",al={"who wrote the state of lakeshire","who made state of lakeshire","state of lakeshire author"},it="origin",add="629511cc"},{q="Why is The State of Lakeshire so urgently needed?",a="Lakeshire stands under constant siege, and Magistrate Solomon knows the town cannot hold out alone without royal reinforcements. General Marcus Jonathan needs this official accounting in hand to justify dispatching elements of the Stormwind Army and to present Lakeshire's dire plight directly before the King and Highlord Bolvar Fordragon.",al={"why is state of lakeshire needed","why deliver state of lakeshire","why does marcus jonathan want state of lakeshire"},it="why_wanted",add="09d61feb"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, the report shows how exposed the outer settlements are and how political delays in the capital hold up military aid.",["race:Human"]="As a human of the kingdom, carrying this report shows how the common folk of Redridge are losing their ties to the distant crown in Stormwind."},kw={"dispatch","magistrate solomon","marcus jonathan","redridge","reinforcements","report","state of lakeshire","stormwind"},rel={"quest:120","npc:magistrate-solomon","npc:general-marcus-jonathan","subzone:lakeshire","zone:redridge","topic:stormwind-army","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"The State of Lakeshire","Messenger to Stormwind"}}
E["item:token-of-thievery"] = {t="item",n="Token of Thievery",z="redridge",s="In the Redridge Mountains, rogues face a test set by Lucius at Alther's Mill. A locked footlocker holds the Token of Thievery, proof of skill recovered during their training.",h="In the Redridge Mountains, rogues face a test set by Lucius at Alther's Mill.",sec={{t="A Test of Finesse",b="In Lakeshire, Lucius tests promising rogues in the field. He hides the Token of Thievery in a locked footlocker among the ruins of Alther's Mill, where Blackrock orcs threaten the area. Recovering it tests whether an initiate can pick a lock under mortal danger. Success earns a Certificate of Thievery.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Token of Thievery?",a="Lucius locks the Token of Thievery in a footlocker at Alther's Mill. Rogue initiates must pick its lock under danger to prove their skill.",al={"token of thievery use","what is token of thievery","lucius token"},it="identity"},{q="Who puts the token in the lockbox?",a="Lucius, an experienced rogue mentor in Lakeshire, puts the token in the footlocker as part of his training for young rogues.",al={"who owns the token","lucius lockbox owner","who hid the token"},it="origin"},{q="Why is the chest placed at Alther's Mill?",a="Alther's Mill lies up the road from Lakeshire, and prowling Blackrock orcs make it dangerous. Lucius sends trainees there to pick locks quickly and quietly in hostile territory.",al={"why althers mill","mill lockbox reason","danger at the mill"}},{q="What do you receive in exchange for the token?",a="Returning the token to Lucius earns a rogue a Certificate of Thievery, recognizing their foundational training in lockpicking.",al={"token reward","what does lucius give you","certificate of thievery"},it="why_wanted"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you prove your skill with lockpicks by recovering the Token of Thievery from ruins threatened by Blackrock orcs."},kw={"alther's mill","certificate of thievery","lakeshire","lockpicking","lucius","redridge","thieves' tools","token of thievery"},rel={"quest:2282","npc:lucius","quest:2281","topic:rogue","subzone:lakeshire","zone:redridge","quest:2300"},src={"Token of Thievery","Alther's Mill (quest)"}}
E["item:underbelly-whelp-scale"] = {t="item",n="Underbelly Whelp Scale",z="redridge",s="South of Lake Everstill, Underbelly Whelp Scale trades hands among Redridge craftsmen. Black dragon whelps provide the pliable scales, and local artisans value them when coin is scarce.",h="South of Lake Everstill, Underbelly Whelp Scale trades hands among Redridge craftsmen.",sec={{t="A Rare Trade Commodity",b="Black dragons bear tough scales, but facing a full-grown one is deadly for ordinary folk. South of Lake Everstill, black dragon whelps nest among the crags. Their back plates can be brittle or coarse, while the softer scales beneath their bellies bend more readily and still offer protection. Those qualities make Underbelly Whelp Scale valuable in local trade. Craftsmen prize it, and creditors can accept it in place of coin.",sp=0},{t="Verner's Debt",b="In Lakeshire, craftsmen sometimes barter when coin runs short or trade routes are strained. Verner Osgood, the local blacksmith, owes a heavy debt to Argus, a blacksmith in Goldshire. The debt began with a shipment of shoes brought in from Goldshire. Argus favors rare trade goods, so Verner depends on travelers to gather underbelly whelp scales. They can help settle what he owes and keep his workshop in good standing.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where do Underbelly Whelp Scales come from?",a="Black dragon whelps provide Underbelly Whelp Scale. They roost in rocky cliffs and hills south of Lakeshire in the Redridge Mountains, and the scales can also be gathered from mature whelps such as Snarlflare.",al={"who drops underbelly whelp scales","where to get whelp scales","how to find whelp scales"},it="origin"},{q="Why does Verner Osgood want these scales?",a="Verner Osgood owes Argus, the blacksmith in Goldshire, for a shipment of imported horseshoes. Argus accepts dragon scales as payment, and any extra scales give Verner material for making tough protective gear.",al={"why does verner need scales","verner osgood underbelly scales"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why are underbelly scales preferred over regular dragon scales?",a="Young dragons' underbelly scales are pliable enough to cut, shape, and sew into practical armor or reinforced gear. Their dorsal scales are often too rigid, thick, or warped for ordinary leatherworking and smithing techniques.",al={"why underbelly","what makes underbelly scales special"}},{q="Why are black dragon whelps in Redridge at all?",a="The Black Dragonflight has kept a presence in the burning peaks and crags along the borders of the Burning Steppes and Redridge. Its whelps brood and grow in the high, hard-to-reach cliffs.",al={"why are there dragons in redridge","black whelps redridge"}},{q="What is an Underbelly Whelp Scale?",a="These are the supple scales harvested from the underside of black dragon whelps prowling the southern reaches of Redridge. Unlike the rigid, impenetrable plates that cover an adult drake's back, the underbelly scales of a young whelp are both remarkably durable and pliable enough to be worked by skilled craftsmen, making them prized crafting material.",al={"what are underbelly whelp scales","underbelly whelp scale item","whelp scales lore"},it="identity",add="4599dc10"}},ang={["profession:Blacksmithing"]="Argus and other artisans value these scales for their strength. They can be worked into linings, grips, and specialized protective fittings, stronger than ordinary cowhide.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you know Lakeshire's isolated defenders depend on barter with Elwynn Forest to stay equipped. Dangerous local bounties such as dragon scales help maintain the town's supplies."},kw={"argus","black dragon whelp","lakeshire","redridge","snarlflare","underbelly scales","underbelly whelp scale","verner osgood"},rel={"quest:122","npc:verner-osgood","zone:redridge","subzone:lakeshire","quest:118","quest:119","subzone:goldshire"},src={"Underbelly Whelp Scale","Underbelly Scales"}}
E["item:verner-s-note"] = {t="item",n="Verner's Note",z="redridge",s="In Redridge, Verner Osgood sends a written requisition west to Smith Argus in Goldshire. It describes Lakeshire’s iron shortage and asks the Elwynn smith for horseshoes.",h="In Redridge, Verner Osgood sends a written requisition west to Smith Argus in Goldshire.",sec={{t="A Plea for Iron",b="Lakeshire’s defense has consumed nearly all of Verner Osgood’s iron. The town’s blacksmith has used his reserves to arm and armor the Stormwind Guard, who are stretched thin against invading gnolls and local perils. Meanwhile, Lakeshire’s stables have fallen into neglect, without even basic horseshoes for their mounts. Verner asks Smith Argus in Goldshire to send prepared shoes from Elwynn, so the town can shoe its horses.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is written in Verner's Note?",a="Verner’s Note tells Smith Argus that Verner has spent nearly all his iron reserves arming and armoring the Stormwind Guard in Lakeshire. With no iron left for horseshoes, he asks Argus to send them from Goldshire.",al={"verners note contents","what does the note say","verner note message"},it="item"},{q="Who is Verner Osgood?",a="Verner Osgood is the blacksmith operating out of Lakeshire in the Redridge Mountains. He outfits the town’s defenders and keeps working gear and beasts shod.",al={"who is verner","verner osgood redridge"},it="people"},{q="Who receives this note?",a="The note is carried westward down the road to Smith Argus, the blacksmith outside the forge in Goldshire, Elwynn Forest.",al={"who gets verners note","where do i bring the note","who is smith argus"},it="target"},{q="Why can't Verner make the horseshoes himself?",a="Verner has used his iron reserves to forge weapons and make repairs for the Stormwind Guard, who face gnolls and other local perils. That leaves no iron for horseshoes.",al={"why does lakeshire need shoes","why send to goldshire for shoes"},it="motive"},{q="What is Verner's Note?",a="It is a handwritten letter penned by Lakeshire's local smith, Verner Osgood, intended for Smith Argus in Goldshire. The letter explains that Lakeshire's forge has exhausted its iron reserves equipping the local Stormwind Guards against the rising regional threats, leaving none to craft shoes for the town's stable horses. It serves as an official requisition asking Argus to supply a crate of horseshoes in relief.",al={"verners note","what is this note","verner note purpose"},it="identity",add="486dfee9"},{q="Where does Verner's Note come from, and who made it?",a="The note was penned directly by Verner Osgood at his smithy in Lakeshire, Redridge Mountains. Strained by the incessant demands of arming the beleaguered town guard against surrounding gnolls and orcs, Verner drafted the letter to arrange an emergency supply shipment from his fellow blacksmith in Elwynn Forest.",al={"who wrote verners note","where did verners note come from","origin of verners note"},it="origin",add="b8effef9"},{q="Why does anyone want Verner's Note?",a="The note explains Verner Osgood's shortage of iron to Smith Argus and asks to borrow fifty pairs of horseshoes until Verner's next iron shipment arrives. Delivering it lets Argus arrange help for Lakeshire's stables.",al={"why does argus want verners note","who needs verners note","why deliver verners note"},it="why_wanted",add="c0af4e8d"}},ang={["profession:Blacksmithing"]="As a blacksmith, you can see how frontier warfare consumes supplies. When weapons and armor use every ingot, Lakeshire must import farrier supplies from safer settlements like Goldshire.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can see the strain on Stormwind’s rural settlements. Lakeshire must coordinate with villages in the heartland to maintain its supply lines."},kw={"goldshire","horseshoes","lakeshire","redridge mountains","smith argus","the price of shoes","verner osgood","verner's note"},rel={"quest:118","quest:119","npc:verner-osgood","npc:smith-argus","zone:redridge","subzone:goldshire","topic:stormwind-guard","topic:gnoll"},src={"Verner's Note","The Price of Shoes"}}
E["item:yowler-s-paw"] = {t="item",n="Yowler's Paw",z="redridge",s="In Lakeshire, Yowler's Paw is brought to Verner Osgood as proof the feared gnoll leader is dead. Yowler leads the packs menacing the hills above Lakeshire.",h="In Lakeshire, Yowler's Paw is brought to Verner Osgood as proof the feared gnoll leader is dead.",sec={{t="Trophy of the Pack Leader",b="Yowler leads the Redridge gnolls that terrorize the heights around Lake Everstill, their howls reaching Lakeshire. He is feared above all, a ruthless alpha driving the packs' expansion. Verner Osgood asks brave adventurers to bring him Yowler's paw, the customary proof of a bounty across human territories. Taking the paw marks the death of an unusually cunning predator and a blow against the chain of command among his disorganized followers.",sp=0},{t="A Town Left on Its Own",b="Yowler's Paw points to the danger facing Lakeshire. The Stormwind Army is consumed by the Blackrock orc threat entrenched around Stonewatch Keep, leaving civil authorities and townspeople to hire passing mercenaries for defense. Without regular royal garrisons, settlers such as Verner Osgood rely on proof that threats have been dealt with to keep local roads marginally safe for trade and travel.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who asks for Yowler's Paw?",a="Verner Osgood, a prominent tradesman and Lakeshire resident, asks for Yowler's Paw. He wants proof that the dangerous alpha gnoll terrorizing the hills has been dealt with for good.",al={"who wants yowlers paw","verner osgood paw quest","turn in yowlers paw"}},{q="Who is Yowler?",a="Yowler leads the Redridge gnoll packs. His brute strength and cunning let him rally multiple packs, making him an urgent danger to nearby townsfolk.",al={"who is yowler","yowler lore","redridge gnoll leader"},it="target"},{q="Why does Lakeshire rely on bounties instead of Stormwind soldiers?",a="The Stormwind Army is overwhelmed by Blackrock orcs fortified at Stonewatch Keep in eastern Redridge. With no reinforcements to spare, townsfolk such as Verner Osgood rely on freelance adventurers to hunt threats like Yowler.",al={"why no stormwind guard","where is stormwind army","why does verner hire mercenaries"},it="threat"},{q="What happens once Yowler is killed?",a="Killing Yowler breaks the leadership holding the aggressive gnolls together. His pack scatters into the wilderness, giving Lakeshire's residents temporary breathing room.",al={"what happens after yowler dies","gnolls after yowler","howling in the hills ending"},it="next_step"},{q="What is Yowler's Paw?",a="Yowler's Paw is the severed paw of the Redridge gnoll pack leader, taken as physical proof of his demise. Verner Osgood in Lakeshire asks adventurers to hunt down the savage alpha and retrieve it to verify the brute has finally been slain.",al={"what is yowlers paw","yowler paw item","yowlers paw"},it="identity",add="5e9f7255"},{q="Where does Yowler's Paw come from?",a="It is not a crafted item, but the severed limb of Yowler himself. Yowler leads the aggressive gnolls prowling the hills above Lakeshire, far fiercer and more cunning than the ordinary mongrels threatening the Redridge Mountains.",al={"where do you get yowlers paw","who made yowlers paw","yowler paw origin"},it="origin",add="c7fb7fcc"},{q="Why does Verner Osgood want Yowler's Paw?",a="Verner Osgood demands the paw as undeniable evidence that the menacing gnoll leader is dead. With Stormwind's army stretched thin against the Blackrock orcs, Lakeshire depends on traveling adventurers to cull local predators, and Verner requires proof before rewarding you.",al={"why is yowlers paw wanted","why verner want yowlers paw","yowler paw bounty"},it="why_wanted",add="034bdc4c"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Defeating Yowler and recovering his paw helps steady Redridge Mountains while Stormwind's military is stretched too thin to protect its own eastern frontier.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, tracking the Redridge gnolls' alpha and claiming his paw tests your skills at tracking and handling beasts against a dangerous predator."},kw={"gnoll pack leader","howling in the hills","lakeshire","redridge gnoll","redridge mountains","verner osgood","yowler","yowler's paw"},rel={"quest:126","npc:verner-osgood","topic:gnoll","zone:redridge","subzone:lakeshire","quest:124","topic:stormwind-army","quest:119"},src={"Yowler's Paw","Howling in the Hills"}}
E["npc:bailiff-conacher"] = {t="npc",n="Bailiff Conacher",z="redridge",s="In Lakeshire Town Hall, Bailiff Conacher keeps Stormwind law in force under Magistrate Solomon. He relies on travelers to uphold local decrees across the embattled Redridge Mountains.",h="In Lakeshire Town Hall, Bailiff Conacher keeps Stormwind law in force under Magistrate Solomon.",sec={{t="Justice in Lakeshire",b="Bailiff Conacher works with Magistrate Solomon in Lakeshire Town Hall to uphold law across the Redridge Mountains. Blackrock orcs and local gnolls besiege the town, leaving Conacher without ordinary civic procedures or royal garrisons to rely on. He issues legal decrees that authorize passing travelers to carry out capital justice in the realm's name.",sp=0},{t="Applying Solomon's Law",b="When the dark mage Morganth took the Tower of Ilgalar and bent the local Shadowhide gnolls to his will, the Court of Lakeshire judged the beasts guilty of high treason. Stormwind law sentences those who aid a fugitive and criminal to death. Conacher invokes Solomon's Law and sends travelers across the ridges to find Shadowhide gnolls and bring back their pendants as proof that the crown's law has been carried out.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Bailiff Conacher?",a="Bailiff Conacher serves the Court of Lakeshire and helps Magistrate Solomon uphold civil authority and Stormwind law in the Redridge Mountains.",al={"bailiff conacher role","who is conacher","conacher lore"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Bailiff Conacher be found?",a="You can find Bailiff Conacher inside Lakeshire Town Hall, on the north side of the bridge in the Redridge Mountains.",al={"bailiff conacher location","where is conacher","conacher redridge"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is Solomon's Law?",a="Solomon's Law applies Stormwind law by decree of Magistrate Solomon. Aiding known criminals such as the rogue sorcerer Morganth carries a death sentence, making his allied Shadowhide gnolls liable to execution.",al={"what is solomons law","solomon law gnolls","shadowhide law"}},{q="Why does Conacher ask for Shadowhide pendants?",a="The pendants prove that a Shadowhide gnoll has been slain under Lakeshire's legal sentence against those aiding Morganth.",al={"why collect pendants","shadowhide pendants purpose"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Whose side is Bailiff Conacher on?",a="Bailiff Conacher serves the Alliance and answers directly to Magistrate Solomon in the town of Lakeshire. As an official of the Redridge court, his duty is to uphold Stormwind law and protect the local citizens from encroaching threats.",al={"conacher allegiance","who does conacher serve","is conacher alliance"},it="side",add="6ce891cc"},{q="What does Bailiff Conacher want?",a="Conacher seeks to enforce Lakeshire's laws and safeguard Redridge. With the renegade mage Morganth enlisting the local Shadowhide gnolls, the bailiff recruits able adventurers to bring judgment upon the gnolls and curb the dark mage's influence.",al={"conacher goal","what does bailiff conacher need"},it="wants",add="5d999432"},{q="Why is Bailiff Conacher here in Lakeshire?",a="Conacher is stationed at the Lakeshire Town Hall as the town bailiff. Working alongside Magistrate Solomon, he assists in administering local justice and managing civic defense during a time when Stormwind cannot spare reinforcements for the region.",al={"why is conacher in redridge","conacher lakeshire town hall"},it="why_here",add="8124ae86"},{q="Who is Bailiff Conacher tied to?",a="Conacher works directly under Magistrate Solomon as part of the Court of Lakeshire. He cooperates closely with town officials and local guards to keep order in the settlement against outside invaders.",al={"conacher allies","who does conacher work with"},it="ties",add="df8ac9aa"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you can see how far Stormwind law reaches in a border town left largely to fend for itself."},kw={"bailiff","conacher","lakeshire","morganth","redridge","shadowhide","solomon","town hall"},rel={"npc:magistrate-solomon","quest:91","subzone:lakeshire-town-hall","subzone:lakeshire","subzone:tower-of-ilgalar","quest:249","topic:gnoll","zone:redridge"},src={"Bailiff Conacher"}}
E["npc:barkeep-daniels"] = {t="npc",n="Barkeep Daniels",z="redridge",s="At the Lakeshire Inn, Barkeep Daniels keeps drinks flowing as raiders disrupt the roads. The town guards, fishermen, and travelers who gather there depend on the inn for a welcome pause, but supplies are running low.",h="At the Lakeshire Inn, Barkeep Daniels keeps drinks flowing as raiders disrupt the roads.",sec={{t="Keeping Spirits High in Lakeshire",b="Barkeep Daniels pours drinks and greets visitors at the Lakeshire Inn, near the bridge. Gnolls and Blackrock orcs have kept Lakeshire under pressure for months, and its defenders turn to the tavern after grim patrols. Raids and severed roads have disrupted trade across the region. With liquor running low when the town needs good cheer, Daniels welcomes travelers willing to fetch shipments from safer settlements.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Barkeep Daniels?",a="Barkeep Daniels keeps the counter at the Lakeshire Inn, serving drinks to townsfolk, travelers, and the town guard.",al={"daniels redridge","lakeshire barkeep","who is daniels"},it="identity"},{q="Why is he running low on drinks?",a="Blackrock orc and gnoll raids have choked off caravans and trade routes into the Redridge Mountains. With deliveries cut off and stressed defenders drinking through the stores, Daniels struggles to restock the shelves.",al={"why out of booze","dry times quest lore","why no alcohol"},it="why_here"},{q="What does he need help with?",a="Daniels needs travelers to bring fresh liquor from outside Redridge so the inn can keep serving its patrons.",al={"barkeep daniels quest","what does he want","daniels errand"},it="wants"},{q="Whose side is Barkeep Daniels on?",a="Barkeep Daniels is a loyal citizen of the Alliance and a fixture of Lakeshire. He serves the town's local folk, visitors, and garrisoned defenders straight from behind the counter at the Lakeshire Inn, standing firmly with the kingdom of Stormwind amid the rising Blackrock threat.",al={"barkeep daniels faction","is barkeep daniels alliance","daniels redridge allegiance"},it="side",add="2f43c9bf"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, keeping morale high in Lakeshire matters. The settlement is the kingdom's battered buffer against the Blackrock stronghold in the north."},kw={"barkeep daniels","bartender","daniels","dry times","lakeshire inn","redridge innkeeper"},rel={"subzone:lakeshire-inn","subzone:lakeshire","zone:redridge","quest:116"},src={"Barkeep Daniels"}}
E["npc:chef-breanna"] = {t="npc",n="Chef Breanna",z="redridge",s="In Lakeshire, Chef Breanna feeds the Stormwind soldiers guarding the Redridge Mountains. She leads the town's kitchen and uses hearty local ingredients to keep the defenders on their feet.",h="In Lakeshire, Chef Breanna feeds the Stormwind soldiers guarding the Redridge Mountains.",sec={{t="Feeding Lakeshire's Defenders",b="Chef Breanna works from a restaurant house in northwestern Lakeshire with her assistants, Crystal Boughman and Gretchen Vogel. She is responsible for feeding the entire local battalion. Blackrock orcs, gnolls, and murlocs besiege the town, and Stormwind's understaffed garrison must stay strong. Her signature Redridge Goulash uses wild game and beasts from the surrounding ridges to feed the weary guards.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Chef Breanna?",a="Chef Breanna runs the kitchen house in the northwestern corner of Lakeshire. She feeds the Stormwind soldiers defending the Redridge Mountains.",al={"chef breanna","breanna lakeshire","who is breanna"},it="identity"},{q="What does Chef Breanna need help with?",a="Chef Breanna needs local game meat to make Redridge Goulash for the garrison. You can gather tough condor meat, goretusk snouts, and crisp spider meat in the wilderness around Lakeshire.",al={"breanna quest","redridge goulash ingredients","what does she want"},it="wants"},{q="Who works with Chef Breanna?",a="Crystal Boughman and Gretchen Vogel work with Chef Breanna at her restaurant house. They help manage the establishment and tend to hungry townsfolk and soldiers.",al={"breanna helpers","crystal boughman","gretchen vogel"},it="ties"},{q="Whose side is Chef Breanna on?",a="Chef Breanna is loyal to the Alliance and the Kingdom of Stormwind. Running her kitchen out of Lakeshire, she is directly responsible for provisioning the local Stormwind battalion stationed to defend the town and its surrounding borders.",al={"chef breanna faction","who does breanna serve","is chef breanna alliance"},it="side",add="33f751f4"},{q="Why is Chef Breanna here in Lakeshire?",a="Breanna operates the town restaurant in northwestern Lakeshire. Her primary role is keeping the local Stormwind soldiers fed and ready for duty amidst the mounting threats encircling Redridge, relying on fresh local ingredients to sustain the garrison.",al={"why is breanna in redridge","why is chef breanna in lakeshire","breanna purpose lakeshire"},it="why_here",add="f2dfd1fc"}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="Breanna's Redridge Goulash uses spiders, condors, and goretusks from the surrounding wilds to make a hearty meal for a military outpost.",["faction:Alliance"]="Chef Breanna feeds the soldiers holding Lakeshire's bridge and town perimeter. Without her cooking, the strained garrison could quickly tire against the relentless orc and gnoll incursions."},kw={"breanna","chef breanna","cook","garrison","goulash","lakeshire","redridge goulash"},rel={"quest:92","subzone:lakeshire","zone:redridge","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Chef Breanna"}}
E["npc:darcy-parker"] = {t="npc",n="Darcy",z="redridge",s="At the Lakeshire Inn, Darcy keeps the town's defenders fed and spirits up. She serves drinks and warm meals, with a special care for Guard Parker.",h="At the Lakeshire Inn, Darcy keeps the town's defenders fed and spirits up.",sec={{t="A Friendly Face at the Inn",b="Darcy keeps the Lakeshire Inn's counter working through long days and nights. The town's militia come there for food and drink while gnolls and Blackrock orcs keep Lakeshire under pressure. Darcy also looks out for guards posted around town. She asks travelers to carry hot meals and friendly errands to defenders stationed along the borders.",sp=0},{t="Romance on the Guard Post",b="Darcy pays special attention to Guard Parker, who patrols the roads near Three Corners. She thinks he works too hard on an empty stomach and often sends travelers with lunch for him. Darcy watches Martie Jainrose closely, believing her to be jealous and a rival for Parker's favor. Their feelings mingle with the work of defending Lakeshire.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Darcy?",a="Darcy works as a human waitress at the Lakeshire Inn in the Redridge Mountains. She prepares food for the town's defenders and asks passing travelers to deliver meals to guards on duty.",al={"who is darcy","darcy parker npc","lakeshire waitress"},it="identity"},{q="What is Darcy's relationship with Guard Parker?",a="Darcy is deeply fond of Guard Parker. She packs him fresh lunches and sends them with travelers while he patrols the roads near Three Corners.",al={"darcy and guard parker","guard parker darcy","who does darcy like"},it="ties"},{q="Why is Darcy suspicious of Martie Jainrose?",a="Darcy thinks Martie Jainrose is jealous and sees her as a romantic rival for Guard Parker's attention.",al={"darcy and martie","martie jainrose","darcy rival"}},{q="Where can Darcy be found?",a="You can find Darcy serving patrons at the Lakeshire Inn in Lakeshire, by the northern shore of Lake Everstill in Redridge.",al={"darcy location","where is darcy","find darcy"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Darcy on?",a="Darcy stands squarely with the Grand Alliance and the local folk of the Redridge Mountains. As a waitress at the Lakeshire Inn, her daily life is dedicated to looking after the town's defenders, cooking meals, and providing hospitality to townspeople and visiting Alliance adventurers alike.",al={"darcy faction","is darcy alliance","who does darcy serve"},it="side",add="e14c1e0c"},{q="What does Darcy want?",a="Darcy wants to keep the local guards fed and tended to, but she also has her eyes set on romance. She is particularly smitten with Guard Parker stationed out on the road, going out of her way to prepare and send him hot lunches while fretting over potential rivals like Martie Jainrose.",al={"what does darcy need","darcy goal","darcy quest motive"},it="wants",add="b7996d79"},{q="Why is Darcy in Lakeshire?",a="Darcy lives and works in Lakeshire as the waitress of the local inn. While the town faces constant pressure from orcs and gnolls, someone has to keep the inn running and serve hot meals to weary soldiers and travelers arriving across the great bridge.",al={"why is darcy here","darcy lakeshire role","darcy at lakeshire inn"},it="why_here",add="4cbadea5"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you can find Darcy among Lakeshire's everyday folk, keeping spirits high and bellies full while the town waits for aid from Stormwind."},kw={"darcy","guard parker","lakeshire","lakeshire inn","martie jainrose","redridge","waitress"},rel={"npc:watch-captain-parker","npc:martie-jainrose","subzone:lakeshire-inn","subzone:lakeshire","zone:redridge","quest:129","quest:131"},src={"Darcy Parker"}}
E["npc:deputy-feldon"] = {t="npc",n="Deputy Feldon",z="redridge",s="South of the Great Lakeshire Bridge, Deputy Feldon watches the road into Lakeshire. Gnoll packs are creeping toward the town, and he keeps a nervous vigil.",h="South of the Great Lakeshire Bridge, Deputy Feldon watches the road into Lakeshire.",sec={{t="A Guard on Edge",b="Deputy Feldon stands watch south of the Lakeshire bridge, guarding a road needed for trade and travel. Blackrock orcs press from the north while gnoll packs overrun the southern hills, stretching the town guard thin. Feldon cannot leave his post without weakening Lakeshire's perimeter. He depends on passing adventurers to drive back the gnolls before they cut the town off.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Deputy Feldon?",a="Deputy Feldon serves in the Lakeshire town guard, stationed just south of the bridge to the main southern road in Redridge Mountains.",al={"feldon","who is feldon","deputy feldon role"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Deputy Feldon worried about gnolls?",a="Gnoll camps have been spotted along the road toward Elwynn Forest. Feldon fears they may push into the human homeland, leaving Lakeshire no longer the only town under siege. The guard is ill-equipped to face them.",al={"why gnolls","feldon gnoll problem","encroaching gnolls"},it="wants"},{q="Why doesn't Feldon deal with the gnolls himself?",a="The Lakeshire guard is understaffed and facing orcs and gnolls at once. Feldon cannot leave his bridge post without leaving the town entrance unguarded.",al={"why doesn't feldon fight","feldon duty"}},{q="Where can Deputy Feldon be found?",a="Deputy Feldon stands watch on the road just south of the Great Lakeshire Bridge, guarding the town's southern approaches.",al={"feldon location","where is feldon"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Deputy Feldon on?",a="Deputy Feldon is a loyal lawman of the Alliance, serving Redridge Mountains under the authority of the Lakeshire town guard and Magistrate Solomon. He works to protect the kingdom's citizens and keep the roads leading into town safe from encroaching threats.",al={"deputy feldon faction","who does feldon serve","deputy feldon alliance"},it="side",add="1b9b43bf"},{q="Why is Deputy Feldon stationed near the bridge?",a="Deputy Feldon is posted just south of the Lakeshire bridge to watch the southern approaches. With gnoll packs pushing dangerously close to town, he monitors the road to keep travel open and enlist able-bodied travelers to stem the invasion before the bridge itself is overwhelmed.",al={"why is feldon here","deputy feldon location why","what is feldon doing here"},it="why_here",add="dc2592f9"},{q="Who is Deputy Feldon tied to?",a="Feldon answers to Magistrate Solomon and the local peacekeeping forces tasked with guarding Lakeshire. He is part of the sparse local watch that defends Redridge in the absence of substantial military reinforcements from Stormwind.",al={"deputy feldon ties","who does feldon report to","deputy feldon sheriff"},it="ties",add="5e39d198"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance champion, you can see how strained Stormwind's outer territories are: local guardsmen need passing champions to help keep the king's peace."},kw={"bridge","deputy feldon","feldon","gnolls","guard","lakeshire","redridge"},rel={"subzone:lakeshire","zone:redridge","quest:244","quest:246","topic:gnoll"},src={"Deputy Feldon"}}
E["npc:foreman-oslow"] = {t="npc",n="Foreman Oslow",z="redridge",s="At Lakeshire, Foreman Oslow struggles to rebuild the Everstill Bridge. Blackrock orcs shattered the crossing, while lost tools and stolen supplies have stalled the work. He needs help recovering his equipment and gathering materials so the town can restore its trade route.",h="At Lakeshire, Foreman Oslow struggles to rebuild the Everstill Bridge.",sec={{t="A Town Cut in Two",b="Foreman Oslow works beside the broken Everstill Bridge, trying to reconnect Lakeshire. The span crosses Lake Everstill, linking the western roads toward Elwynn with the eastern shore. Blackrock orcs came down from the crags of Stonewatch and struck the crossing to cripple Lakeshire's trade and military movement. With the bridge broken, the town is split and exposed.",sp=0},{t="Sunken Steel and Stolen Stone",b="Foreman Oslow has lost the tools and materials needed for repairs. After the bridge fell, replacement tools traveled overland from Goldshire, then went aboard a lake ferry. Blackrock orc catapults struck the vessel, sending Oslow's heavy iron toolbox to the muddy bed of Lake Everstill. Gnolls in Redridge also seized a caravan of new materials from Stormwind, taking the iron pikes and rivets needed to raise the arches.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Foreman Oslow?",a="Foreman Oslow is a human stonemason and builder in Lakeshire. He leads the work to maintain and rebuild the Everstill Bridge.",al={"foreman oslow","who is oslow","lakeshire builder"},it="identity"},{q="Why is the Everstill Bridge broken?",a="Blackrock orcs shattered the Everstill Bridge. Its destruction severed Lakeshire's main route, weakened the town's defenses, and cut easy travel between the eastern and western shores.",al={"why is the bridge broken","who broke lakeshire bridge","everstill bridge destroyed"},it="ruin"},{q="Where are Oslow's lost tools?",a="Oslow's heavy toolbox lies at the bottom of Lake Everstill. A Blackrock catapult barrage struck and sank the boat carrying it from Goldshire.",al={"where are the tools","lost tools location","oslow toolbox"},gp=true},{q="Why hasn't the bridge been repaired yet?",a="Oslow cannot resume construction because Blackrock orc catapults sank his tools in the lake and gnolls stole building supplies from incoming shipments. He needs outside help to recover equipment and materials.",al={"why is bridge not fixed","lakeshire bridge delay"},it="conflict"},{q="Where did Oslow's supplies come from originally?",a="Oslow's replacement tools came by wagon from Goldshire in Elwynn Forest, then transferred to a lake ferry to bypass the broken bridge.",al={"supply wagon origin","where did tools come from"},it="origin"},{q="What threats is Oslow dealing with?",a="Oslow faces Blackrock orcs in the nearby heights, whose siege engines bombard the lake, and prowling gnolls that attack supply convoys.",al={"oslow enemies","who attacks the bridge"},it="threat"},{q="Whose side is Foreman Oslow on?",a="Foreman Oslow serves the Kingdom of Stormwind and the local township of Lakeshire. As the town's chief builder and foreman, his duty lies in maintaining Redridge's vital infrastructure and helping its people survive despite relentless attacks from surrounding Blackrock orcs and hostile gnolls.",al={"oslow faction","who does foreman oslow serve","foreman oslow alliance"},it="side",add="cf681f3e"},{q="What does Foreman Oslow want?",a="Oslow's primary goal is to rebuild the ruined Everstill Bridge and keep Lakeshire connected to the rest of the kingdom. To accomplish that, he desperately needs his sunken toolbox dredged from Lake Everstill and the construction supplies that were ambushed and stolen by local gnolls recovered.",al={"what does oslow want","foreman oslow goal","why does oslow need help"},it="wants",add="1a3f577b"},{q="Why is Foreman Oslow in Lakeshire?",a="Oslow is stationed by the lake to supervise public works and lead the reconstruction of the Everstill Bridge. The bridge is Lakeshire's lifeblood, but relentless enemy assaults and devastating supply losses keep him stranded right at the water's edge, waiting on aid to continue his work.",al={"why is oslow here","oslow lakeshire purpose","foreman oslow job"},it="why_here",add="765147a2"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you know Lakeshire's broken bridge leaves the eastern frontier exposed. Restoring it is vital to securing the border.",["profession:Mining"]="As a miner, you know Oslow depends on raw materials, metalwork, and quarry shipments to rebuild the broken masonry."},kw={"blackrock","everstill bridge","foreman oslow","goldshire","lakeshire","oslow","redridge","toolbox"},rel={"quest:89","quest:125","subzone:lakeshire","zone:redridge","topic:gnoll","subzone:goldshire","quest:347","quest:345"},src={"Foreman Oslow"}}
E["npc:gath-ilzogg"] = {t="npc",n="Gath'Ilzogg",z="redridge",s="Stonewatch Keep remains under Gath'Ilzogg's command in the Redridge Mountains. The Blackrock warlord's force holds the fortress and raids Lakeshire, where Magistrate Solomon has placed a bounty on him.",h="Stonewatch Keep remains under Gath'Ilzogg's command in the Redridge Mountains.",sec={{t="The Scourge of Stonewatch",b="Gath'Ilzogg came north from the Burning Steppes to secure Redridge for the Blackrock clan. With help from the renegade human warlock Morganth's foul sorcery, his warband battered Stonewatch Keep's defenders and seized the heights above the region. From the fortress, Gath'Ilzogg directs raids through the valleys and toward Lakeshire's bridge, tightening pressure on the human settlement. Elite Blackrock guards and a vicious black dragon whelp named Singe stay close to him.",sp=0},{t="A Fragile Hold",b="Gath'Ilzogg's hold on Stonewatch brought new dangers. Morganth turned against his former orcish allies and raised Shadowhide gnolls under Lieutenant Fangore. They prey on Blackrock patrols and human travelers alike. Magistrate Solomon has placed an open bounty on Gath'Ilzogg and calls on Alliance mercenaries or adventurers to climb Stonewatch Keep's ramparts and end his terror before Lakeshire falls entirely.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Gath'Ilzogg?",a="Gath'Ilzogg leads the Blackrock vanguard that invaded Redridge and captured Stonewatch Keep from the Alliance.",al={"gath'ilzogg lore","who is gathilzogg","blackrock boss redridge"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Gath'Ilzogg be found?",a="Gath'Ilzogg holds the top of Stonewatch Keep, in the eastern crags of the Redridge Mountains.",al={"gath'ilzogg location","where is gathilzogg","find gathilzogg"},gp=true},{q="Why does Gath'Ilzogg have a dragon whelp?",a="Gath'Ilzogg keeps a black dragon whelp named Singe at his side. Many believe Lord Victor Nefarius gave Singe to him for seizing Stonewatch Keep.",al={"why whelp next to gathilzogg","singe dragon","black dragon whelp gathilzogg"}},{q="Why is there a bounty on his head?",a="Magistrate Solomon of Lakeshire placed a high-priority bounty on Gath'Ilzogg because his raids and occupation of Stonewatch threaten the town with complete destruction.",al={"wanted gath'ilzogg","who wants gathilzogg dead","magistrate solomon bounty"},it="danger"},{q="What happened between Gath'Ilzogg and Morganth?",a="Morganth, a human warlock, first aided Gath'Ilzogg's conquest of Stonewatch with dark magic. After the fortress fell, Morganth betrayed the orcs and raised Shadowhide gnolls to attack both humanity and the Blackrock clan.",al={"morganth gathilzogg alliance","why are gnolls attacking orcs","morganth betrayal"},it="conflict"},{q="Whose side is Gath'Ilzogg on?",a="Gath'Ilzogg is a warlord of the Blackrock clan, loyal to the Dark Horde rooted in Blackrock Mountain. He and his forces actively war against the Kingdom of Stormwind, showing utter hostility toward the Alliance and any who trespass on their conquered territory.",al={"gath'ilzogg faction","who does gath'ilzogg serve","is gath'ilzogg blackrock"},it="side",add="9f2c44f6"},{q="What does Gath'Ilzogg want?",a="From his stronghold at Stonewatch Keep, Gath'Ilzogg plots the destruction of Lakeshire and the complete conquest of Redridge. He directs raids against human settlements and works to expand the Blackrock clan's dominion over the surrounding lands.",al={"what is gath'ilzogg's goal","gath'ilzogg plan","why is gath'ilzogg attacking"},it="wants",add="56c8e0ec"},{q="Why is Gath'Ilzogg here?",a="Gath'Ilzogg led the assault that overwhelmed the Alliance defenders at Stonewatch Keep. Having captured the fortress, he now uses it as a fortified base of operations to strike deeper into Redridge and organize raids against Lakeshire.",al={"why is gath'ilzogg in redridge","why is gath'ilzogg at stonewatch","gath'ilzogg stonewatch"},it="why_here",add="d3a450f6"},{q="Who is Gath'Ilzogg tied to?",a="Beyond commanding the local Blackrock orcs, Gath'Ilzogg once formed a treacherous alliance with the rogue human warlock Morganth to take Stonewatch Keep. He also commands the whelp Singe, a creature likely granted to him by Lord Victor Nefarius as a reward for his victory.",al={"gath'ilzogg allies","who works with gath'ilzogg","gath'ilzogg connections"},it="ties",add="d6829113"},{q="Why is Gath'Ilzogg feared?",a="Gath'Ilzogg proved his lethality by successfully orchestrating the fall of Stonewatch Keep, crushing the local Alliance garrison. Magistrate Solomon views him as the foremost military threat to Lakeshire's survival, prompting a severe bounty on the warlord's head.",al={"why is gath'ilzogg dangerous","is gath'ilzogg famous","gath'ilzogg reputation"},it="fame",add="b07f2498"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, defeating Gath'Ilzogg would break the backbone of the Blackrock offensive threatening Lakeshire and answer Magistrate Solomon's desperate call.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, Gath'Ilzogg shows the Blackrock clan's old, warmongering ways under the Dark Horde, wholly separate from Thrall's new Horde in Kalimdor."},kw={"blackrock","gath'ilzogg","gathilzogg","lakeshire","morganth","singe","solomon","stonewatch","stonewatch keep"},rel={"quest:169","subzone:stonewatch-keep","subzone:stonewatch","npc:magistrate-solomon","quest:249","topic:blackrock-clan","subzone:lakeshire","zone:redridge"},src={"Gath'Ilzogg"}}
E["npc:general-marcus-jonathan"] = {t="npc",n="General Marcus Jonathan",z="redridge",s="At Stormwind's gates, General Marcus Jonathan guards the capital and weighs calls for aid from the kingdom's frontier settlements. A veteran of the Second War, he commands Stormwind Defense and oversees the garrison.",h="At Stormwind's gates, General Marcus Jonathan guards the capital and weighs calls for aid from the kingdom's...",sec={{t="Commander of the Gates",b="General Marcus Jonathan commands Stormwind's defense from horseback in the Valley of Heroes. He is the highest-ranking officer at the city gates and its first line of defense. During the Second War, he fought beside soldiers such as Reginald Windsor under General Turalyon. Now he must protect the capital while frontier towns, including Lakeshire, make increasingly desperate appeals for help.",sp=0},{t="A Strained Command",b="General Marcus Jonathan assures local magistrates that he is committed to helping towns such as Lakeshire repel Blackrock orcs and gnolls. In private, he confides that the court has grown distant and the boy-king's regency behaves strangely.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where can I find General Marcus Jonathan?",a="General Marcus Jonathan is on horseback just inside Stormwind City's main gates, overlooking the entrance bridge in the Valley of Heroes.",al={"marcus jonathan location","where is general jonathan","stormwind gate commander"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is Marcus Jonathan's military history?",a="General Marcus Jonathan served under General Turalyon during the Second War and fought beside comrades such as Reginald Windsor. He eventually rose to become the High Commander of Stormwind Defense.",al={"marcus jonathan past","marcus jonathan lore","did marcus fight in the second war"},it="history"},{q="Who is General Marcus Jonathan?",a="General Marcus Jonathan is the High Commander of Stormwind Defense. A seasoned veteran who served under General Turalyon during the Second War, he now oversees the military forces safeguarding the capital city and its surrounding territories.",al={"who is marcus jonathan","marcus jonathan identity","who is general jonathan"},it="identity",add="d649e9ed"},{q="Whose side is General Marcus Jonathan on?",a="He is utterly devoted to the Kingdom of Stormwind and the Grand Alliance. He takes his duty to defend the realm and protect its citizens with absolute seriousness, answering directly to the crown and Stormwind's high leadership.",al={"marcus jonathan allegiance","who does marcus jonathan serve","marcus jonathan faction"},it="side",add="59fdae30"},{q="What does General Marcus Jonathan want?",a="Jonathan wants to safeguard Stormwind and ensure its outlying settlements, like Lakeshire, receive the military support they desperately require. However, with King Varian Wrynn missing and the royal court acting strangely, his ability to mobilize troops as he wishes is severely hindered.",al={"marcus jonathan goal","what does marcus jonathan need","marcus jonathan motives"},it="wants",add="5549e5c1"},{q="Why is General Marcus Jonathan relevant to Redridge?",a="Magistrate Solomon of Lakeshire directs pleas for military aid straight to General Jonathan, knowing his word carries substantial weight in Stormwind. As the commander of the army, Jonathan is the official with the authority to petition the crown for reinforcements to defend Redridge.",al={"why marcus jonathan redridge","marcus jonathan lakeshire","why send message to marcus jonathan"},it="why_here",add="b8230eb1"},{q="Who is General Marcus Jonathan tied to?",a="He shares a long history with Marshal Reginald Windsor, having fought alongside him under General Turalyon during the Second War. In Stormwind, he regularly coordinates with the crown and answers urgent appeals from regional leaders such as Magistrate Solomon.",al={"marcus jonathan connections","who knows marcus jonathan","marcus jonathan allies"},it="ties",add="ab66a8e6"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance fighter, you can see Stormwind's martial pride in Marcus Jonathan, stationed at the capital's gate.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you can look to General Marcus Jonathan, commander of Stormwind's gates and a Second War veteran, as an example of the kingdom's martial duty in its infantry ranks."},kw={"general jonathan","lakeshire","magistrate solomon","marcus jonathan","reginald windsor","stormwind army","stormwind defense","valley of heroes"},rel={"subzone:valley-of-heroes","zone:stormwind","quest:120","npc:magistrate-solomon","subzone:lakeshire","topic:stormwind-army","topic:second-war","zone:redridge"},src={"General Marcus Jonathan"}}
E["npc:guard-berton"] = {t="npc",n="Guard Berton",z="redridge",s="Outside the Lakeshire Inn, Guard Berton seeks swift justice for Targorr the Dread. The human guardsman is tired of Stormwind's delays while Redridge faces the Blackrock orc invasion.",h="Outside the Lakeshire Inn, Guard Berton seeks swift justice for Targorr the Dread.",sec={{t="A Guard Seeking Justice",b="Guard Berton keeps watch outside the Lakeshire Inn as Redridge Mountains faces the Blackrock orc invasion. His concern is Targorr the Dread, an enemy captured and locked deep within the Stormwind Stockade. Sentenced to death for crimes against the kingdom, Targorr remains imprisoned because Stormwind has postponed his execution indefinitely. Berton will not let the brutal raider linger in a cell while Lakeshire bleeds. He hires willing adventurers to bypass the delays and kill the orc.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Guard Berton?",a="Guard Berton is an Alliance guard posted outside the Lakeshire Inn in Redridge Mountains. He hires adventurers to carry out justice against an infamous orc prisoner.",al={"berton lakeshire","who is berton"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Guard Berton want Targorr the Dread killed?",a="Stormwind has put Targorr the Dread's execution on hold, despite his sentence for crimes against the kingdom. With Redridge under siege, Berton arranges for Targorr to be killed inside the Stockade.",al={"why kill targorr","targorr execution","what comes around quest lore"},it="wants"},{q="Where is Targorr the Dread held?",a="Targorr the Dread is held in the Stockade, a high-security dungeon in Stormwind City's Canal district.",al={"targorr location","where is targorr"},it="target"},{q="Where can Guard Berton be found?",a="Guard Berton keeps watch just outside the Lakeshire Inn, overlooking Lakeshire's town center in Redridge.",al={"where is berton","berton location"},it="why_here"},{q="Whose side is Guard Berton on?",a="Guard Berton is a loyal defender of the Kingdom of Stormwind and the Alliance. Stationed in Redridge Mountains, his duty is to protect the beleaguered town of Lakeshire and its people from the surrounding perils of the wilderness, including the marauding Blackrock orcs.",al={"berton faction","who does guard berton serve","is berton alliance"},it="side",add="352370f6"},{q="Who is Guard Berton tied to?",a="Berton serves among the Redridge town guard stationed in Lakeshire, standing alongside his fellow protectors outside the local inn. Beyond his local garrison, his grievances tie him directly to Targorr the Dread, a notorious captive held within the Stormwind Stockade.",al={"guard berton connections","berton town guard","who does berton work with"},it="ties",add="bd53caa6"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance defender, you can see why border towns grow frustrated when Stormwind's bureaucracy delays justice while they fight for survival."},kw={"berton","guard berton","lakeshire","redridge","targorr","targorr the dread","the stockade","what comes around"},rel={"npc:targorr-the-dread","quest:386","subzone:lakeshire-inn","subzone:lakeshire","zone:stockade","subzone:stormwind-stockade","zone:redridge","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Guard Berton"}}
E["npc:guard-howe"] = {t="npc",n="Guard Howe",z="redridge",s="Near Lakeshire's bridge, Guard Howe watches the road and seeks fighters against the Blackrock orcs. A personal vendetta drives him to offer bounties for proof of their defeat.",h="Near Lakeshire's bridge, Guard Howe watches the road and seeks fighters against the Blackrock orcs.",sec={{t="A Grudge on the Bridge",b="Guard Howe keeps watch just south of the stone bridge over Lake Everstill, near the heart of Lakeshire. Blackrock orcs press into the Redridge Mountains, and Howe sees them as a threat to the valley. He holds a bitter grudge against the clan and recruits passing fighters to hunt orcs in the eastern hills. In return, he offers pay for proof that they have been defeated.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Guard Howe?",a="Guard Howe is a human town guard stationed just south of Lakeshire's bridge in the Redridge Mountains. He helps protect the settlement and sends fighters against the invading Blackrock orcs.",al={"guard howe","howe lakeshire","who is howe"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Guard Howe want Blackrock orcs killed?",a="Howe seeks vengeance against the Blackrock clan, whose forces have pushed deep into the Redridge Mountains and keep Lakeshire under pressure. He offers bounties to those who thin their ranks.",al={"why blackrock bounty","howe orcs","why does howe hate orcs"},it="wants"},{q="Is Guard Howe related to anyone else in the region?",a="Guard Howe shares a surname with Soloman Howe, so they may be kin. Howe keeps his attention on guarding Lakeshire and fighting the orcs.",al={"howe relatives","soloman howe relation"},it="ties"},{q="Whose side is Guard Howe on?",a="Guard Howe serves the Kingdom of Stormwind and stands with the town guard of Lakeshire. Stationed on the front lines of Redridge, he fights to defend the local human populace against the relentless incursions threatening their borders.",al={"guard howe faction","is guard howe alliance","who does guard howe serve"},it="side",add="59b92c48"},{q="Why is Guard Howe here?",a="Guard Howe is stationed just south of the Lakeshire bridge to watch the perimeter of the town. Redridge is besieged by gnolls and encroaching Blackrock orcs, making the bridge a vital crossing and an essential choke point to defend from sudden attacks.",al={"why is guard howe in lakeshire","guard howe post","why guard howe bridge"},it="why_here",add="d5289960"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Stormwind gives Lakeshire little direct aid, so frontline guards like Howe rely on visiting Alliance champions to keep the Blackrock orcs from overrunning the town."},kw={"blackrock bounty","blackrock orcs","guard howe","howe","lakeshire","redridge"},rel={"quest:128","subzone:lakeshire","zone:redridge"},src={"Guard Howe"}}
E["npc:magistrate-solomon"] = {t="npc",n="Magistrate Solomon",z="redridge",s="Lakeshire looks to Magistrate Solomon as gnolls and orcs close in. From the town hall, he governs local affairs and pleads with Stormwind for military aid, but the capital is distracted and gives no help.",h="Lakeshire looks to Magistrate Solomon as gnolls and orcs close in.",sec={{t="A Town Under Siege",b="Magistrate Solomon governs Lakeshire as danger closes around the town. Redridge and Shadowhide gnolls prowl the surrounding hills, while Blackrock orcs descend from the north in organized warbands. Solomon and Marshal Marris work to keep order and muster a defense, but Lakeshire's guards and militia are stretched to their limit.",sp=0},{t="Appeals to Deaf Ears",b="Magistrate Solomon has sent messengers across the kingdom, pleading for aid from Westfall, Darkshire, and Stormwind. The replies bring little hope. Westfall struggles under the Defias Brotherhood, Duskwood faces its own creeping terrors, and Stormwind City refuses to send troops to the eastern frontier. Lakeshire is left to defend itself.",sp=0},{t="The Court's Refusal",b="Magistrate Solomon sends a warning to Highlord Bolvar Fordragon when evidence links the Blackrock orcs to the black dragonflight. Royal advisor Lady Katrana Prestor dismisses Solomon's pleas as wild exaggeration. Guided by her counsel and limited by Stormwind's thinly spread forces, Bolvar refuses to commit the Stormwind Army and gives Solomon royal sanction to deputize independent mercenaries.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Magistrate Solomon?",a="Magistrate Solomon leads Lakeshire's civil affairs and presides over the Court of Lakeshire. From the town hall, he oversees the town's administration and organizes its defense against gnolls and orcs.",al={"magistrate solomon lore","who is solomon","lakeshire leader"},it="identity"},{q="Why can't Stormwind send troops to help him?",a="Stormwind's military is already stretched thin across several troubled regions. When Solomon appeals for aid, Highlord Bolvar Fordragon is influenced by royal advisor Lady Katrana Prestor, who questions Solomon's reports and discourages sending regular troops to Redridge.",al={"why no stormwind army","why won't stormwind help lakeshire","bolvar aid redridge"},sp=1},{q="Did Ironforge try to send help?",a="Yes. At Solomon's plea, King Magni Bronzebeard sent a relief contingent led by Princess Moira Bronzebeard. The expedition never reached Redridge; it was ambushed and captured in the Burning Steppes.",al={"dwarf reinforcements lakeshire","ironforge help redridge","moira bronzebeard lakeshire"},sp=1,it="allies"},{q="What threats are troubling Lakeshire?",a="Lakeshire faces Redridge and Shadowhide gnolls in its hills and on its roads, along with Blackrock orcs raiding south from Stonewatch Keep and the Burning Steppes.",al={"what is attacking lakeshire","redridge enemies","why is solomon worried"},it="threat"},{q="Who works with Solomon to defend the town?",a="Solomon works chiefly with Marshal Marris, who directs the local town guard. With no regular reinforcements, the two officials enlist and deputize traveling adventurers to push back the threats.",al={"lakeshire defenders","marshal marris and solomon"},it="ties"},{q="Why does Solomon send couriers to Darkshire and Westfall?",a="Solomon sends couriers to Darkshire and Westfall in hopes of forming mutual aid pacts with nearby Alliance settlements. Westfall is held in the grip of the Defias Brotherhood, while Duskwood is overwhelmed by undead and feral beasts; neither can spare a defender.",al={"messenger to darkshire","messenger to westfall","solomon aid other towns"},it="motive"},{q="Whose side is Magistrate Solomon on?",a="Solomon is loyal to the Kingdom of Stormwind and the Grand Alliance. As the civil authority in Lakeshire, he answers to the royal court in Stormwind City, petitioning Highlord Bolvar Fordragon for military support to protect his people.",al={"magistrate solomon faction","who does solomon serve","solomon allegiance"},it="side",add="85afa026"},{q="What does Magistrate Solomon want?",a="Solomon desperately seeks military aid and resources to defend Lakeshire from imminent destruction. Hemmed in by aggressive gnoll packs and the encroaching Blackrock orcs, he wants reinforcements from Stormwind and neighboring settlements—or capable adventurers willing to take the fight to the enemy.",al={"solomon goal","what does solomon need","magistrate solomon motivation"},it="wants",add="c7aa651d"},{q="Why is Magistrate Solomon here in Lakeshire?",a="Solomon presides in Lakeshire's town hall because he is the town's magistrate and the judge of the Court of Lakeshire. He remains at his post despite mounting danger, managing local affairs and organizing the defense of the Redridge Mountains.",al={"why is solomon in redridge","solomon role in lakeshire","magistrate solomon job"},it="why_here",add="dc9ff3b9"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Solomon's abandonment reveals deep fractures within the Alliance of Stormwind, leaving its outer provinces to rely on freelance heroes.",["race:Human"]="As a human traveler, you can hear from Solomon how grim the kingdom's condition is beyond Elwynn Forest's inner borders.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you may see a tragic link to Ironforge's effort to answer Solomon's distress call: the expedition was ambushed, and Princess Moira Bronzebeard was captured."},kw={"blackrock","bolvar","lakeshire","magistrate solomon","marris","prestor","redridge","solomon","town hall"},rel={"subzone:lakeshire-town-hall","subzone:lakeshire","npc:marshal-marris","zone:redridge","topic:stormwind-army","quest:120","quest:169"},src={"Magistrate Solomon"}}
E["npc:marshal-marris"] = {t="npc",n="Marshal Marris",z="redridge",s="At Lakeshire's bridge, Marshal Marris directs a thin guard against the Blackrock advance. With Stormwind's army absent, he turns to visiting fighters to slow the orcs in the Redridge Mountains.",h="At Lakeshire's bridge, Marshal Marris directs a thin guard against the Blackrock advance.",sec={{t="A Town Under Siege",b="Lakeshire faces gnolls to the west and the Blackrock clan to the east. Marshal Marris commands the guard line at the town's main bridge, but his supplies are low and his soldiers are stretched thin. Stormwind has sent no royal reinforcements, leaving Marris to keep the town from being overrun.",sp=0},{t="Breaking the Blackrock Vanguard",b="Marshal Marris knows defense alone cannot save Redridge, so he orders strikes on the orc camps. He sends fighters against Blackrock warriors and shadowcasters, then after Tharil'zun, the commander holding Stonewatch Keep's ruins. Marris aims to break the orcs' command before they can overwhelm Lakeshire.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Marshal Marris?",a="Marshal Marris commands Lakeshire's defense. He keeps watch near the western end of the town's bridge, working to fortify the settlement against attack.",al={"marris","marshal marris lore","who is the guard at lakeshire bridge"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Marshal Marris hiring independent adventurers?",a="Stormwind has sent too few reinforcements to the Redridge Mountains, leaving Lakeshire's guard outnumbered. With gnolls and Blackrock orcs pressing in, Marris hires mercenaries to strike at the threats.",al={"why does marris need help","why no stormwind army"},it="motive"},{q="What threats is Marshal Marris fighting against?",a="Gnolls trouble the outskirts, but Marshal Marris is chiefly fighting the Blackrock orcs holding Stonewatch Keep. Tharil'zun commands them, and their shadowcasters add to the danger facing Lakeshire and the kingdom.",al={"marris enemies","who is attacking lakeshire"},it="threat"},{q="Is Marshal Marris related to Nathanos Marris?",a="Marris is a surname found in the human kingdoms of Lordaeron and Stormwind. No record confirms a family tie between Marshal Marris in Redridge and Nathanos Marris, the famed ranger from the north.",al={"is marris related to nathanos","marris family"},it="ties"},{q="What is Marris's plan to defeat the Blackrock clan?",a="Marris orders fighters to kill Blackrock infantry, collect magical components from their shadowcasters, and enter Stonewatch Keep to kill Tharil'zun.",al={"marris plan","how to beat blackrock orcs"},it="wants"},{q="Where can Marshal Marris be found?",a="Marshal Marris is in Lakeshire, in the Redridge Mountains, at the bridge near the center of town.",al={"marris location","where is marshal marris"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Marshal Marris on?",a="Marshal Marris is a loyal officer of the Kingdom of Stormwind and the Alliance. Stationed at the front line in Lakeshire, he represents the local military authority trying desperately to protect the Redridge Mountains and its citizens from encroaching enemies.",al={"marshal marris faction","who does marris serve","marris alliance or stormwind"},it="side",add="4fad023e"},{q="Why is Marshal Marris here in Lakeshire?",a="Marshal Marris is posted near the Lakeshire bridge to coordinate defenses against the Blackrock orcs spilling out of the mountains. With official reinforcements from Stormwind scarce, he stands guard in Redridge to rally any capable adventurers willing to take the fight to the enemy stronghold.",al={"why is marshal marris in redridge","why is marris here","marshal marris location reason"},it="why_here",add="4230d686"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, Marshal Marris shows how exposed its rural lands are when Stormwind cannot act. Lakeshire must fight to survive on its own.",["race:Human"]="As a human of the kingdom, you can see in Marris a frontier guard holding the line against the Old Horde's remnants.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you know the value of direct martial discipline. Marris sends front-line fighters into Stonewatch to face seasoned Blackrock veterans."},kw={"blackrock","bridge","lakeshire","marris","marshal marris","redridge","stonewatch","tharil'zun"},rel={"subzone:lakeshire","zone:redridge","quest:19","quest:20","quest:115","quest:219"},src={"Marshal Marris"}}
E["npc:martie-jainrose"] = {t="npc",n="Martie Jainrose",z="redridge",s="In Lakeshire, Martie Jainrose tends a garden beside Lake Everstill. She gathers herbs and flowers for the town while wild beasts threaten her plots, and she seems fond of Guard Parker.",h="In Lakeshire, Martie Jainrose tends a garden beside Lake Everstill.",sec={{t="A Garden by the Lake",b="Martie Jainrose tends herbs and flowers for Lakeshire as its herbalist. Blackrock orcs, gnolls, and local brigands threaten the Redridge Mountains, but Martie keeps the town supplied with fresh herbs and floral arrangements. Wild animals disrupt her work, especially Bellygrub, a monstrous boar that often ravages her garden beds. Martie also seems fond of Guard Parker. Parker is courting Darcy, who calls Martie a jealous rival.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Martie Jainrose?",a="Martie Jainrose tends herbs in Lakeshire, in the Redridge Mountains. Her garden lies beside Lake Everstill, where she grows plants and prepares remedies for local residents.",al={"martie jainrose","who is martie","lakeshire herbalist"},it="identity"},{q="What trouble does Martie have with the local wildlife?",a="Bellygrub, a massive and stubborn wild boar, raids Martie's garden. He tramples her plants and eats her herbs before she can harvest them.",al={"martie boar problem","bellygrub garden","who is destroying her garden"},it="conflict"},{q="Who does Martie fancy in Lakeshire?",a="Martie seems fond of Guard Parker, one of Lakeshire's guards. Parker is courting Darcy. When he sends Darcy a bouquet of Martie's daffodils, he asks that Martie not be told who it is for.",al={"martie crush","martie guard parker","delivering daffodils romance"},it="ties"},{q="Whose side is Martie Jainrose on?",a="Martie is a loyal citizen of the Alliance living peacefully in Lakeshire. While she does not fight on the front lines or carry arms, she supports the town and its defenders through her trade as an herbalist.",al={"martie jainrose faction","is martie alliance"},it="side",add="4d2b4277"},{q="What does Martie Jainrose want?",a="Martie wants to tend her garden in peace and pursue her herbal craft without interference. Her immediate nuisance is a massive boar named Bellygrub that keeps trampling her precious crops, and she gladly welcomes any traveler willing to drive the beast away.",al={"martie jainrose goal","what does martie need"},it="wants",add="e745a8a7"},{q="Why is Martie Jainrose in Lakeshire?",a="Lakeshire is Martie's home, where she makes her living cultivating herbs and tending her garden along the tranquil shores of Lake Everstill, despite the rising troubles troubling the surrounding Redridge Mountains.",al={"why is martie in redridge","why is martie jainrose here"},it="why_here",add="6d429f48"}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="As an herbalist traveling through Redridge, you share Martie's care for fragile plants, even as wild boars and encroaching enemies threaten them.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you can see Martie's persistence in Lakeshire. Redridge's people keep up ordinary life while Stormwind leaves the town largely to fend for itself."},kw={"bellygrub","daffodils","guard parker","herbalist","lakeshire","martie jainrose","redridge"},rel={"subzone:lakeshire","zone:redridge","quest:131","quest:130"},src={"Martie Jainrose"}}
E["npc:nida"] = {t="npc",n="Hilary",z="redridge",s="At the Lakeshire docks, Hilary cries over the necklace she lost in Lake Everstill.",h="At the Lakeshire docks, Hilary cries over the necklace she lost in Lake Everstill.",sec={{t="A Child's Lost Keepsake",b="Hilary waits in tears by the Lakeshire pier, afraid her father will be angry. She dropped the necklace he gave her into Lake Everstill, and hopes someone brave will dive in to find it. Gnoll invasions and Blackrock orc warbands press upon Lakeshire, but children there still face troubles of their own.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Hilary?",a="Hilary is a young human girl in Lakeshire, often found crying near the docks.",al={"who is nida","nida lakeshire","crying girl lakeshire"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Hilary crying?",a="Hilary cries because the necklace her father bought for her slipped into Lake Everstill, and she fears his anger when he learns it is missing.",al={"why is she crying","why is nida sad","nida crying sound"},it="wants"},{q="Who is trying to help her find the necklace?",a="Her playmate Shawn sees her distress and asks passing adventurers to dive into Lake Everstill for her necklace.",al={"who helps nida","nida friend","who gives nida quest"},it="ties"},{q="Where is the lost necklace located?",a="The necklace lies underwater in Lake Everstill, near the Lakeshire docks where Hilary dropped it.",al={"where is nidas necklace","necklace location lake everstill"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Hilary on?",a="Hilary is a young human child living peacefully under the protection of the Alliance in Lakeshire. She takes no part in politics or soldiering, simply living her childhood among the local townsfolk beside Lake Everstill.",al={"nida faction","is nida alliance","whose side is nida on"},it="side",add="7ae322dc"},{q="Why is Hilary in Lakeshire?",a="Lakeshire is Hilary's home. She lives in the lakeside settlement with her family and spends her days playing around the docks and shoreline alongside her childhood friend, Shawn.",al={"why is nida here","why is nida in lakeshire","what is nida doing here"},it="why_here",add="3c3e0c86"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As the Redridge Mountains face larger troubles, helping Hilary brings a small measure of warmth and innocence to Lakeshire."},kw={"child","hilary","lake everstill","lakeshire","necklace","nida","redridge","shawn"},rel={"quest:3741","subzone:lakeshire","zone:redridge"},src={"Nida"}}
E["npc:smith-argus"] = {t="npc",n="Smith Argus",z="redridge",s="At Goldshire's forge, Smith Argus keeps travelers and local smiths supplied. He repairs gear, teaches new smiths, and sends horseshoes to Redridge while coordinating with Stormwind craftsmen.",h="At Goldshire's forge, Smith Argus keeps travelers and local smiths supplied.",sec={{t="The Anvil of Goldshire",b="Smith Argus works the forge near the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire. Gnolls, kobolds, and Defias bandits threaten the area, but Argus keeps the local militia and passing adventurers equipped. He mends armor and makes sturdy tools. As a blacksmithing trainer, he teaches new smiths to work copper and bronze.",sp=0},{t="Inter-Town Trade and Demands",b="Goldshire's central position makes Smith Argus a link in Stormwind's regional supply. Craftsmen in nearby settlements turn to him for specialized gear and raw materials. Farrier Verner Osgood in Redridge depends on Argus for crafted horseshoes for pack animals and cavalry. Metalworkers in Stormwind's Dwarven District also arrange deliveries through him.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Smith Argus?",a="Smith Argus works at the outdoor anvil and forge behind the armor shop in Goldshire, near the Lion's Pride Inn in central Elwynn Forest.",al={"argus location","where is smith argus","smith argus elwynn"},it="why_here",gp=true},{q="What services does Smith Argus provide?",a="Argus teaches new blacksmiths the fundamentals. His Classic title is Journeyman Blacksmith.",al={"what does argus teach","argus trainer","goldshire blacksmith trainer"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Why does a blacksmith in Redridge send me to Smith Argus?",a="Verner Osgood, a craftsman in Lakeshire, needs horseshoes to keep supply wagons and mounts moving against the Blackrock orc threat. He contracts Argus in Goldshire to forge and supply them.",al={"the price of shoes quest","verner horseshoes","why argus horseshoes"},it="ties"},{q="What is Argus's connection to Stormwind City?",a="Argus coordinates supply runs with dwarven smiths in Stormwind City, including Grimand Elmore in the Dwarven District.",al={"elmore's task","stormwind gryphon argus"},it="ties"},{q="Can Smith Argus train advanced or expert blacksmithing?",a="Argus teaches the early stages of blacksmithing. Advanced techniques require more experienced masters in larger settlements.",al={"argus expert blacksmith","how high can argus train"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Does Smith Argus belong to any particular guild?",a="Argus is a loyal subject of the Kingdom of Stormwind and belongs to the local craftsmen community serving the Alliance in Elwynn Forest.",al={"argus faction","argus guild"},it="side"},{q="Who is Smith Argus?",a="Smith Argus is a blacksmith serving the Kingdom of Stormwind from the forge in Goldshire. A reliable fixture in Elwynn Forest, he shapes iron and steel for local defenders while training aspiring craftsmen and maintaining supply lines with fellow smiths across human lands.",al={"who is argus","smith argus lore","who is smith argus"},it="identity",add="07d5dba5"},{q="Whose side is Smith Argus on?",a="Smith Argus is loyal to the Kingdom of Stormwind and the Alliance. Stationed at the bustling crossroads of Goldshire, he works closely with regional craftsmen to keep Stormwind's outlying settlements supplied and fortified against gathering threats.",al={"smith argus faction","argus alliance or horde","who does argus serve"},it="side",add="79448098"},{q="Why is Smith Argus here?",a="Argus operates the vital forge in Goldshire, positioning him directly along the trade route linking Stormwind City to Redridge and Westfall. From here, he can readily supply regional outposts, shoe horses, and instruct new smiths essential to the kingdom's defense.",al={"why is argus in goldshire","what brought smith argus here"},it="why_here",add="bbf4c38d"},{q="What does Smith Argus want?",a="Smith Argus wants to keep his forge running smoothly and maintain active trade with distant colleagues like Verner Osgood in Redridge. Whether fulfilling specialized orders for horseshoes or exchanging technical shipments, he works to ensure the kingdom's settlements remain well-equipped.",al={"argus motive","what does argus need","smith argus goals"},it="wants",add="d8765a7e"}},ang={["profession:Blacksmithing"]="For Alliance characters starting in Elwynn, Argus may be their first forge teacher. He teaches initial recipes for rough copper gear and useful items.",["profession:Mining"]="Miners bring metal to Goldshire's forge, where Argus teaches new smiths to shape it into useful tools.",["race:Human"]="Argus reflects the hard work of Elwynn's tradesmen amid political neglect and bandit unrest."},kw={"blacksmith","elwynn forest","forge","goldshire","horseshoes","lion's pride","smith argus","trainer","verner osgood"},rel={"subzone:goldshire","zone:elwynn","quest:118","quest:119","quest:1097","quest:6181","zone:redridge"},src={"Smith Argus"}}
E["npc:verner-osgood"] = {t="npc",n="Verner Osgood",z="redridge",s="Outside Lakeshire’s smithy, Verner Osgood keeps the forge working. He balances local trade with the Stormwind Guard’s demands for horseshoes, weapons, and armor as gnolls raid the hills.",h="Outside Lakeshire’s smithy, Verner Osgood keeps the forge working.",sec={{t="The Anvil of Lakeshire",b="At Lakeshire’s forge, Verner Osgood makes horseshoes and other supplies for the town. His stock is constantly taken to make weapons and armor for the Stormwind Guard. With the kingdom’s forces stretched thin and local garrisons short on supplies, Verner carries much of the burden of keeping Redridge’s defenders equipped.",sp=0},{t="A Plague of Gnolls",b="Gnoll raids threaten Verner’s work as well as the town’s horses. Packs ambush livestock in the Redridge hills and seize working horses that stray beyond Lakeshire. Verner recruits travelers to hunt the marauders and their packleader, Yowler.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Verner Osgood?",a="Verner Osgood tends the forge in Lakeshire, making metalwork and shoes for horses while meeting the local garrison’s heavy demands for equipment.",al={"verner osgood","lakeshire blacksmith","who is verner"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Verner low on horseshoes and iron?",a="Iron supplies are continually requisitioned to make weapons and armor for the Stormwind Guard in Redridge, leaving Verner barely enough metal to shoe the town’s horses.",al={"verner out of iron","price of shoes quest lore","why no horseshoes"}},{q="What problem does Verner have with the gnolls?",a="Gnoll raiders near Lakeshire seize Verner’s horses whenever they stray beyond town. He hires travelers to protect his livelihood and take retribution by hunting the packs.",al={"verner gnoll problem","why does verner hate gnolls"},it="conflict"},{q="Who is Yowler and why does Verner want him dead?",a="Yowler leads the local gnoll packs in the hills. Verner wants him slain to break the raiders’ coordination and stop them from terrorizing the town and killing his horses.",al={"who is yowler","verner yowler quest"},it="target"},{q="What is Verner's connection to Magistrate Solomon?",a="Verner works under Magistrate Solomon’s civic authority in Lakeshire, balancing civilian craft with the civic and military needs of the magistrate’s beleaguered administration.",al={"verner magistrate solomon","verner and the town leadership"},it="ties"},{q="Does Verner have family in Stormwind?",a="Verner shares his surname with Stormwind tradesmen Donal and Basil Osgood, suggesting an established lineage of working-class human craftsmen across the region.",al={"verner relatives","osgood family"},it="ties"},{q="Whose side is Verner Osgood on?",a="Verner is firmly loyal to the Alliance and the township of Lakeshire. As the settlement's blacksmith, he devotes much of his iron and labor to outfitting the local garrison and keeping the Stormwind Army supplied, even when it leaves his own shop short on raw materials.",al={"verner alliance","who does verner osgood serve","verner osgood faction"},it="side",add="55e99553"},{q="What does Verner Osgood want?",a="Verner wants to protect Lakeshire and keep his forge running. His immediate priority is securing enough iron to shoe his horses, replenishing his workshop's depleted resources, and seeing the surrounding gnoll packs wiped out so they can no longer slaughter livestock and threaten the town.",al={"verner osgood goals","what does verner need","verner osgood motive"},it="wants",add="238f7baf"},{q="Why is Verner Osgood in Lakeshire?",a="Verner lives and works in Lakeshire as the town's resident blacksmith. He tends the smithy by the lake, forging gear for local defenders, outfitting draft animals, and trying to maintain normal trade despite the constant threats closing in on Redridge.",al={"why is verner here","verner osgood location","why is verner in redridge"},it="why_here",add="2b67bbb2"}},ang={["profession:Blacksmithing"]="As a blacksmith, Verner balances civilian horse shoeing with the harsh quotas imposed by garrison defense.",["faction:Alliance"]="Lakeshire depends on local craftsmen like Verner to endure while Stormwind’s military aid remains dangerously constrained.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you share the resilience of Stormwind’s common folk, holding ground against gnolls and shortages alike."},kw={"blacksmith","gnolls","horses","lakeshire","magistrate solomon","redridge","verner osgood","yowler"},rel={"subzone:lakeshire","zone:redridge","quest:118","quest:126","quest:124","npc:magistrate-solomon","topic:stormwind-guard","topic:gnoll"},src={"Verner Osgood"}}
E["npc:watch-captain-parker"] = {t="npc",n="Watch Captain Parker",z="redridge",s="At Three Corners, Watch Captain Parker guards the road and travelers bound for Lakeshire. He patrols the junction and watches the gnoll packs gathering nearby, an early line of defense for those heading into town.",h="At Three Corners, Watch Captain Parker guards the road and travelers bound for Lakeshire.",sec={{t="On Guard at Three Corners",b="At Three Corners, Watch Captain Parker watches the roads between Elwynn Forest, Duskwood, and Redridge. Stormwind has few troops to spare, and little official help reaches the region. Parker and other lone watchmen must keep the crossroads clear of bandits, prowling predators, and raiding gnolls.",sp=0},{t="Assessing the Gnoll Threat",b="Gnoll camps gathering north and east of Parker’s post draw his attention. As the packs press closer to the road, he sends able-bodied travelers to warn Deputy Feldon in Lakeshire. The Redridge gnolls grow bolder, threatening supply convoys and refugees seeking shelter in town.",sp=0},{t="A Touch of Warmth",b="A lonely roadside post can be grim, yet kindness reaches Three Corners. Darcy, a server at the Lakeshire Inn, sends Parker a warm lunch while he patrols. Touched by her kindness, Parker asks the traveler who brought it to fetch a bouquet from Lakeshire’s herbalist and take it back to Darcy. He asks that the herbalist not be told who the flowers are from or for.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Guard Parker located?",a="Parker is stationed at Three Corners, where roads meet in southwestern Redridge Mountains near the crossings to Duskwood and Elwynn Forest.",al={"parker location","where is parker","find guard parker"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is Parker stationed all the way out at Three Corners?",a="Parker patrols the southern roads from Three Corners and watches the encroaching gnoll packs, helping keep travel and supply routes open to Lakeshire.",al={"parker duties","why is parker alone","three corners guard"},it="why_here"},{q="What threats is Parker monitoring in Redridge?",a="Parker watches the Redridge gnolls threatening the highway and stays alert to Blackrock orcs at Stonewatch and Shadowhide gnolls near the Tower of Ilgalar.",al={"redridge threats","what enemies are near parker","gnoll threat redridge"},it="threat"},{q="What is Parker's relationship with Darcy?",a="Darcy works at the Lakeshire Inn and sends Parker a hot lunch at his remote post. In return, Parker asks the traveler who brought it to fetch flowers from the town herbalist for her, as thanks and a sign of his affection.",al={"darcy and parker","who is darcy","a free lunch quest lore"},it="ties"},{q="Why doesn't Parker receive reinforcements from Stormwind?",a="Stormwind sends little help to Redridge while King Varian Wrynn is missing and the capital is caught in political paralysis. Local guards and magistrates must rely on roaming adventurers.",al={"why no stormwind army","stormwind aid redridge","parker reinforcements"}},{q="What quests does Guard Parker offer?",a="Parker asks travelers to report the gnoll camps gathering near the road to Deputy Feldon in Lakeshire. He also arranges for fresh flowers to be carried to Darcy at the Lakeshire Inn.",al={"parker quests","quests from parker"},gp=true},{q="Who is Watch Captain Parker?",a="Parker is a stalwart member of the Lakeshire town guard tasked with keeping watch over the approaches to the Redridge Mountains. Stationed out at Three Corners along the crossroads between Elwynn, Duskwood, and Redridge, he patrols the outlying roads to monitor enemy movements and safeguard travelers journeying toward Lakeshire.",al={"who is guard parker","who is parker","watch captain parker"},it="identity",add="bec4d61f"},{q="Whose side is Watch Captain Parker on?",a="He is loyal to the Kingdom of Stormwind and serves the township of Lakeshire as part of the local Redridge guard. He stands ready to assist any Alliance champion willing to defend the embattled region against hostile gnolls and orcs.",al={"parker faction","is parker alliance","who does parker serve"},it="side",add="fd65fed3"},{q="What does Watch Captain Parker want?",a="Parker wants to keep the encroaching gnolls from overrunning the vital crossroads and pushing deeper into Redridge. Besieged by hostile forces, he seeks capable adventurers to scout the surrounding wilderness, culled the gnoll packs, and carry status reports back to his superiors in Lakeshire.",al={"parker goal","what does parker need","parker motive"},it="wants",add="39103803"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance sentry, Parker shows how a stretched frontier defense struggles to protect its own borders.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you can see in Parker an ordinary sentry trying to hold the kingdom’s outlying villages together during a national crisis.",["profession:Herbalism"]="As a herbalist, you can find quiet value in the fresh blooms growing across the Redridge hillsides, which Parker seeks for Darcy."},kw={"darcy","gnolls","guard parker","lakeshire","parker","redridge","three corners","watch captain parker"},rel={"subzone:three-corners","zone:redridge","subzone:lakeshire","subzone:lakeshire-inn","quest:129","quest:130","quest:244","topic:gnoll"},src={"Watch Captain Parker"}}
E["quest:115"] = {t="quest",n="Shadow Magic",z="redridge",s="Marshal Marris calls for action against Shadow Magic in Redridge. Blackrock shadowcasters carry demon-tainted midnight orbs that turn dark energies against Lakeshire's defenders. The orbs must be taken from them and destroyed to protect the town's line.",h="Marshal Marris calls for action against Shadow Magic in Redridge.",sec={{t="A Sinister Arsenal",b="Blackrock strength has always rested on brute force, but the clan's raids in the Redridge Mountains now bring a darker threat. Shadowcasters wield dark powers and channel fel and shadow energies through demon-tainted midnight orbs. These artifacts have dealt terrible losses to the local militia, worsening a war already turning against the defenders.",sp=0},{t="Containing the Taint",b="Marshal Marris directs Lakeshire's strained defense from the town center, and he knows ordinary steel cannot easily overcome dark relics. If the Blackrock orcs keep their midnight orbs, Redridge's eastern borders may collapse. Marris orders the shadowcasters slain and the orbs seized so the demonic relics can be destroyed, not put to use.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What are midnight orbs?",a="Midnight orbs are demon-tainted conduits carried by Blackrock shadowcasters. They focus dark magic into devastating blows against Redridge's mortal defenders.",al={"midnight orb","what is a midnight orb","what do midnight orbs do"},it="item"},{q="Why does Marshal Marris want these orbs?",a="Marshal Marris wants the orbs taken from the battlefield to cripple the Blackrock shadowcasters' offensive power. He plans to have the demonic relics safely disposed of and destroyed.",al={"why collect midnight orbs","marris orbs","marris plan for orbs"},it="motive"},{q="Who are the Blackrock shadowcasters?",a="Blackrock shadowcasters are orcish spellcasters who wield shadow and fel-tainted magic. They support the clan's brute warriors with magical artillery and curses.",al={"blackrock shadowcasters","who uses shadow magic","blackrock casters"},it="target"},{q="Where are the shadowcasters found?",a="Blackrock shadowcasters hold camps and fortified positions throughout the northeastern Redridge Mountains.",al={"where are shadowcasters","shadowcaster location","blackrock shadowcaster camps"},it="target",gp=true},{q="Will Lakeshire study or use the orbs?",a="No. Marshal Marris considers the orbs dangerous and demon-tainted, and says the world would be better off without them. He wants them destroyed at once.",al={"will lakeshire use the orbs","can the alliance use the orbs","are orbs useful"},it="motive"},{q="Why is demonic magic appearing in Redridge?",a="The Blackrock clan has consorted with dark and fel entities since the days of the Old Horde. Its spellcasters still use demonic relics and shadow magic to bolster the clan's conquests.",al={"why demons in redridge","blackrock demonic taint","fel in redridge"},it="origin"},{q="Why does Marshal Marris need an adventurer instead of his own guards?",a="Lakeshire's local garrison is stretched to its breaking point. With Stormwind withholding reinforcements, Marshal Marris can barely muster enough soldiers to defend the town bridge and keep the roads clear of gnolls and orc scouting parties. Infiltrating enemy strongholds to cut down Blackrock shadowcasters requires an independent adventurer capable of striking behind hostile lines where regular town guards cannot be spared.",al={"why me shadow magic","why does marris need me","why not send the lakeshire guards"},it="why_me",add="809c126b"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Lakeshire is on the brink of being overrun, with virtually no reinforcements from Stormwind. Depriving the Blackrock clan of its dark artillery is crucial to the region's survival.",["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you can see the Blackrock clan's enduring fel roots in the midnight orbs and the raw demonic channeling used by orcish spellcasters.",["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, confronting shadowcasters and securing demon-tainted relics directly fulfills your holy duty to purge demonic corruption from the mortal realm."},kw={"blackrock orcs","demon-tainted","lakeshire","marshal marris","midnight orb","redridge","shadow magic","shadowcaster"},rel={"npc:marshal-marris","zone:redridge","subzone:lakeshire"},m={start="Marshal Marris",level="23",faction="Alliance",id=115},src={"Shadow Magic"}}
E["quest:116"] = {t="quest",n="Dry Times",z="redridge",s="Barkeep Daniels needs drink for Lakeshire's inn while Blackrock orcs keep the town under siege. The roads are unsafe, and the usual supplies have stopped coming.",h="Barkeep Daniels needs drink for Lakeshire's inn while Blackrock orcs keep the town under siege.",sec={{t="A Town Under Siege",b="Blackrock orcs descend from Stonewatch Keep, pressing Lakeshire hard. With supply lines cut and roads unsafe, the inn is running low on drink. Barkeep Daniels turns to travelers who can cross the blocked roads and bring supplies back for frightened villagers and the town guards.",sp=0},{t="A Grand Tour of the Kingdom",b="Daniels needs drink from across Stormwind's lands. You can find Merlot in the capital, Sweet Rum at the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire, Moonshine in Darkshire in Duskwood, and Thunderbrew Lager from Grimbooze Thunderbrew in the hills of Westfall.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is Lakeshire running out of alcohol?",a="Blackrock orcs have disrupted Redridge's trade and stopped the supply caravans. Daniels's usual shipments are overdue, and his inn is running dry while Lakeshire faces the strain of war.",al={"why dry times","why no booze lakeshire","barkeep daniels problem"},it="motive"},{q="Where do I find all the drinks Barkeep Daniels needs?",a="You can find Merlot in Stormwind City, Sweet Rum in Goldshire in Elwynn Forest, Moonshine in Darkshire in Duskwood, and Thunderbrew Lager from Grimbooze Thunderbrew in the hills of Westfall.",al={"dry times drink locations","where to buy merlot moonshine rum","where to get drinks for daniels"},gp=true},{q="Who is Grimbooze Thunderbrew?",a="Grimbooze Thunderbrew is a dwarven brewer in the hills of Westfall. Daniels wants his lager, and you need to secure a fresh keg for Grimbooze first.",al={"grimbooze location","where is grimbooze thunderbrew","westfall thunderbrew"},it="people"},{q="Who is Barkeep Daniels?",a="Barkeep Daniels runs the inn in Lakeshire. With Blackrock orcs threatening the town, he hires travelers to bring supplies along the dangerous roads.",al={"barkeep daniels","lakeshire innkeeper","who gives dry times"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Daniels need drinks from so many different regions?",a="Daniels serves refugees, local militiamen, and passing adventurers. He needs dwarven lager, fine wine from the capital, and spirits from Duskwood and Elwynn.",al={"why so many drinks","why visit duskwood and westfall"},it="purpose"},{q="What reward does Barkeep Daniels give for making the run?",a="Daniels reimburses your travel expenses with coins and gives you a hand-crafted cloak sewn by his wife for braving the contested roads.",al={"dry times reward","what does daniels give"},gp=true},{q="Why does Barkeep Daniels need your help fetching drinks?",a="Daniels cannot leave his tavern unattended, especially with Lakeshire on edge and patrons desperate for a drink to forget their troubles. Meanwhile, the local guardsmen and town militia are entirely consumed with fending off the Blackrock orc invasion pressing down from the north. Only a roaming adventurer has the freedom to safely travel across the kingdom's dangerous highways to gather supplies.",al={"why me dry times","why does daniels need an adventurer","why send me for drinks"},it="why_me",add="266c2dd6"},{q="What is the Keg of Thunderbrew for?",a="The keg contains potent Thunderbrew Lager brewed by Grimbooze Thunderbrew out in the hills of Westfall. Barkeep Daniels needs it to replenish Lakeshire's dwindling cellars, giving the frightened townsfolk and beleaguered defenders a stout dwarven ale to keep their spirits high against the Blackrock threat.",al={"keg of thunderbrew dry times","why keg of thunderbrew","what is thunderbrew lager for"},it="item",add="8f4cd8c5"},{q="What is the Skin of Sweet Rum for?",a="This skin of Sweet Rum comes directly from the Lion's Pride Inn down in Goldshire. Daniels includes it in his emergency liquor run to satisfy his patrons' taste for sweeter spirits while the town's standard supply lines remain severed by the orcs.",al={"skin of sweet rum dry times","why sweet rum","what is sweet rum for"},it="item",add="0ca5cd6a"},{q="What is the Cask of Merlot for?",a="Sourced from the heart of Stormwind City, this cask of fine red wine provides a touch of civilized comfort amidst the grim frontier war. Daniels needs it to ensure his tavern cellar does not run completely dry while the roads remain under siege.",al={"cask of merlot dry times","why cask of merlot","what is merlot for"},it="item",add="41f763cb"},{q="What is the Bottle of Moonshine for?",a="Brewed in the shadowy hamlet of Darkshire, this bottle of harsh Moonshine provides a stiff, unrefined kick. Barkeep Daniels brings it in to cater to patrons who need something exceptionally strong to steady their nerves against the constant threat of invasion.",al={"bottle of moonshine dry times","why bottle of moonshine","what is moonshine for"},it="item",add="88b6ac2e"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance courier, you see how unsafe roads in Redridge disrupt daily life. You help reconnect trade between Stormwind, Elwynn, Westfall, Duskwood, and Redridge.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you know human taverns depend on dwarven brewing, even during an orc invasion. Couriers travel to Westfall for Grimbooze Thunderbrew's renowned lager."},kw={"barkeep daniels","dry times","grimbooze thunderbrew","lakeshire","merlot","moonshine","redridge","sweet rum","thunderbrew lager"},rel={"npc:barkeep-daniels","quest:117","npc:grimbooze-thunderbrew","subzone:lakeshire","zone:redridge","subzone:darkshire","subzone:goldshire","zone:westfall"},m={start="Barkeep Daniels",level="15",faction="Alliance",id=116,ri={"Bottle of Moonshine","Cask of Merlot","Keg of Thunderbrew","Skin of Sweet Rum"}},src={"Dry Times"}}
E["quest:118"] = {t="quest",n="The Price of Shoes",z="redridge",s="Verner Osgood has run out of iron in Lakeshire, where the guard's gear needs constant repair. He sends you west across Elwynn Forest to ask Smith Argus in Goldshire for horseshoes.",h="Verner Osgood has run out of iron in Lakeshire, where the guard's gear needs constant repair.",sec={{t="A Frontier Strained to the Limit",b="Lakeshire faces gnolls, orcs, and murlocs, while Stormwind sends little help. The garrison fights each day to keep the town from falling, and battle quickly wears down its gear. Verner Osgood spends nearly every waking hour repairing dented breastplates, reshaping dulled swords, and keeping the guards clad in iron. The work has exhausted his supply of raw materials.",sp=0},{t="Supply Lines to Elwynn",b="Without iron, even ordinary work in a frontier town can stop. Horses without shoes cannot carry messengers swiftly or haul supplies along Redridge's rocky paths. Verner swallows his pride and sends you west along the Three Corners road to Goldshire. Smith Argus there still has regular access to the kingdom's mineral stores.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is Verner out of iron?",a="Lakeshire's guards face constant assaults from hostile wildlife, gnolls, and Blackrock orcs. Verner has used his iron to repair their battered armor and weapons, leaving none for civilian needs.",al={"why no iron","verner out of metal","lakeshire iron shortage"},it="motive"},{q="Who is Smith Argus?",a="Smith Argus is Goldshire's blacksmith in Elwynn Forest. His forge has easier access to raw ingots and supplies than frontier towns such as Lakeshire.",al={"argus goldshire","who is argus","blacksmith in goldshire"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Lakeshire lack supplies from Stormwind?",a="Stormwind's rulers are caught in political inertia while King Varian Wrynn is missing. The House of Nobles withholds troops and funds, leaving frontier towns such as Lakeshire to fend for themselves with whatever regional trade they can muster.",al={"why no help from stormwind","lakeshire ignored","stormwind neglect"},it="history"},{q="Why are horseshoes so critical in Redridge?",a="Redridge's rocky terrain quickly wears down unshod hooves. Without horseshoes, couriers, supply wagons, and patrol mounts can go lame, cutting Lakeshire off from the rest of the kingdom.",al={"why need horseshoes","why shoes matter"},it="purpose"},{q="What happens after reaching Smith Argus?",a="Argus accepts Verner's note and gives you horseshoes to carry back to Lakeshire. The town's struggle to hold out continues.",al={"next quest","what after argus"},it="next_step"},{q="Where is Smith Argus located in Goldshire?",a="Smith Argus works at the outdoor forge near the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire, just off Elwynn Forest's main road.",al={"where is argus","argus location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Verner send you instead of going himself or sending a guard?",a="Verner is Lakeshire's primary smith and cannot abandon his forge while town defenses are stretched thin. Redridge is already under siege by gnolls and orcs, leaving every local guard needed on the ramparts and along the bridge. With local supply lines completely strained, traveling all the way through Elwynn Forest falls to able traveling adventurers like you.",al={"why send me","why doesnt verner go","why not send a guard"},it="why_me",add="24418d93"}},ang={["profession:Blacksmithing"]="A frontier smith must spend scarce materials keeping soldiers alive, leaving little for ordinary farmsteads.",["faction:Alliance"]="Lakeshire depends on Goldshire for supplies, showing how thinly stretched the kingdom's logistics are under Stormwind's regency."},kw={"elwynn","goldshire","horseshoes","iron","lakeshire","redridge","smith argus","verner osgood"},rel={"npc:verner-osgood","npc:smith-argus","quest:119","zone:redridge","subzone:goldshire","topic:stormwind-guard","topic:stormwind-kingdom","quest:124"},m={start="Verner Osgood",["end"]="Smith Argus",level="18",faction="Alliance",id=118},src={"The Price of Shoes"}}
E["quest:120"] = {t="quest",n="Messenger to Stormwind",z="redridge",s="In Lakeshire, Magistrate Solomon sends an urgent plea for help to Stormwind. Gnolls and Blackrock orcs press around the town, and he has no garrison troops to spare for the journey. He entrusts a traveler with The State of Lakeshire for General Marcus Jonathan in Stormwind City.",h="In Lakeshire, Magistrate Solomon sends an urgent plea for help to Stormwind.",sec={{t="A Cry Across the Mountains",b="Gnolls contest every road from Lakeshire, while Blackrock orcs raid from the north. The town's guardsmen are stretched beyond their limits. Magistrate Solomon cannot spare fighting men for the days-long ride to the capital, so a traveler carries his official plea for regular troops to the city gates.",sp=0},{t="Bureaucracy and the High Seat",b="General Marcus Jonathan commands Stormwind's defense. Solomon's report reaches him, and he respects the magistrate's leadership and recognizes the urgency. Yet army protocol bars Jonathan from mobilizing troops without a royal directive. Redridge's defense must wait until he consults the young King Anduin and the regency council.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Magistrate Solomon need a messenger?",a="Gnolls and Blackrock orcs threaten Lakeshire, and every local guardsman is needed to defend the town and hold the bridge. Magistrate Solomon entrusts travelers with his urgent appeals for aid.",al={"why send me","why a messenger","solomon messenger"},it="motive"},{q="What is in 'The State of Lakeshire' report?",a="The State of Lakeshire is an official account of the crisis in the Redridge Mountains. It details rising enemy numbers, casualties, and the town's imminent fall without regular soldiers from the capital.",al={"state of lakeshire","solomon report","what is the letter"},it="item"},{q="Who is General Marcus Jonathan?",a="General Marcus Jonathan commands the Stormwind City Guard and is a high-ranking leader in the Stormwind Army. He monitors the city gates and reports directly to Highlord Bolvar Fordragon and the crown.",al={"marcus jonathan","who is the general","general of stormwind"},it="identity"},{q="Why doesn't General Jonathan send soldiers right away?",a="General Jonathan cannot deploy the army on his own authority. He must bring Solomon's report before the King and regency council for an official royal mandate before troops can march.",al={"why no troops","where are reinforcements","jonathan response"},it="conflict"},{q="Is the road between Lakeshire and Stormwind safe?",a="No. Aggressive gnoll bands and Defias highwaymen plague the paths through Redridge and into Elwynn, making the journey perilous for lone messengers.",al={"road to stormwind","safe travel","redridge road"},it="danger"},{q="Does Stormwind end up sending help?",a="Political turmoil and delay in the capital hold back any real army response. Lakeshire and Magistrate Solomon are left to rely almost entirely on mercenaries and volunteers.",al={"do reinforcements arrive","help for lakeshire"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Magistrate Solomon send an adventurer instead of a town guard?",a="Lakeshire is stretched to its absolute breaking point. The town is under constant pressure from gnolls and Blackrock orcs encroaching from the surrounding hills. Magistrate Solomon simply cannot spare a single sworn defender or town guard from their battle lines without leaving the township's defenses critically compromised. Entrusting an able-bodied adventurer to carry the plea to Stormwind allows every local sentry to remain at their post.",al={"why send me","why lake guards not deliver","why adventurer messenger"},it="why_me",add="3f8e995f"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, Lakeshire's plea reveals the strain between the prosperous capital and border settlements fighting for survival on the kingdom's edges.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you know Redridge is ancestral Stormwind territory. Seeing fellow humans left behind by bureaucratic red tape can sting your patriotism.",["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you carry the desperate's pleas to leaders held back by court politics, testing your duty, your protection of others, and your righteous action."},kw={"general marcus jonathan","lakeshire","magistrate solomon","messenger to stormwind","redridge mountains","reinforcements","stormwind army","the state of lakeshire"},rel={"npc:magistrate-solomon","npc:general-marcus-jonathan","subzone:lakeshire","zone:redridge","topic:stormwind-army","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Magistrate Solomon",["end"]="General Marcus Jonathan",level="14",faction="Alliance",id=120},src={"Messenger to Stormwind"}}
E["quest:122"] = {t="quest",n="Underbelly Scales",z="redridge",s="Verner Osgood needs black dragon whelp underbelly scales to settle his trade debt with Smith Argus of Goldshire. You gather them from young drakes wandering the crags south of Lakeshire. The scales settle Verner’s account and leave enough raw hide to craft a piece of gear.",h="Verner Osgood needs black dragon whelp underbelly scales to settle his trade debt with Smith Argus of...",sec={{t="A Frontier Debt",b="Verner Osgood runs a forge on the outskirts of Lakeshire and often trades with craftsmen beyond the Redridge Mountains. Smith Argus of Goldshire sent him a shipment of horseshoes, but Verner is short on coin. Argus demands valuable dragonhide in payment: the highly prized, softer underbelly scales of the black dragon whelps nesting in the region. Without them, collectors may come from Elwynn Forest to claim the debt.",sp=0},{t="Brood of the Black Flight",b="Black dragon whelps in the Redridge Mountains alarm the local defenders. Gnolls and orcs contest the roads, while the Black Dragonflight nests in the high peaks and its brood wanders the skies south of Lake Everstill. The young predators’ underbelly scales are tough yet pliable. Armorers, smiths, and leatherworkers across the kingdom prize them, if they dare to harvest them.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Verner Osgood need dragon scales?",a="Verner owes Smith Argus of Goldshire for a shipment of horseshoes. Argus demands underbelly scales from black dragon whelps instead of regular coin. Verner needs them delivered quickly, before Argus sends collectors to enforce the debt.",al={"why dragon scales","verner debt","argus scales"},it="motive"},{q="Where are the black dragon whelps found in Redridge?",a="Black dragon whelps commonly roam the rocky crags and valleys south of Lakeshire. They wander across the southern foothills, so hunters often patrol the trails and ridges to spot them in flight.",al={"whelp locations","where are whelps","dragon whelp location redridge"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Smith Argus?",a="Smith Argus is the blacksmith stationed at Goldshire in Elwynn Forest. He provides metalwork and forged goods to nearby settlements, including horseshoes for Verner Osgood in Redridge.",al={"argus goldshire","who is argus","smith argus"},it="people"},{q="Why are black dragon whelps in Redridge Mountains?",a="The Black Dragonflight keeps a presence throughout the Burning Steppes and the surrounding peaks of Redridge. Its whelps hunt and wander south through the mountain passes into the Redridge foothills.",al={"why are there dragons in redridge","black dragons redridge","black flight redridge"},it="target"},{q="What makes underbelly scales special?",a="Underbelly scales are supple and flexible, unlike the thick, rigid scales along a drake’s back. They retain high resistance to heat and punctures, making them useful for specialized leatherworking, tailored reinforcement, and exotic trade goods.",al={"why underbelly scales","scale value","dragonhide quality"},it="item"},{q="Does clearing this debt lead to other tasks for Verner?",a="This follows Verner Osgood’s request after you bring him his horseshoe shipment. Alongside this optional gathering, Verner sends adventurers to hunt gnoll scouts and leaders as the threat in Redridge grows.",al={"what comes next","verner questline","osgood follow up"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Verner ask you to hunt the dragon whelps instead of doing it himself?",a="Verner Osgood is tied down running Lakeshire's busy stables and smithy, while the local guards are fully stretched defending against the surrounding gnoll and orc incursions. Venturing south into the hills to hunt roving black dragon whelps takes skilled adventurers who can track dangerous wildlife and handle themselves in the wilderness.",al={"why does verner need me","why cant verner hunt whelps","why ask me underbelly scales"},it="why_me",add="43de1078"}},ang={["profession:Blacksmithing"]="Smith Argus’s demand shows how smiths barter rare reagents like dragon scales when standard coin is scarce.",["faction:Alliance"]="The Black Dragonflight’s growing threat south of Lakeshire adds to the burdens on Redridge’s already overstretched garrison.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you know trade routes between Elwynn and Redridge supply towns like Lakeshire, though frontier craftsmen often pay steep prices to city merchants."},kw={"black dragon whelp","dragonflight","goldshire","lakeshire","redridge","smith argus","underbelly scales","verner osgood"},rel={"npc:verner-osgood","quest:118","quest:119","quest:124","quest:126","zone:redridge","subzone:lakeshire","subzone:goldshire"},m={start="Verner Osgood",level="18",faction="Alliance",id=122,ri={"Underbelly Whelp Scale"}},src={"Underbelly Scales"}}
E["quest:124"] = {t="quest",n="A Baying of Gnolls",z="redridge",s="Gnolls raid Verner Osgood’s stable in Lakeshire from the Redridge foothills. Blackrock orcs already threaten the region, and Verner asks travelers to drive off the brutes and mystics endangering his horses.",h="Gnolls raid Verner Osgood’s stable in Lakeshire from the Redridge foothills.",sec={{t="Horses on the Ridge",b="Verner Osgood’s stable in Lakeshire has become dangerous to run. Blackrock orcs hold the heights, and gnoll packs roam the ridges around town. Gnoll raiders have reached the northern edge of Verner’s paddocks, preying on horses that wander too close to the bluffs.",sp=0},{t="A Coordinated Menace",b="Gnoll packs north of Lakeshire bring both brute force and primitive spellcraft. Their brutes overwhelm prey while mystics wield wild magic. Thinning their numbers gives the settlement a brief respite, but their aggression points to a greater power higher in the hills.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does Verner Osgood need help with gnolls?",a="Gnolls from the northern ridges have begun reaching Verner’s stables and snatching horses that stray from the paddocks. With Blackrock orcs also threatening the region, he cannot protect his stock alone.",al={"verner problem","why verner wants gnolls killed","lakeshire stable gnolls"},it="motive"},{q="Where are these gnolls located?",a="Redridge brutes and mystics prowl the elevated ridges and foothills directly north and east of Lakeshire, overlooking the town and the road toward the Everstill Bridge.",al={"where are redridge brutes","redridge mystic location","gnolls north of stables"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why are gnolls an issue alongside the Blackrock orcs?",a="Blackrock orcs are Redridge’s main military threat, and local gnoll packs take advantage of the distraction. Lakeshire’s defenders are stretched thin, and Stormwind sends few reinforcements, leaving the predators free to range up to the village perimeter.",al={"orcs and gnolls redridge","why both gnolls and orcs"},it="threat"},{q="What comes after dealing with these gnolls?",a="After the brutes and mystics are thinned, the howling continues in the hills. It points to a greater leadership threat in the surrounding heights.",al={"baying of gnolls follow up","what next after baying of gnolls"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why are mystics particularly dangerous?",a="Redridge mystics use rudimentary nature and elemental magic, turning erratic, feral incantations against trespassers. Their presence among the brutes suggests an organized clan rather than lone scavengers.",al={"redridge mystics lore","gnoll shamans redridge"},it="danger"},{q="Is Stormwind sending soldiers to protect Lakeshire's stables?",a="No. Stormwind’s royal court has left Redridge largely to defend itself amid political turmoil and troop shortages. Magistrate Solomon and citizens like Verner Osgood must recruit wandering adventurers.",al={"stormwind guard redridge","why no guards helping verner"},it="why_me"},{q="Who are the gnolls threatening Verner's horses?",a="You are sent against the Redridge brutes and mystics prowling the hills directly north of Verner Osgood's stables. These feral hyena-folk inhabit the ridges overlooking Lakeshire, taking advantage of the town's distractions to snatch unwary livestock and terrorize the local homesteads.",al={"redridge gnolls","redridge brutes and mystics","what gnolls are attacking lakeshire"},it="target",add="114f5694"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Stormwind’s neglect strains small communities across the southern kingdom. Tradesmen like Verner must hire private help to protect essential supply lines.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you face wild beasts and feral packs in Redridge that have grown bold without organized culls. They threaten domestic animals and travelers."},kw={"gnolls","horses","lakeshire","redridge brute","redridge mountains","redridge mystic","stables","verner osgood"},rel={"npc:verner-osgood","quest:126","quest:122","quest:119","quest:89","topic:gnoll","zone:redridge"},m={start="Verner Osgood",level="20",faction="Alliance",id=124},src={"A Baying of Gnolls"}}
E["quest:125"] = {t="quest",n="The Lost Tools",z="redridge",s="Blackrock fire has sunk Foreman Oslow's tools in Lake Everstill. With Lakeshire under pressure, local hands must maintain its defenses, and the tools shipped from Goldshire are needed to rebuild the shattered bridge.",h="Blackrock fire has sunk Foreman Oslow's tools in Lake Everstill.",sec={{t="A Delivery Gone Awry",b="The Great Bridge no longer connects Lakeshire to Elwynn Forest. A replacement shipment of stonemasonry and carpentry tools came overland from Goldshire, but the wagons could not reach town. The crew loaded the supplies into a rowboat to cross Lake Everstill. A Blackrock orc catapult struck the boat, destroying it and sending Oslow's heavy ironbound toolbox to the lake floor.",sp=0},{t="Hazards of the Deep",b="Lake Everstill holds dangers below its surface. Aggressive murloc tribes prowl the shallows, while predatory threshers hunt in the murky depths. Foreman Oslow needs his tools to resume repairs on the bridge and keep Lakeshire from falling further into ruin.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why were the tools sent by boat in the first place?",a="Blackrock orcs destroyed a large span of the stone bridge over Lake Everstill, so supply wagons from Goldshire could not reach Lakeshire. The crew unloaded the tools and tried to ferry them across the water.",al={"why boat","how did the tools sink","why lake transport"},it="history"},{q="How did the boat sink?",a="Blackrock orcs struck the transport boat with a catapult projectile from the surrounding heights as it crossed Lake Everstill. The boat sank with its cargo.",al={"who destroyed the boat","how did it get hit"},it="conflict"},{q="Who is Foreman Oslow?",a="Foreman Oslow is Lakeshire's chief builder and overseer, responsible for public works and civil maintenance. His most urgent work is rebuilding the ruined bridge.",al={"foreman oslow","oslow role"},it="identity"},{q="What threats are in Lake Everstill?",a="Hostile murloc tribes patrol the shores and ruins, while vicious, carnivorous lake threshers hunt in open water and the deeper depths.",al={"what's in the lake","lake monsters","lake everstill danger"},it="danger"},{q="Why does Lakeshire need these tools so badly?",a="Lakeshire is under siege, cut off from immediate reinforcements and regular shipments. Without heavy tools, Oslow cannot rebuild the bridge or repair the defenses needed against attacking orcs and gnolls.",al={"why are tools important","bridge repair tools"},it="motive"},{q="Where does the quest lead next?",a="After his toolbox is recovered, Foreman Oslow asks adventurers to gather the raw building materials needed to repair the Great Bridge in The Everstill Bridge.",al={"next quest","what after lost tools"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="What is Oslow's Toolbox used for?",a="Oslow's Toolbox holds the heavy iron tools needed to rebuild Lakeshire's ruined infrastructure. With the Blackrock orcs besieging the town and blasting the great bridge into rubble, construction and repairs have completely ground to a halt. Oslow cannot repair the bridge or reinforce the town's defenses without his specialized equipment, leaving Lakeshire vulnerable and cut off until the kit is recovered from the lakebed.",al={"oslows toolbox","what is the toolbox for","foreman oslow tools"},it="item",add="fed346ea"},{q="Why does Foreman Oslow ask an adventurer rather than the town guard?",a="Lakeshire is stretched to its absolute breaking point under an active siege. The few remaining town guards and magistrates are pinned down defending the perimeter from Blackrock orcs, gnolls, and incoming catapult fire. Oslow himself is a builder, not a fighter or diver, and Lake Everstill is swarming with aggressive murlocs and monstrous threshers. He needs a capable traveler willing to brave hostile waters while Lakeshire's defenders hold the line.",al={"why me lost tools","why doesnt oslow get it himself","why not send lakeshire guards"},it="why_me",add="b04d784a"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you help Lakeshire hold the eastern frontier against the Blackrock clan. Civilian builders need their equipment to maintain the Kingdom of Stormwind's defenses.",["profession:Blacksmithing"]="As a blacksmith, you know quality tools are hard to forge under siege. Recovering the specialized smithing and construction implements sent from Goldshire matters to the town."},kw={"catapult","foreman oslow","goldshire","lake everstill","lakeshire","murloc","redridge","thresher","toolbox"},rel={"npc:foreman-oslow","subzone:lake-everstill","quest:89","subzone:lakeshire","zone:redridge","subzone:goldshire","topic:murloc"},m={start="Foreman Oslow",level="16",faction="Alliance",id=125,ri={"Oslow's Toolbox"}},src={"The Lost Tools"}}
E["quest:126"] = {t="quest",n="Howling in the Hills",z="redridge",s="Gnoll calls carry across the hills around Lakeshire, where Verner Osgood offers a bounty on Yowler. Stormwind's forces are stretched thin by the Blackrock orcs, leaving the town to rely on visitors against the gnolls.",h="Gnoll calls carry across the hills around Lakeshire, where Verner Osgood offers a bounty on Yowler.",sec={{t="The Voice in the Heights",b="Gnoll cries still echo through the Redridge hills after lesser gnolls are driven from the paths around Lakeshire. Verner Osgood, the town's farrier, knows the pack will keep raiding while its leader lives. Yowler is a huge, cunning gnoll whose calls direct the pack across the hills. Verner asks for Yowler's paw as proof that the leader has been killed and the calls silenced.",sp=0},{t="A Town Abandoned by the Army",b="Stormwind's eastern border towns face danger with little help from the kingdom's army. King Varian Wrynn is missing, and disputes over the regency have paralyzed high command. Royal soldiers are focused on the Blackrock orc clans in the north, leaving Lakeshire without defenders against gnolls. Townsfolk such as Verner Osgood arrange their own bounties to keep their homes from being overrun.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Yowler?",a="Yowler leads the Redridge gnolls in the hills outside Lakeshire. Verner says he is stronger and more dangerous than the common gnolls, and directs the pack against travelers and homesteads.",al={"yowler","who is the gnoll boss","yowler lore","yowler gnoll"},it="target"},{q="Why is Verner Osgood issuing this bounty instead of the town guard?",a="Verner Osgood offers the bounty because Lakeshire's leadership and militia are overwhelmed by the Blackrock orcs. A local craftsman and stable master, he depends on safe roads for his livelihood and hires wandering mercenaries to face immediate dangers.",al={"why verner","why not magistrate solomon","why osgood hiring"},it="why_me"},{q="Where are the Stormwind soldiers who should be protecting Lakeshire?",a="Stormwind's soldiers are occupied elsewhere. The army is in Redridge to monitor and contain the Blackrock orc clans farther up in the mountains, leaving Lakeshire without support against local wildlife, murlocs, and gnolls.",al={"where is the army","why no stormwind guards","stormwind military lakeshire"},it="threat"},{q="What happens to the Redridge gnolls once Yowler is dead?",a="Yowler's death scatters the gnoll pack's command and blunts its coordinated raids on the town's borders. Gnolls remain a stubborn nuisance in Redridge's craggy heights.",al={"did gnolls leave","what happens after yowler dies"},it="next_step"},{q="What prerequisite quests lead up to this contract?",a="Verner first sends you to secure horse gear in 'The Price of Shoes' and 'Return to Verner.' After you deal with underbelly scales and thin the pack in 'A Baying of Gnolls,' he offers the bounty on Yowler.",al={"yowler quest pre reqs","unlock howling in the hills","chain for howling in the hills"},gp=true},{q="Why does Verner need Yowler's paw as proof?",a="Verner needs Yowler's severed paw as physical proof before paying the bounty. It shows him and Lakeshire's uneasy residents that the beast whose calls echo through the hills has fallen.",al={"why yowler paw","yowlers paw proof"},it="item"},{q="Why does Verner Osgood want Yowler killed?",a="Verner hears the gnolls baying as they prowl the ridges above Lakeshire day and night. With the Stormwind army entirely occupied battling Blackrock orcs, town locals like Verner are left defenseless against roving predators. He believes cutting down Yowler, the ferocious pack leader, will shatter the gnolls' morale and scatter the beasts before they descend directly upon the town.",al={"verner osgood motive","why kill yowler","verner howling in the hills motive"},it="motive",add="f0418674"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance adventurer, you can see how Lakeshire's reliance on mercenaries reflects the strain weakening Stormwind's kingdom.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you can track Yowler in his mountain lair by watching for territorial marks and signs of pack behavior.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you face Yowler, who rules his pack through physical dominance and demands a direct clash of strength."},kw={"blackrock","gnolls","lakeshire","paw","redridge","stormwind army","verner osgood","yowler"},rel={"npc:verner-osgood","quest:124","quest:122","subzone:lakeshire","zone:redridge","topic:gnoll","topic:stormwind-army","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Verner Osgood",level="21",faction="Alliance",id=126,ri={"Yowler's Paw"}},src={"Howling in the Hills"}}
E["quest:127"] = {t="quest",n="Selling Fish",z="redridge",s="Dockmaster Baren pays travelers to bring in spotted sunfish from Lake Everstill. The fish are a Lakeshire staple, but murlocs along the shore make them dangerous to gather.",h="Dockmaster Baren pays travelers to bring in spotted sunfish from Lake Everstill.",sec={{t="A Staple of Lake Everstill",b="Spotted sunfish are a delicate catch prized across the lands around Lake Everstill. Townspeople and passing merchants keep demand high, yet Lakeshire's supplies often run thin despite the fish below the surface. Local threats stretch the town's strength, so even trade in basic goods depends on travelers.",sp=0},{t="Trouble on the Shallows",b="Anglers nearby could usually meet Dockmaster Baren's orders with ease. Now aggressive murloc tribes haunt the shallows and banks, keeping ordinary townsfolk from the water. You can fish while watching for danger, or take sunfish from the foraging murlocs that trouble the shore.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Dockmaster Baren?",a="Dockmaster Baren oversees the docks and boat traffic on Lake Everstill in Lakeshire. He manages the town's water trade and depends on capable travelers to bring in fresh fish and deal with threats around the lake.",al={"baren","who is the dockmaster","dockmaster baren"},it="identity"},{q="Why are spotted sunfish in such high demand?",a="Spotted sunfish are famed across the lands around Lake Everstill, making them a Lakeshire staple and an important trade good. The town's stocks run low because ordinary anglers cannot fish safely while hostile creatures trouble the lake.",al={"why sunfish","spotted sunfish lore","why does lakeshire want fish"},it="why_wanted"},{q="How do murlocs end up with the sunfish?",a="Murloc tribes along Lake Everstill forage and hunt in the shallows. They kill or drive away local fishermen, then gather fish for their camps, where travelers can take the catch instead of fishing for it.",al={"murloc fish","why do murlocs drop fish","murlocs stealing fish"},it="origin"},{q="Where can spotted sunfish be found?",a="Spotted sunfish live in Lake Everstill in Redridge Mountains. You can catch them with a fishing rod or take them from murlocs along the banks and shallows.",al={"where are sunfish","lake everstill fish location","how to get spotted sunfish"},it="place",gp=true},{q="How does this quest fit with Murloc Poachers?",a="Dockmaster Baren offers help with the murloc poachers and the sunfish at the same time. Since murlocs prowl the lake and take its fish, dealing with them can also recover the sunfish they have gathered.",al={"murloc poachers connection","baren other quest","dockmaster quests"}},{q="Is fishing required to help Dockmaster Baren?",a="You need no fishing gear or skill to help Dockmaster Baren. You can angle for sunfish, or, as Baren openly suggests, take the fish by force from the murloc tribes that hunt the lake.",al={"do i need fishing","can i do this without fishing pole","fishing required"},gp=true},{q="Why does Dockmaster Baren need more Spotted Sunfish?",a="Lake Everstill is renowned for its spotted sunfish, creating steady trade and appetites that keep Dockmaster Baren busy on the Lakeshire docks. With his local stock running dangerously low, he needs a fresh batch of ten to fulfill demand and keep his barter trade afloat.",al={"why does baren want fish","dockmaster baren motive","why selling fish"},it="motive",add="2b5f9eab"},{q="What is the Spotted Sunfish used for?",a="Spotted Sunfish are freshwater fish native to Lake Everstill, prized throughout Redridge for their flavor. They serve as a staple local food source and a valuable commodity for Lakeshire's commerce, fetching dependable trade from travelers and residents alike.",al={"what are spotted sunfish","spotted sunfish lore","what is spotted sunfish used for"},it="item",add="d0647bad"}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="As a cook, you can look to Lakeshire's waters for spotted sunfish, a freshwater delicacy prized in the town.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you can help sustain Redridge's food supply, since the Kingdom of Stormwind offers little military aid to the region."},kw={"dockmaster baren","lake everstill","lakeshire","murloc","redridge","selling fish","spotted sunfish"},rel={"subzone:lakeshire","subzone:lake-everstill","quest:150","topic:murloc","zone:redridge"},m={level="21",faction="Alliance",id=127,ri={"Spotted Sunfish"}},src={"Selling Fish"}}
E["quest:128"] = {t="quest",n="Blackrock Bounty",z="redridge",s="In Lakeshire, Blackrock Bounty draws fighters as Blackrock forces gather in northern Redridge. Stormwind sends no royal soldiers, so Magistrate Solomon and Guard Howe offer payment to independent fighters who strike at Blackrock Champions and disrupt the clan’s assault.",h="In Lakeshire, Blackrock Bounty draws fighters as Blackrock forces gather in northern Redridge.",sec={{t="Holding the Sovereign Line",b="Redridge belongs to the Kingdom of Stormwind, yet the Blackrock clan ignores human borders. Orcs pour through mountain passes from the Burning Steppes and fortify camps across northern Redridge. King Varian Wrynn is missing, and Stormwind’s regency withholds royal soldiers. As Lakeshire’s coffers dwindle, Magistrate Solomon and other local leaders offer bounties to protect the town.",sp=0},{t="Targeting the Champions",b="Guard Howe names the Blackrock Champions as the backbone of the invading vanguard. These squad leaders are battle-hardened veterans who coordinate their warbands and drive lesser grunts forward. Lakeshire’s defenders hope a bounty on the Champions will break the clan’s tactical leadership and stall a full-scale push south. The town’s outer defenses may soon collapse.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is Guard Howe offering bounties instead of sending the town guard?",a="Lakeshire’s garrison is stretched thin. Its guards patrol Lake Everstill, protect the bridges, and hold off gnolls and orc raiders. They cannot spare enough fighters to assault the fortified orc camps without leaving the town defenseless.",al={"why bounties","where is town guard","guard howe bounty"},it="why_me"},{q="Where are the Blackrock Champions located?",a="The Blackrock Champions are stationed in the sprawling Blackrock camps in northern Redridge Mountains, just west of the high road that climbs toward the Burning Steppes.",al={"where are champions","champion location","blackrock champion camp"},gp=true},{q="Why are the Blackrock orcs invading Redridge?",a="The Blackrock clan operates from Blackrock Mountain to the north and seeks to conquer and pillage the surrounding hills. With Stormwind’s defense fragmented, the orcs aim to drive out human settlements and claim the mountain passes.",al={"why blackrock in redridge","why orcs attacking lakeshire","blackrock invasion"},it="conflict"},{q="Why doesn't Stormwind send royal soldiers to clear them out?",a="King Varian Wrynn is missing, and the royal court under Regent Bolvar Fordragon and Lady Prestor says the kingdom’s armies cannot be spared. Lakeshire has repeatedly petitioned the capital for help, but its requests are denied. The town is left to hire passing mercenaries.",al={"why no stormwind army","where is stormwind help","magistrate solomon reinforcements"},it="history"},{q="What role do Champions serve within the Blackrock clan?",a="Blackrock Champions are frontline tactical leaders. They direct attacks, enforce brutal discipline, and lead charges into Alliance territory.",al={"what are blackrock champions","champion rank","blackrock leader unit"},it="target"},{q="Who authorized this bounty contract?",a="Magistrate Solomon, Lakeshire’s civic leader, authorized the bounty and tasked Guard Howe with recruiting capable fighters to carry out the culling.",al={"who pays bounty","who wants champions dead","magistrate solomon bounty"},it="in_charge"},{q="Why does Guard Howe want the Blackrock Champions slain?",a="The Blackrock clan has openly invaded sovereign Stormwind territory, threatening Lakeshire and the surrounding Redridge Mountains. Guard Howe acts on the direct orders of Magistrate Solomon to defend the township. By targeting the Champions—the battle-hardened unit leaders directing the encampment—the town aims to break the invaders' command structure before an all-out assault overwhelms Redridge's meager defenses.",al={"why kill blackrock champions","guard howe motive","why does howe want them dead"},it="motive",add="ae8dcd14"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Lakeshire is Stormwind’s eastern shield. If the Blackrock orcs break through the mountain camps, the Alliance’s core farmlands lie open to invasion.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you face a clan that destroyed the original Kingdom of Stormwind in the First War. Stopping the Blackrock return south is a bitter ancestral necessity.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you face Blackrock Champions who are heavily armored and seasoned veteran brawlers. Their martial combat tests your discipline and endurance."},kw={"blackrock","bounty","burning steppes","champion","guard howe","lakeshire","magistrate solomon","redridge","stormwind"},rel={"npc:guard-howe","npc:magistrate-solomon","subzone:lakeshire","zone:redridge","topic:blackrock-clan","topic:stormwind-kingdom","zone:burningsteppes"},m={start="Guard Howe",level="25",faction="Alliance",id=128},src={"Blackrock Bounty"}}
E["quest:129"] = {t="quest",n="A Free Lunch",z="redridge",s="Darcy asks you to carry a prepared meal from Lakeshire to Guard Parker on the southern road. Gnolls and Blackrock orcs threaten the approaches, and the town's guards are stretched thin.",h="Darcy asks you to carry a prepared meal from Lakeshire to Guard Parker on the southern road.",sec={{t="A Meal for the Road",b="Darcy, the cook in Lakeshire, has packed a meal for Guard Parker but cannot carry it beyond town herself. Redridge gnolls and roaming orc warbands make the roads outside the gates too dangerous for a civilian. She asks passing travelers to take the food along the road toward Darkshire, where Parker keeps watch.",sp=0},{t="Guarding the Border",b="Guard Parker watches the road south of Lakeshire, along the route toward Duskwood. Redridge's guards have too few reinforcements from the Stormwind army to face the growing gnoll packs and the Blackrock clan in the mountains. Sentries like Parker keep watch alone in hostile country, and a hot meal from town can lift their spirits.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can Guard Parker be found?",a="Guard Parker patrols the southern dirt road from Lakeshire toward Duskwood and Darkshire.",al={"guard parker location","where is parker","find guard parker"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why doesn't Darcy deliver the lunch herself?",a="Darcy is a civilian and considers the outskirts of Lakeshire too dangerous to travel alone. Gnolls and Blackrock orcs prowl the roads outside town.",al={"why cant darcy go","darcy redridge"},it="why_me"},{q="What threats is Guard Parker dealing with?",a="Parker faces Redridge gnoll packs and Blackrock orc war parties on the southern road.",al={"parker enemies","redridge threats"},it="danger"},{q="What happens after Guard Parker gets his lunch?",a="Darcy's meal earns Parker's gratitude. He then sends you on further errands between the guards and townspeople, beginning with a visit to the local herbalist.",al={"a free lunch next quest","parker follow up"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why are Stormwind guards struggling to keep Redridge safe?",a="Stormwind has sent too few reinforcements to outlying settlements like Lakeshire, leaving the town guards to face the threats with little support.",al={"why is lakeshire undefended","stormwind neglect redridge"},it="threat"},{q="What is Darcy's promised reward?",a="Darcy promises to prepare and serve you a free lunch when you return to town with Parker's meal.",al={"what is the free lunch","darcy reward"},it="for_you"},{q="Why does Darcy want Parker to have this lunch?",a="Darcy has a kind heart and looks after the town's defenders. Guard Parker is stationed far out along the road toward Duskwood, facing constant threat from gnolls and Blackrock orcs without relief. Knowing how grueling and lonely patrol duty can be in these dangerous times, Darcy prepared a fresh meal to sustain him and show that Lakeshire appreciates his service.",al={"darcy motive lunch","why send parker lunch","darcy care about parker"},it="motive",add="a6c03f8c"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Carrying Darcy's food shows the strain on ordinary people and sentries in outlying Alliance settlements left largely to fend for themselves.",["profession:Cooking"]="A warm meal can sustain a lone sentry keeping watch in hostile country."},kw={"blackrock orcs","darcy","darkshire","free lunch","gnolls","guard parker","lakeshire","parker's lunch","redridge mountains"},rel={"quest:130","quest:131","subzone:lakeshire","zone:redridge","subzone:darkshire","topic:stormwind-guard","topic:gnoll","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Darcy",["end"]="Guard Parker",level="15",faction="Alliance",id=129},src={"A Free Lunch"}}
E["quest:130"] = {t="quest",n="Visit the Herbalist",z="redridge",s="Guard Parker sends you to buy flowers for Darcy before you return to the Lakeshire inn. He wants the gift to stay secret.",h="Guard Parker sends you to buy flowers for Darcy before you return to the Lakeshire inn.",sec={{t="A Guard's Secret Request",b="At his post on Lakeshire's southern approach, Guard Parker watches for blackrock orcs and gnolls. You bring him a warm meal from Darcy at the Lakeshire Inn. Grateful for her kindness, Parker asks you to stop at the herbalist shop on the west end of town and buy flowers for her.",sp=0},{t="Town Gossip and Secret Courting",b="Parker asks you to keep the order private when you visit Martie Jainrose, the herbalist. Lakeshire is a small town, and he does not want Martie to know who sent the flowers or who will receive them. At the shop, Martie teases you, guessing you have already found a sweetheart in town. With orc incursions and brigands troubling Redridge, a small gesture of romance brings some welcome relief.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends you to visit the herbalist?",a="Guard Parker, stationed on the southern road into the Redridge Mountains just north of Duskwood, sends you to the herbalist.",al={"who gives this quest","quest giver","guard parker"},it="origin"},{q="Who is the herbalist in Lakeshire?",a="Martie Jainrose is Lakeshire's herbalist and florist. Her shop is at the western end of town.",al={"who is martie jainrose","where is herbalist","lakeshire herbalist"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Guard Parker want flowers?",a="Parker wants to thank Darcy, the Lakeshire Inn waitress who sent him a free lunch, and show his romantic interest with flowers.",al={"why buy flowers","who are flowers for","parker motive"},it="motive"},{q="Why does Parker want the purchase kept secret?",a="Parker feels bashful about courting Darcy and wants to keep the purchase from Martie Jainrose and the other townsfolk.",al={"why secrecy","why hide who flowers are for","dont tell martie"},it="motive"},{q="What happens after talking to Martie Jainrose?",a="Martie prepares a bouquet of daffodils for you to take to Darcy at the Lakeshire Inn.",al={"what comes next","delivering daffodils","after herbalist"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Where does this fit in the quest chain?",a="This visit follows 'A Free Lunch', when you bring lunch to Guard Parker, and comes before 'Delivering Daffodils', when you carry the flowers back to Darcy.",al={"quest chain","prerequisite","free lunch chain"},sp=1,it="history"},{q="Why does Guard Parker ask you to visit the herbalist instead of going himself?",a="Parker is stationed on duty guarding the roads of Redridge and cannot simply abandon his post to run personal errands in town. More importantly, he is deeply embarrassed about his feelings for Darcy. He specifically wants the romantic gesture kept a secret from Martie Jainrose and the rest of Lakeshire, which would be impossible if he were seen buying flowers himself.",al={"why does parker need me","why cant parker get the flowers himself","why ask me visit herbalist"},it="why_me",add="07240ec3"}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="Martie Jainrose is Lakeshire's herbalism and alchemy merchant, at the western edge of town.",["faction:Alliance"]="Gnoll packs and blackrock orcs threaten Redridge, while romance still finds a place among Lakeshire's defenders."},kw={"daffodils","darcy","flowers","guard parker","lakeshire","martie jainrose","redridge","visit the herbalist"},rel={"quest:129","quest:131","npc:martie-jainrose","subzone:lakeshire","zone:redridge"},m={start="Guard Parker",["end"]="Martie Jainrose",level="15",faction="Alliance",id=130},src={"Visit the Herbalist"}}
E["quest:131"] = {t="quest",n="Delivering Daffodils",z="redridge",s="In Lakeshire, you carry flowers from Martie Jainrose to Darcy, and an awkward rivalry comes to light. First, you bring lunch to Guard Parker, who asks you to collect a bouquet for Darcy at the Lakeshire Inn.",h="In Lakeshire, you carry flowers from Martie Jainrose to Darcy, and an awkward rivalry comes to light.",sec={{t="A Fragrant Errand",b="Guard Parker thanks you for bringing his lunch and asks you to fetch flowers from Martie Jainrose for Darcy, the cook who prepared his meal. Martie arranges a bouquet of daffodils, her own favorite flowers, without knowing who will receive them.",sp=0},{t="Town Rivalries",b="At the Lakeshire Inn, Darcy's delight turns to suspicion when she sees the daffodils. She knows they are Martie's favorite and considers Martie a jealous rival. Darcy fears Martie might have poisoned the stems if she had known who would receive them, but she does not blame you. She gives you hot sauteed sunfish for your trouble.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Darcy?",a="Darcy works at the Lakeshire Inn in Redridge Mountains, where she prepares meals for locals and town guards. She sent lunch to Guard Parker, who asked you to bring her flowers in thanks.",al={"darcy","who is darcy in lakeshire","lakeshire cook darcy"},it="people"},{q="Who is Martie Jainrose?",a="Martie Jainrose is Lakeshire's herbalist and a flower enthusiast. Guard Parker sends you to her for a bouquet, and she chooses daffodils, her own favorite flowers.",al={"martie jainrose","lakeshire herbalist","who gave the flowers"},it="people"},{q="Why is Darcy upset about the daffodils?",a="Darcy recognizes the daffodils as Martie's favorite flowers and considers Martie a jealous rival. She fears Martie would have poisoned the stems if she had known the bouquet was meant for Darcy.",al={"why is darcy angry","darcy martie feud","why poisoned flowers"},sp=1,it="conflict"},{q="Did Martie actually poison the bouquet?",a="No. Martie did not know the flowers were for Darcy; Parker only asked you to pick up a bouquet, so Martie chose her own favorites.",al={"are daffodils poisoned","is bouquet poisoned"},sp=1},{q="What quests lead up to this delivery?",a="The chain begins with A Free Lunch, where you carry Darcy's meal to Guard Parker. Parker then sends you to buy a gift from Martie Jainrose in Visit the Herbalist, which leads to Delivering Daffodils.",al={"quest chain","daffodils prerequisites","delivering daffodils chain"},it="history",gp=true},{q="What reward do you get for delivering the flowers?",a="Darcy gives you a hearty bundle of sauteed sunfish, some copper and experience, and standing with the kingdom of Stormwind.",al={"quest reward","daffodils rewards"},it="for_you",gp=true},{q="Why does Martie Jainrose want you to deliver daffodils to Darcy?",a="Martie Jainrose chose daffodils simply because they are her own favorite flower, unaware of whom Parker intended them for. Guard Parker asked you to fetch a bouquet to return Darcy's kindness, and Martie happily assembled her personal favorites for the gesture. What she sees as a lovely arrangement, however, Darcy immediately perceives as an insult from a petty romantic rival.",al={"why daffodils","martie jainrose motive","why send daffodils"},it="motive",add="12ade65f"}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="Darcy rewards you with seasoned sauteed sunfish, a taste of simple Redridge lakeside cooking.",["profession:Herbalism"]="Martie Jainrose draws on her knowledge of plants and her eye for fresh lakeside flowers, showing the quieter side of gathering herbs.",["faction:Alliance"]="Helping the town guard and innkeeper in Lakeshire bolsters civilian morale as the town faces Blackrock and gnoll incursions."},kw={"daffodil bouquet","darcy","delivering daffodils","guard parker","lakeshire","martie jainrose","redridge","sauteed sunfish"},rel={"quest:130","quest:129","npc:martie-jainrose","zone:redridge","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Martie Jainrose",["end"]="Darcy",level="15",faction="Alliance",id=131},src={"Delivering Daffodils"}}
E["quest:143"] = {t="quest",n="Messenger to Westfall",z="redridge",s="Magistrate Solomon sends a plea from Lakeshire to Westfall for help against the Blackrock orcs and gnolls. With Stormwind's forces absent, he hopes Gryan Stoutmantle's People's Militia can lend aid.",h="Magistrate Solomon sends a plea from Lakeshire to Westfall for help against the Blackrock orcs and gnolls.",sec={{t="A Desperate Appeal",b="Blackrock orcs and gnolls besiege Lakeshire, and the Stormwind Army has not arrived in force. Magistrate Solomon knows the town guards and irregulars cannot hold the Redridge Mountains alone. With no royal reserves in sight, he writes a formal plea for help. Word has reached him of a citizen defense group forming west of Elwynn Forest, so he sends his appeal there.",sp=0},{t="Reaching Across Borders",b="Gryan Stoutmantle is a veteran commander rallying volunteer fighters under the People's Militia banner. Solomon sends his dispatch across the kingdom, hoping Westfall's volunteers can reinforce Lakeshire's borders until the Crown's armies mobilize. But Westfall is fighting its own desperate struggle against the Defias Brotherhood.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is Magistrate Solomon asking Westfall for help?",a="Stormwind has not sent the reinforcements Lakeshire needs against the orcs and gnolls. Solomon has heard that an armed citizen force is gathering in Westfall, and hopes Gryan Stoutmantle can spare troops for Redridge.",al={"why westfall","solomons plea","why ask gryan"},it="motive"},{q="Who is Gryan Stoutmantle?",a="Gryan Stoutmantle is a veteran soldier at Sentinel Hill in Westfall. With Crown authority and protection absent, he formed and leads the People's Militia to defend local farmsteads from brigands and the Defias Brotherhood.",al={"who is gryan","stoutmantle role","who leads westfall"},it="target"},{q="Where does this courier journey lead?",a="You carry the message from Lakeshire's town hall west across Redridge and Elwynn Forest to Sentinel Hill in central Westfall.",al={"where do i deliver","where is stoutmantle","redridge to westfall"},it="place"},{q="Why hasn't the Stormwind Army relieved Lakeshire?",a="Magistrate Solomon says something is amiss with the army, since promised troops have not arrived. The king is absent and Highlord Bolvar Fordragon rules as regent, while outlying territories are left to fend for themselves without the expected reserves.",al={"why no stormwind army","where are royal guards","stormwind army missing"},it="conflict"},{q="Can Westfall actually spare any troops for Redridge?",a="No. When you reach Sentinel Hill, Westfall is barely holding together against the Defias Brotherhood. The People's Militia has no troops to spare and struggles to protect its own borders.",al={"does westfall help","will militia come","can gryan help"},sp=1,it="allies"},{q="What comes after delivering the letter?",a="Gryan Stoutmantle receives the message and drafts a reply explaining Westfall's dire situation. He sends you back to Magistrate Solomon with his response.",al={"what next","follow up quest","after messenger to westfall"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Magistrate Solomon send an adventurer instead of his own guards?",a="Lakeshire's local town watch is stretched to its absolute breaking point. Gnolls, murlocs, and Blackrock orcs press in on every border, threatening to overrun the town at any moment. Solomon cannot spare a single guard to make the long trek across Elwynn Forest to Westfall, forcing him to rely on capable travelers like you to carry his desperate appeals for aid.",al={"why send me","why does solomon need an adventurer","why not send a guard to westfall"},it="why_me",add="dcf2b619"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="This dispatch shows how little central defense remains in the Kingdom of Stormwind, leaving border towns to seek mutual aid on their own.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you share the hardships of settlers in Redridge and Westfall, who rely on volunteers and mercenaries while the capital sits idle."},kw={"gryan stoutmantle","lakeshire","magistrate solomon","peoples militia","redridge mountains","sentinel hill","solomons plea","westfall"},rel={"npc:magistrate-solomon","npc:gryan-stoutmantle","quest:12","subzone:lakeshire","zone:redridge","zone:westfall","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:stormwind-army"},m={start="Magistrate Solomon",["end"]="Gryan Stoutmantle",level="14",faction="Alliance",id=143},src={"Messenger to Westfall"}}
E["quest:145"] = {t="quest",n="Messenger to Darkshire",z="redridge",s="In Lakeshire, Magistrate Solomon sends an urgent plea to Darkshire for aid. Blackrock orcs and gnolls threaten Redridge, and Solomon turns to his neighbor for military support. A courier must cross Duskwood's shadowed roads to deliver the letter to Lord Ello Ebonlocke, Darkshire's mayor.",h="In Lakeshire, Magistrate Solomon sends an urgent plea to Darkshire for aid.",sec={{t="A Desperate Call for Aid",b="Redridge faces growing pressure from Blackrock orcs and gnoll packs, and Lakeshire's guards are stretched thin. Stormwind's royal court has ignored Magistrate Solomon's pleas, while Westfall is caught up in its own insurrection. With little help nearby, Solomon writes to Mayor Ello Ebonlocke in Duskwood, hoping Darkshire can lend or hire its Night Watch to strengthen Lakeshire's defenses.",sp=0},{t="The Road into the Gloom",b="Solomon's letter must travel south through Duskwood, a forest under supernatural gloom. He warns you to keep to the roads, since the wilderness between Lakeshire and Darkshire is perilous. The letter is bound for Town Hall, where Lord Ebonlocke can receive it. Whether Duskwood can spare any forces is another matter.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is Lakeshire asking Darkshire for help?",a="Stormwind has withheld formal military aid, leaving Lakeshire to face threats such as the Blackrock orcs alone. Magistrate Solomon is asking nearby allies for help and hopes Darkshire's Night Watch can lend trained fighters.",al={"why ask duskwood","why darkshire","solomon darkshire plea"},it="motive"},{q="Who is Lord Ello Ebonlocke?",a="Lord Ello Ebonlocke is Darkshire's mayor and a prominent civilian leader in Duskwood. He oversees the town from Town Hall and coordinates civic affairs with Commander Althea Ebonlocke, who leads the Night Watch.",al={"ello ebonlocke","who is ebonlocke","mayor of darkshire"},it="identity"},{q="What is the Night Watch?",a="The Night Watch is Darkshire's independent civilian militia. Without Stormwind garrison troops, it patrols the town's perimeter and fights undead, beasts, and shadows in Duskwood.",al={"night watch duskwood","who are night watch"},it="allies"},{q="Why does Solomon warn me to stay on the roads?",a="Duskwood's wilderness holds undead horrors, spiders, and feral beasts. Leaving the paved road puts you within reach of predators and ambushes.",al={"duskwood road warning","stay on roads duskwood"},it="danger"},{q="Where did this questline start?",a="Magistrate Solomon's series of urgent letters began with his plea to Gryan Stoutmantle in Westfall. He is continuing his effort to find help for Lakeshire.",al={"previous quest","messenger quest order"},it="history"},{q="Does Darkshire actually have guards to spare?",a="Duskwood faces its own crisis, with risen dead, rogue worgen, and lurking monstrosities. The Night Watch has barely enough fighters to defend Darkshire, so Solomon's plea is a long shot.",al={"will darkshire help","does ebonlocke send guards"},it="conflict"},{q="Why does Magistrate Solomon send an adventurer instead of his own guards?",a="Lakeshire's local guard is stretched to the breaking point holding off the Blackrock orcs and Redridge gnolls encroaching on the town. Magistrate Solomon cannot spare a single watchman from the perimeter to make the perilous journey south through Duskwood. With Stormwind ignoring his pleas for royal troops, he must rely on reliable travelers like you to carry his urgent appeals to neighboring towns.",al={"why send me darkshire","why doesnt solomon send a guard","why me messenger to darkshire"},it="why_me",add="532260e8"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Solomon's urgent letters show how neglected the outlying Alliance towns have become while Stormwind's royal court remains paralyzed.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you share the plight of southern human settlements, which rely on local militias after the kingdom withdrew its regular army patrols."},kw={"darkshire","duskwood","ebonlocke","lakeshire","messenger","night watch","redridge","solomon"},rel={"npc:magistrate-solomon","npc:lord-ello-ebonlocke","subzone:lakeshire","subzone:darkshire","zone:duskwood","zone:redridge","topic:night-watch","quest:56"},m={start="Magistrate Solomon",["end"]="Lord Ello Ebonlocke",level="18",faction="Alliance",id=145},src={"Messenger to Darkshire"}}
E["quest:150"] = {t="quest",n="Murloc Poachers",z="redridge",s="Along Lake Everstill, Murloc Poachers are stripping Lakeshire's waters of fish. Dockmaster Baren needs you to thin their swelling ranks before the town loses its main food supply.",h="Along Lake Everstill, Murloc Poachers are stripping Lakeshire's waters of fish.",sec={{t="A Threat to the Town's Pantry",b="Dockmaster Baren needs you to protect the fish that feed Lakeshire. Lake Everstill supplies the mountain town and its market with fresh catches. Large tribes of murlocs now crowd the shallows and scour the waters for food. Left unchecked, they could wipe out the local fish and leave Lakeshire without its main food supply.",sp=0},{t="Strange Inland Migration",b="Murlocs usually scavenge along the coast, so their numbers high in the Redridge Mountains are hard to explain. Dockmaster Baren wonders why they have come so far from the open ocean. They may be fleeing predators at sea, losing territorial fights, or drawn by Lake Everstill's plentiful waters. Whatever brought them inland, their presence points to trouble elsewhere in the region.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Dockmaster Baren?",a="Dockmaster Baren oversees the docks and fishing traffic along Lake Everstill's shore at Lakeshire. He handles supplies brought by water and hires you to defend the lake's resources from aquatic threats.",al={"baren","who gives murloc poachers","dockmaster baren"},it="identity"},{q="Why are murlocs in Redridge Mountains?",a="Murlocs usually live along coastal shores and marshes, so their presence at high-altitude Lake Everstill is unusual. Dockmaster Baren suspects the tribes came inland to escape something worse along the coasts.",al={"why are murlocs in lake everstill","murlocs inland redridge","why fishmen in lake"},it="why_here"},{q="What threat do the murlocs pose to Lakeshire?",a="Lakeshire relies on Lake Everstill for fish and commerce. The murloc tribes are overfishing its waters, threatening the town's main food supply and local trade.",al={"why kill murlocs","murloc problem lakeshire","lake everstill fish depleted"},it="threat"},{q="Why does Dockmaster Baren collect murloc fins?",a="Dockmaster Baren collects eight murloc fins as proof that you have culled the tribes along the shore and helped deter their advance.",al={"why murloc fins","fin bounty lakeshire"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Are there other tasks involving Lake Everstill's murlocs?",a="Yes. Dockmaster Baren also offers Selling Fish, which asks you to bring him the lake's famous spotted sunfish, caught by line or taken from the murlocs.",al={"selling fish quest connection","other murloc quests redridge"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="What reward does Dockmaster Baren give for clearing the poachers?",a="After you bring him eight fins, Dockmaster Baren gives you a well-crafted Dwarven Fishing Pole to encourage care for the lake's waters.",al={"murloc poachers reward","dwarven fishing pole quest"},it="for_you",gp=true},{q="Why does Dockmaster Baren want the murlocs hunted?",a="Baren oversees the docks and fishing trade of Lake Everstill. The expanding packs of murlocs along the shores are aggressively poaching the waters, threatening to exhaust the town's primary local food supply before anyone can stop them.",al={"baren motive","why cull murlocs","why kill poachers"},it="motive",add="04b19c02"},{q="What is the Murloc Fin used for?",a="The fins serve as physical proof of the cull. Baren has no special craft or alchemy in mind for them; collecting eight severed fins simply guarantees that you have driven back the poachers thinning the fish stocks in Lake Everstill.",al={"murloc fin use","what is murloc fin for","why murloc fins"},it="item",add="38e35746"},{q="Who are the murloc poachers targeted at Lake Everstill?",a="You are hunting the encroaching murlocs that have gathered around the eastern banks of Lake Everstill. Unusually distant from the ocean shores, these amphibious predators have begun establishing camps and devouring the lake's freshwater fish.",al={"who are the poachers","murloc poachers target","why are lake everstill murlocs here"},it="target",add="4daf19f8"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Lakeshire is already hard pressed by blackrock orcs and gnolls, leaving the Alliance town with little defense to protect its vital food supply in Lake Everstill.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you know Redridge was once a tranquil vacation haven for the kingdom of Stormwind. Hostile murlocs now overrun its pristine mountain waters, a sign of how far order has deteriorated."},kw={"dockmaster baren","dwarven fishing pole","lake everstill","lakeshire","murloc fin","poachers","redridge"},rel={"quest:127","subzone:lake-everstill","subzone:lakeshire","topic:murloc","zone:redridge"},m={level="20",faction="Alliance",id=150,ri={"Murloc Fin"}},src={"Murloc Poachers"}}
E["quest:1618"] = {t="quest",n="Gearing Redridge",z="redridge",s="At Lakeshire, a besieged garrison needs sturdy copper equipment from Ironforge. Tormus Deepforge asks aspiring Alliance smiths to forge the gear and help resident smith Verner Osgood defend the region from hostile orcs and gnolls.",h="At Lakeshire, a besieged garrison needs sturdy copper equipment from Ironforge.",sec={{t="A Plea Across Kingdoms",b="At Ironforge's Great Forge, dwarven smiths know the Alliance's frontline struggles reach beyond Dun Morogh. In the Redridge Mountains, Lakeshire faces repeated attacks from Blackrock orcs marching from Stonewatch Keep and gnolls roaming the northern ridges. Royal reinforcements from Stormwind are slow to arrive, and local supplies remain dangerously low.",sp=0},{t="The Anvils of Lakeshire",b="Lakeshire's resident blacksmith, Verner Osgood, works nearly alone at his outdoor forge, mending shattered armor and replacing broken weapons. Seeing the strain on his human counterpart, Tormus Deepforge asks developing smiths to bring four Runed Copper Belts and four Heavy Copper Mauls to Lakeshire. In return for bolstering the militia's defensive reserves, Verner teaches traveling craftsmen finer trade techniques.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who starts the Gearing Redridge quest?",a="Tormus Deepforge, a dwarven smith at Ironforge's Great Forge, offers this work to Alliance smiths with adequate skill in their trade.",al={"gearing redridge questgiver","who gives gearing redridge","tormus quest"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Lakeshire need weapons and armor from Ironforge?",a="Lakeshire faces constant attacks from Blackrock orcs occupying Stonewatch Keep and aggressive gnolls in the northern ridges. Its solitary smith, Verner Osgood, is overwhelmed mending arms and armor for the militia on his own.",al={"why redridge needs gear","why lakeshire needs weapons","redridge supply shortage"},it="purpose"},{q="Who receives the shipment in Redridge?",a="Verner Osgood, Lakeshire's local blacksmith, receives the shipment near the forge in the lakeside town.",al={"where to turn in gearing redridge","verner osgood location","redridge blacksmith turnin"},it="identity"},{q="What equipment must be forged for the task?",a="You need to make four Runed Copper Belts and four Heavy Copper Mauls. Together, they show skill in protective plating and heavy striking craftsmanship.",al={"gearing redridge items needed","materials for gearing redridge","what to craft for tormus"},it="item",gp=true},{q="What threats are troubling Redridge at this time?",a="Blackrock orcs hold Stonewatch Keep, while violent gnoll packs prowl the northern foothills around Lakeshire.",al={"redridge enemies","who is attacking lakeshire","redridge threats"},it="threat"},{q="What reward does Verner Osgood offer in return?",a="Freed from the frantic burden of outfitting every guardsman from scratch, Verner teaches you finer blacksmithing techniques.",al={"verner osgood training","reward for gearing redridge","what do i get"},it="for_you",gp=true},{q="Why does Tormus Deepforge want this done?",a="Tormus Deepforge recognizes that Ironforge's human allies are hard-pressed and fighting their own desperate battles. With the Blackrock clan mounting relentless raids against Lakeshire, Tormus seeks to strengthen the ties between dwarves and humans by providing crucial smithing aid to an ally stretched thin.",al={"why help redridge","tormus deepforge motive","why send supplies to redridge"},it="motive",add="ba6aca96"},{q="What is the Runed Copper Belt for?",a="These enchanted belts provide vital armor reinforcement for the Lakeshire defenders. With local smiths overwhelmed repairing broken gear, sturdy crafted belts help protect the town guards and militia facing constant skirmishes with Blackrock orcs and gnolls.",al={"runed copper belt use","why runed copper belts","purpose of runed copper belt"},it="item",add="e26bdf46"},{q="What is the Heavy Copper Maul for?",a="The heavy copper mauls furnish the frontline defenders of Lakeshire with durable, punishing weaponry. Redridge's defenders clash constantly against armored Blackrock orcs and tough Redridge gnolls, making crushing blunt weapons indispensable to their war effort.",al={"heavy copper maul purpose","why heavy copper mauls","heavy copper maul redridge"},it="item",add="61555f3e"},{q="Why does Tormus Deepforge need you rather than delivering them himself?",a="Tormus is a master blacksmith training apprentices and managing the Great Forge of Ironforge, an essential post he cannot abandon for a journey to the human lands. Entrusting the shipment to an aspiring smith both aids their allies and allows you to learn trade techniques from Verner Osgood.",al={"why send me to redridge","why can't tormus deliver","why me gearing redridge"},it="why_me",add="330fd0fb"}},ang={["profession:Blacksmithing"]="As a blacksmith, you prove you can make durable weapons and protective armor in quantity for an active warfront.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you carry aid from Ironforge to the beleaguered human townships of the south, where Stormwind's divided leadership has been slow to act.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you draw on a craft that forms the backbone of the Alliance war effort, and Tormus directs Ironforge's finest smiths to aid their beleaguered allies.",["race:Human"]="As a human of the southern kingdoms, you receive metalwork forged in Khaz Modan, relief against the aggressive Blackrock remnants."},kw={"blackrock orcs","blacksmithing","gnolls","heavy copper maul","lakeshire","redridge","runed copper belt","stonewatch","tormus deepforge","verner osgood"},rel={"npc:tormus-deepforge","npc:verner-osgood","zone:redridge","zone:ironforge","subzone:stonewatch-keep","topic:gnoll"},m={start="Tormus Deepforge",["end"]="Verner Osgood",faction="Alliance",id=1618,ri={"Heavy Copper Maul","Runed Copper Belt"}},src={"Gearing Redridge"}}
E["quest:169"] = {t="quest",n="Wanted: Gath'Ilzogg",z="redridge",s="In Redridge, Magistrate Solomon offers a generous bounty on the warlord behind Blackrock's invasion of Stonewatch. The reward goes to anyone who storms the conquered keep and brings back the commander's severed head.",h="In Redridge, Magistrate Solomon offers a generous bounty on the warlord behind Blackrock's invasion of...",sec={{t="The Warlord of Stonewatch",b="Gath'Ilzogg commands Blackrock raids across the Redridge Mountains. His orcs stormed Stonewatch Keep and made the former human bastion a fortified staging ground for attacks on nearby settlements. From its highest ramparts, he plans further incursions into Lakeshire, threatening to cut Redridge off from the rest of the kingdom.",sp=0},{t="A Town Pushed to the Brink",b="Stormwind's royal army has failed to send reinforcements to the border regions, so Magistrate Solomon takes matters into his own hands. Lakeshire lacks the soldiers to retake Stonewatch Keep by force. Solomon posts a public bounty on Gath'Ilzogg, hoping to break Blackrock's leadership and begin reclaiming the keep for the crown.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Gath'Ilzogg?",a="Gath'Ilzogg is an orc warlord leading the Blackrock forces occupying Stonewatch. He directed the keep's conquest and is responsible for frequent deadly raids against Lakeshire's human settlers.",al={"gath'ilzogg lore","who is gathilzogg","blackrock leader redridge"},it="target"},{q="Where can Gath'Ilzogg be found?",a="Gath'Ilzogg is entrenched at the top of Stonewatch Keep, in the eastern crags of the Redridge Mountains. Blackrock champions and bodyguards guard him.",al={"gath'ilzogg location","where is gathilzogg","stonewatch boss location"},gp=true},{q="Why is Magistrate Solomon offering a bounty instead of sending soldiers?",a="Lakeshire's town guard is stretched thin, and Stormwind's crown has sent no troops to relieve the region. Magistrate Solomon relies on mercenaries and independent adventurers to face major threats.",al={"why a bounty","where are stormwind soldiers","lakeshire guard help"},it="why_me"},{q="What happens after Gath'Ilzogg is killed?",a="Magistrate Solomon sees Gath'Ilzogg's death as the first step toward clearing out the orcs and, eventually, reclaiming Stonewatch Keep for the Kingdom of Stormwind. Blackrock forces remain heavy in the region.",al={"is stonewatch retaken","after gath'ilzogg"},it="next_step"},{q="Why did the Blackrock orcs invade Stonewatch Keep?",a="The Blackrock clan uses Stonewatch Keep as a fortified forward base high in the Redridge Mountains. From there, they control the passes and launch raids against human settlements.",al={"why are blackrock in redridge","why stonewatch taken"}},{q="Who claims the bounty once Gath'Ilzogg is dead?",a="Bring Gath'Ilzogg's head to Magistrate Solomon at Lakeshire's town hall as proof of his defeat.",al={"who to turn in gathilzogg","gathilzogg quest turn in"},gp=true},{q="Why does Lakeshire want Gath'Ilzogg killed?",a="Gath'Ilzogg serves as the general directing the Blackrock orc invasion of Redridge. Under his command, the orcs slaughtered human defenders, captured Stonewatch Keep, and launched violent raids directly against the township of Lakeshire. Town leadership knows that so long as he coordinates their forces, the Blackrock clan will continue to plot atrocities against innocent citizens. Putting an end to him is critical to breaking the siege and eventually reclaiming the keep.",al={"why kill gath'ilzogg","why gath'ilzogg bounty","why does solomon want gath'ilzogg dead"},it="motive",add="1d021e94"},{q="What is the Head of Gath'Ilzogg for?",a="The head provides indisputable proof that the Blackrock warlord has actually fallen. Magistrate Solomon needs concrete evidence of Gath'Ilzogg's demise before he can dispense the town's bounty and reassure the panicked citizens of Lakeshire that the architect behind the attacks has been dealt with.",al={"head of gath'ilzogg purpose","why collect gath'ilzogg head","what do i do with gath'ilzogg head"},it="item",add="69773e29"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Striking down Gath'Ilzogg removes one of the most immediate military threats to the kingdom's eastern borders and buys vital breathing room for Lakeshire's citizens.",["race:Human"]="For Stormwind's people, Stonewatch Keep was hard won. Gath'Ilzogg's slaughter of innocents when it fell makes this bounty a matter of bitter vengeance.",["class:Warrior"]="At Stonewatch Keep's summit, you face the hardened veteran warriors and brute strength of the Dark Horde's frontline command."},kw={"blackrock","bounty","gath'ilzogg","lakeshire","magistrate solomon","redridge","stonewatch","wanted poster"},rel={"subzone:stonewatch-keep","subzone:stonewatch","npc:magistrate-solomon","topic:blackrock-clan","subzone:lakeshire","zone:redridge","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Wanted: Gath'Ilzogg",["end"]="Magistrate Solomon",level="26",faction="Alliance",id=169,ri={"Head of Gath'Ilzogg"}},src={"Wanted: Gath'Ilzogg (quest)"}}
E["quest:1699"] = {t="quest",n="The Rethban Gauntlet",z="redridge",s="In Lakeshire, Yorus Barleybrew sends challengers on a perilous run north and back. They drink his family's fiery Barleybrew Scalder, reach Rethban Caverns, and return within an hour.",h="In Lakeshire, Yorus Barleybrew sends challengers on a perilous run north and back.",sec={{t="A Dwarven Dare",b="In Lakeshire, grim talk of gnoll raids and missing town guards fills the inn. The dwarf Yorus Barleybrew offers a different kind of diversion: a test of speed, courage, and endurance. Before setting out on foot for the northern foothills, challengers drink a draught of his family's Barleybrew Scalder.",sp=0},{t="Running the Wild Hills",b="Redridge gnolls roam the hills between Lakeshire and Rethban Caverns. Runners must fight or slip past their packs, reach the first fork inside the dark tunnels, then hurry back to Yorus within an hour. The fiery drink makes the run harder, leaving challengers staggering as they make their way through the hills.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who issues the Rethban Gauntlet?",a="Yorus Barleybrew, a dwarven brewer staying in Lakeshire, challenges travelers to run the gauntlet and test their fortitude and his brew.",al={"who gives rethban gauntlet","yorus barleybrew quest","who starts the gauntlet"},it="identity"},{q="What makes this challenge particularly difficult?",a="Runners face gnoll packs in the Redridge foothills and have only an hour. First they drink Barleybrew Scalder, which leaves them severely intoxicated and struggling to keep their balance.",al={"why is rethban gauntlet hard","barleybrew scalder effect"},gp=true},{q="Where are the Rethban Caverns located?",a="Rethban Caverns lie in the northern foothills of Redridge Mountains, northwest of Lakeshire. The path runs north past local homesteads toward crags inhabited by gnoll packs.",al={"rethban caverns location","where is rethban","how to get to rethban caverns"},it="place",gp=true},{q="How far into the caves must a runner go?",a="Challengers need only reach the first fork inside the caverns, then turn back and race to Lakeshire.",al={"rethban caverns objective","how far inside rethban"},gp=true},{q="Who inhabits the hills and caverns along the route?",a="Hostile Redridge gnolls overrun the area around the route and the caverns. Runners need stealth or swift combat to survive the trek.",al={"what enemies in rethban","what is in rethban caverns"},it="danger"},{q="Where does this challenge lead next?",a="Surviving the gauntlet proves your endurance to Yorus Barleybrew and opens the way to further tasks in the region, such as seeking out the shieldsmith Furen Longbeard in Stormwind.",al={"rethban gauntlet follow up","what quest comes after rethban gauntlet"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Yorus Barleybrew want this done?",a="Yorus Barleybrew is not looking to solve a crisis or save Lakeshire with this trial. Instead, he devises the Rethban Gauntlet as a boisterous test of nerve, endurance, and alcohol tolerance. By sending daring adventurers deep into gnoll territory while thoroughly intoxicated on his family's fiery Barleybrew Scalder, Yorus seeks pure entertainment and the thrill of watching someone brave enough to conquer both Redridge's savage gnolls and his brew's staggering kick.",al={"why run the gauntlet","yorus barleybrew motive","why does yorus challenge you"},it="motive",add="26a182c4"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you may recognize Yorus's boisterous idea of fun: mixing potent family liquor with a dangerous mountain sprint.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you can help Lakeshire face the gnoll threat by braving the gauntlet and thinning the enemy patrols near the northern caves."},kw={"barleybrew scalder","gnolls","lakeshire","redridge","rethban caverns","rethban gauntlet","timed run","yorus barleybrew"},rel={"quest:1698","subzone:rethban-caverns","subzone:lakeshire","topic:gnoll","quest:1702","npc:martie-jainrose","zone:redridge"},m={start="Yorus Barleybrew",level="22",faction="Alliance",id=1699},src={"The Rethban Gauntlet"}}
E["quest:178"] = {t="quest",n="Theocritus' Retrieval",z="redridge",s="In Redridge, an adventurer finds a gnoll pendant and hears a voice through it. The voice belongs to Theocritus, High Mage of Tower of Azora, who has intercepted the gnolls' mystical network and urgently asks for the pendant to study.",h="In Redridge, an adventurer finds a gnoll pendant and hears a voice through it.",sec={{t="A Voice in the Stone",b="Across the Redridge Mountains, travelers fighting the savage Shadowhide gnolls sometimes find a Shadowhide Pendant. Touching the enchanted trinket brings a calm, distant voice instead of barking or curses. The speaker is Theocritus, a human mage at Tower of Azora, across the border in Elwynn Forest. His message comes from long research into breaking the dark sorceries that direct the gnoll packs.",sp=0},{t="Subverting Morganth's Network",b="The Shadowhide gnolls obey Morganth, a rogue dark caster hidden in the mountains, as well as their own instincts. Morganth makes enchanted pendants to send commands to his gnoll followers. Theocritus spent months unraveling the frequency of Morganth's sending spells. When you bring the faded pendant to Tower of Azora, Theocritus confirms his scrying reached it. Now he can study how to reverse the magic and disable the gnolls.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Theocritus?",a="Theocritus is a high mage of the Alliance at Tower of Azora in eastern Elwynn Forest. He watches for trouble in the region and studies ways to counter dark magic spreading from Redridge.",al={"theocritus lore","who is talking through the pendant","tower of azora mage"},it="identity"},{q="Why were the Shadowhide gnolls carrying magical pendants?",a="Morganth, a renegade wizard, made the pendants as magical conduits. He uses them to send mental commands and direct the Shadowhide clan from afar.",al={"why do gnolls have pendants","shadowhide pendant purpose","gnoll magic item"},it="origin"},{q="Why was the voice delayed when Theocritus sent it?",a="Theocritus sent his message weeks before you found the stone, and first believed the spell had faded without reaching it. Breaking through Morganth's dark wards and linking across such a vast distance delayed the message.",al={"delayed message","why did theocritus take weeks","faded pendant delay"}},{q="What does Theocritus hope to achieve with the retrieved pendant?",a="Theocritus hopes to read the magical frequency linking the pendant to Morganth and reverse its flow. He aims to send an offensive spell through the network that could instantly immobilize every gnoll wearing a pendant.",al={"theocritus plan","what will theocritus do","why study the pendant"},it="motive"},{q="Where does this quest chain lead next?",a="Bringing the pendant to Theocritus completes this errand. His separate struggle against Morganth continues in 'A Watchful Eye', which sends you to spy on Morganth's stronghold at the Tower of Ilgalar.",al={"next quest after theocritus retrieval","morganth chain","what happens next"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Theocritus need an adventurer to deliver the pendant?",a="Theocritus cast his message blindly across the magical frequencies Morganth uses to commune with the gnolls, having no idea where or when a pendant might receive it. Bound to his sanctum at the Tower of Azora in Elwynn Forest, he could not comb the hostile wilds of Redridge Mountains himself. He relies on whatever capable traveler discovers the artifact to carry it back into civilized lands safely.",al={"why send an adventurer","why does theocritus need me","why can't theocritus get the pendant"},it="why_me",add="24fcac1f"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you can see ingenious use of abjuration and divination in Theocritus's work: he breaks into another sorcerer's network to send counterspells across vast distances.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can see Tower of Azora in Elwynn working with Lakeshire's beleaguered defenders. Local mages step in where Stormwind's royal army has left garrisons understaffed."},kw={"elwynn","gnolls","morganth","pendant","redridge","shadowhide","theocritus","tower of azora"},rel={"quest:94","quest:248","quest:249","npc:theocritus","topic:gnoll","zone:redridge","zone:elwynn"},m={start="Glowing Shadowhide Pendant",["end"]="Theocritus",level="23",faction="Alliance",id=178},src={"Theocritus' Retrieval"}}
E["quest:180"] = {t="quest",n="Wanted: Lieutenant Fangore",z="redridge",s="A bounty in Lakeshire calls for Lieutenant Fangore's death. Magistrate Solomon seeks hunters to stop the Shadowhide gnolls pressing into the Redridge Mountains. Fangore serves the renegade sorcerer Morganth, and his death would strike at Morganth's forces.",h="A bounty in Lakeshire calls for Lieutenant Fangore's death.",sec={{t="A Town Under Siege",b="Lakeshire faces growing danger. Stormwind's army is stretched thin, and King Varian Wrynn is mysteriously absent. Highlord Bolvar Fordragon has left frontier settlements like Redridge to defend themselves. The Shadowhide clan raids trade routes, burns farmsteads, and presses against the town's perimeter. Magistrate Solomon posts bounties to draw mercenary blades where royal soldiers will not march.",sp=0},{t="Morganth's Lieutenant",b="Lieutenant Fangore leads the Shadowhide gnolls as Morganth's enforcer. Morganth is a rogue dark wizard hiding in the Redridge hills. Under Fangore, the gnolls coordinate their attacks instead of fighting as scattered scavengers. Their strikes threaten to sever Lakeshire from Elwynn Forest. Fangore's severed paw would give Magistrate Solomon proof that Morganth's brute vanguard has been broken.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Lieutenant Fangore?",a="Lieutenant Fangore leads the Shadowhide gnolls in Redridge, coordinating their raids and enforcing the will of Morganth, a dark sorcerer who threatens Lakeshire.",al={"lieutenant fangore","who is fangore","fangore lore"},it="target"},{q="Who posted the bounty for Lieutenant Fangore?",a="Magistrate Solomon, Lakeshire's town leader, posted the bounty to defend Redridge's perimeter from hostile gnolls and dark spellcasters.",al={"who posted the bounty","who wants fangore dead","magistrate solomon fangore"},it="motive"},{q="Why doesn't Stormwind send soldiers to handle the gnolls?",a="Stormwind is paralyzed by King Varian Wrynn's sudden disappearance and domestic unrest. Highlord Bolvar Fordragon and the House of Nobles have refused to send regular army detachments to outlying towns like Lakeshire, leaving Magistrate Solomon to hire mercenary adventurers.",al={"why no stormwind guard","where are stormwind soldiers","why isn't the army helping"},it="why_me"},{q="What proof is required to claim the bounty?",a="Magistrate Solomon requires Lieutenant Fangore's severed paw as proof that the Shadowhide warlord has been slain.",al={"fangore proof","fangores paw","what item for turn in"},it="item"},{q="Who is Morganth and why does Fangore follow him?",a="Morganth is a rogue human spellcaster who practices dark magic from a tower in the Redridge Mountains. He has bent the Shadowhide gnolls to his will and uses Lieutenant Fangore as an enforcer to terrorize the countryside.",al={"who is morganth","why do gnolls follow morganth","fangore morganth"},it="allies"},{q="What are the Shadowhide gnolls?",a="The Shadowhide are a ferocious gnoll clan in the crags and forests of the Redridge Mountains. Their aggression and brutal ambushes have plagued Lakeshire's settlers for years.",al={"shadowhide clan","redridge gnolls","shadowhide lore"},it="people"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, Lakeshire is a key stronghold in Redridge. Removing Fangore would keep the settlement from being cut off.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you feel Stormwind's neglect in Redridge firsthand. Facing the gnoll chieftains is a matter of survival for your home."},kw={"fangore","gnoll","lakeshire","lieutenant fangore","magistrate solomon","morganth","redridge","shadowhide"},rel={"npc:magistrate-solomon","quest:249","subzone:lakeshire","zone:redridge","topic:gnoll","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Wanted: Lieutenant Fangore",["end"]="Magistrate Solomon",level="26",faction="Alliance",id=180,ri={"Fangore's Paw"}},src={"Wanted: Lieutenant Fangore (quest)"}}
E["quest:19"] = {t="quest",n="Tharil'zun",z="redridge",s="Near Stonewatch Keep, Marshal Marris puts a bounty on Tharil'zun, whose outrunners harass the roads. His death is a critical step in breaking the Blackrock clan's hold over northern Redridge, and his severed head brought to Lakeshire marks a hard-fought victory for its watch.",h="Near Stonewatch Keep, Marshal Marris puts a bounty on Tharil'zun, whose outrunners harass the roads.",sec={{t="The Road to Stonewatch",b="The pass between Lakeshire and Stonewatch Keep has become a gauntlet of sudden ambushes. Blackrock outrunners and renegades prowl the rocky ridges, cutting off scouts and threatening reinforcements trying to reach the fortress. Marshal Marris names Tharil'zun as the commander behind these coordinated strikes. He says Tharil'zun must be eliminated, or Lakeshire may be hemmed in entirely.",sp=0},{t="Decapitating the Outrunners",b="Tharil'zun is a dangerous battlefield leader: vicious, crafty, and able to unite scattered orc raiders into an effective raiding force. To take his head in Stonewatch's shadow, you must cut through entrenched Blackrock outposts. His death breaks the outrunner patrols' cohesion and clears a path for the Alliance to face the garrison inside the keep.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Tharil'zun?",a="Tharil'zun is a formidable Blackrock orc commander who leads the outrunners and renegades ambushing trails between Lakeshire and Stonewatch Keep.",al={"who is tharilzun","tharil'zun lore","tharilzun boss"},it="target"},{q="Where can Tharil'zun be found?",a="Tharil'zun is near Stonewatch Keep in northeastern Redridge, commanding outrunners who patrol the surrounding passes and outposts.",al={"where is tharil'zun","tharilzun location","find tharil'zun"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Marshal Marris want his head?",a="Marris sees Tharil'zun as the cunning tactician directing the ambushes that harass Redridge. He demands Tharil'zun's head to sever the outrunner leadership and prove the threat has been eliminated.",al={"why kill tharilzun","tharilzun bounty reason"},it="motive"},{q="What happens after Tharil'zun is defeated?",a="Defeating Tharil'zun cripples the outrunners' coordination, allowing Lakeshire's defenders and adventurers to push deeper into Stonewatch Keep and confront the main Blackrock garrison.",al={"quest after tharilzun","what follows tharil'zun"},it="next_step"},{q="Why are Blackrock orcs in Redridge Mountains?",a="Blackrock clan remnants moved south from the Burning Steppes into Redridge. They fortified old human outposts such as Stonewatch Keep to threaten the Eastern Kingdoms while Stormwind's military is stretched thin.",al={"why are blackrock orcs in redridge","stonewatch orcs background"},it="origin"},{q="What prerequisite must be completed before hunting Tharil'zun?",a="Before Marshal Marris sends you after Tharil'zun, he requires you to prove your mettle by thinning the invading forces in 'Blackrock Menace'.",al={"tharilzun prereq","how to unlock tharilzun quest"},gp=true},{q="Why does Marshal Marris need Tharil'zun's head?",a="Marshal Marris demands Tharil'zun's head as definitive proof of the warlord's death. Tharil'zun is a crafty and vicious leader directing ambushes against Lakeshire's defenders, and Marris cannot afford to rely on rumors or mistaken reports when the security of the entire region hangs by a thread.",al={"what is tharilzuns head for","tharilzun head purpose","why take tharilzuns head"},it="item",add="3b83e264"},{q="Why does Marshal Marris send you instead of the town guard?",a="Lakeshire's local garrison is stretched to its absolute breaking point. With Stormwind withholding reinforcements and orc ambushes pressing close to the town, Marshal Marris cannot spare men to breach deep into Stonewatch territory. He must rely on seasoned, independent adventurers to take down high-value enemy commanders.",al={"why send an adventurer","why not use redridge guards","why does marris need me"},it="why_me",add="66abe4be"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Lakeshire stands largely isolated, without direct reinforcements from Stormwind. The bounty on Tharil'zun is a vital local measure to keep the town from being besieged.",["race:Human"]="As a human, the Blackrock presence in Redridge recalls the First and Second Wars. Slaying Tharil'zun reclaims ground stolen from the kingdom.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you face Tharil'zun, one of the Old Horde's dark remnants under the Blackrock banner, serving masters who reject Thrall's new order across the sea."},kw={"blackrock","lakeshire","marshal marris","outrunners","redridge","stonewatch","stonewatch keep","tharil'zun","tharilzun"},rel={"npc:marshal-marris","quest:20","subzone:stonewatch-keep","subzone:stonewatch","zone:redridge"},m={start="Marshal Marris",level="25",faction="Alliance",id=19,ri={"Tharil'zun's Head"}},src={"Tharil'zun (quest)"}}
E["quest:20"] = {t="quest",n="Blackrock Menace",z="redridge",s="Redridge's Blackrock orcs press in from the north and southeast, leaving Lakeshire under siege. Marshal Marris calls on adventurers to thin their ranks and bring back their battleworn axes.",h="Redridge's Blackrock orcs press in from the north and southeast, leaving Lakeshire under siege.",sec={{t="A Town Under Siege",b="Lakeshire faces threats from several sides, but the Blackrock orcs are the gravest danger. These seasoned raiders have crossed south from the fiery Burning Steppes into Redridge. They have taken strongholds and roam the craggy passes. Their presence keeps townspeople penned inside Lakeshire, cutting off trade, foraging, and travel along the northern roads.",sp=0},{t="Striking the Vanguard",b="Marshal Marris commands Lakeshire's beleaguered guard, but he cannot spare soldiers to assault the orcs' positions. He calls on you to strike their forward scouts and foot soldiers instead. Their crude, battleworn axes will prove they are dead. Marris hopes to thin the invaders around Stonewatch to the north and in the rugged pockets of southeastern Redridge.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where did these Blackrock orcs come from?",a="They marched south through the jagged mountain passes from the Burning Steppes, where their ancestral stronghold lies around Blackrock Mountain.",al={"where are the orcs from","blackrock invasion redridge","why are orcs in redridge"},it="origin"},{q="Who issues this task?",a="Marshal Marris, Lakeshire's senior military officer, issues the order. He is responsible for defending the town and keeping order as it becomes increasingly surrounded.",al={"who gives blackrock menace","blackrock menace quest giver","marshal marris quest"},it="in_charge"},{q="Where can the Blackrock invaders be found?",a="The Blackrock invaders occupy the northern highlands around Stonewatch Keep and have footholds in the southeastern pocket of the Redridge Mountains.",al={"where are blackrock orcs","battleworn axe locations","redridge orc camps"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Marshal Marris ask for battleworn axes?",a="The battleworn axes give Marshal Marris physical proof that you fought and killed the Blackrock marauders threatening the valley.",al={"why axes","proof of death","battleworn axe purpose"},it="item"},{q="What happens after these scouts are defeated?",a="After the vanguard is thinned, Marshal Marris orders a strike against Tharil'zun, the local Blackrock leader entrenched in the mountains.",al={"what comes after blackrock menace","next quest after blackrock menace","who leads the orcs"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Are the orcs affiliated with Thrall's Horde?",a="No. The Blackrock clan here is made up of Old Horde remnants. They remain violently hostile to the Alliance and operate independently of Thrall's new Horde in Kalimdor.",al={"are these horde orcs","is blackrock clan part of thrall horde","friendly orcs in redridge"},it="allies"},{q="Why does Marshal Marris want the Blackrock orcs killed?",a="The Blackrock clan has pushed down from the Burning Steppes, seizing Stonewatch Keep and marauding the lands north of Lakeshire. Their constant raids have effectively trapped the town's citizens within their borders, penned like cattle. Marshal Marris wants to break this suffocating siege, secure the region's northern borders, and eliminate scouting warbands before Lakeshire is completely overrun.",al={"marris motive","why kill blackrock orcs","why blackrock menace"},it="motive",add="ded9bd4b"},{q="Who are the Blackrock invaders threatening Lakeshire?",a="You are sent against the Blackrock orcs, remnants of the Old Horde who have descended from the Burning Steppes. Having claimed Stonewatch Keep to the north, they actively maraud the wilderness and have begun establishing outposts in the southeastern pockets of Redridge, seeking to strangle Lakeshire and expand their territorial grip across the mountains.",al={"who are the blackrock orcs","who is the target","stonewatch orcs"},it="target",add="29f2a399"},{q="Why does Marshal Marris need adventurers instead of the Lakeshire guard?",a="Lakeshire's local garrison is stretched to its breaking point. With Stormwind's army absent and failing to send reinforcements, Marris and his few remaining guards cannot afford to sally out into the wilderness without leaving the town completely defenseless. To push back the advancing invaders, he relies on capable independent mercenaries and adventurers.",al={"why doesnt the guard fight","why me marris","why need adventurers"},it="why_me",add="e27bf976"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, defending Lakeshire helps hold Stormwind's southern border against old-world adversaries.",["race:Human"]="As a human, facing the Blackrock clan in Redridge brings bitter grief: they destroyed the original Kingdom of Stormwind in the First War.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, meeting seasoned Blackrock marauders shield to shield tests your martial discipline and strength on the front line."},kw={"axes","blackrock","burning steppes","lakeshire","marris","orcs","redridge","stonewatch","tharil'zun"},rel={"npc:marshal-marris","quest:19","subzone:lakeshire","subzone:stonewatch","subzone:stonewatch-keep","zone:redridge","zone:burningsteppes"},m={start="Marshal Marris",level="21",faction="Alliance",id=20,ri={"Battleworn Axe"}},src={"Blackrock Menace"}}
E["quest:219"] = {t="quest",n="Missing In Action",z="redridge",s="In the Redridge Mountains, Corporal Keeshan is missing after his regiment was overrun. Blackrock orcs knocked him unconscious and dragged him into a cave fortress. Now he needs an escort back to Lakeshire, where the garrison can learn what became of the missing men.",h="In the Redridge Mountains, Corporal Keeshan is missing after his regiment was overrun.",sec={{t="A Regiment Overrun",b="Blackrock orcs descend from the northern peaks, making the Redridge Mountains more perilous. Town guard patrols often meet ambushes, and Corporal Keeshan's unit suffered the worst of them. The regiment was outnumbered and overwhelmed, and most of its soldiers fell in the attack. Keeshan survived when a crushing blow knocked him unconscious before the orcs could execute him. They dragged him to their cave as a prisoner.",sp=0},{t="Escape from the Caves",b="Battered and concussed, Keeshan is held deep in enemy territory and cannot make the trek down the mountain alone. You escort him toward Lakeshire, past the orc warbands occupying the ridgelines. Marshal Marris has been trying to learn what happened to the missing regiment while preparing Lakeshire for further attacks. Keeshan's safe return brings him sorely needed relief.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Corporal Keeshan?",a="Corporal Keeshan is an Alliance infantryman stationed in the Redridge Mountains. Blackrock orcs overwhelmed his regiment during a patrol in the rocky hills, then dragged him away. He is the only known survivor.",al={"corporal keeshan","who is keeshan","keeshan lore"},it="identity"},{q="Where was Corporal Keeshan captured?",a="Corporal Keeshan is held deep inside an orc-infested cave in Redridge's northern hills, surrounded by hostile Blackrock warriors.",al={"where is keeshan","keeshan location","keeshan cave"},it="place"},{q="What happened to the rest of Keeshan's unit?",a="Blackrock orcs ambushed and overpowered Keeshan's regiment. Nearly all the men died in the first skirmish.",al={"keeshan squad","what happened to the regiment","keeshan men"},it="history"},{q="Who sends players to rescue Keeshan?",a="Corporal Keeshan sends you to free him from his prison cave, where Alliance adventurers discover him.",al={"who starts missing in action","quest giver","where to pick up missing in action"},it="origin"},{q="Where does Keeshan go after being freed?",a="After you free him, Keeshan needs an escort down the mountainside to Lakeshire. He reports to Marshal Marris near the town's bridge.",al={"turn in missing in action","where does keeshan run","keeshan destination"},it="next_step"},{q="Why are the Blackrock orcs in Redridge?",a="The Blackrock clan pushes south from its strongholds in the Burning Steppes into Redridge. The clan threatens Lakeshire, which is poorly reinforced, and ambushes Kingdom patrols.",al={"blackrock orcs redridge","why orcs in lakeshire","blackrock invasion"},it="conflict"},{q="Why does Corporal Keeshan need your help to escape?",a="Corporal Keeshan is trapped deep inside hostile territory after his entire regiment was ambushed and slaughtered by the Blackrock clan. Having suffered a severe blow to the head during the skirmish, he is badly wounded, disoriented, and in need of an escort. Without an escort to guide him through the surrounding orcs, he faces certain execution or starvation in the cave.",al={"why help keeshan","keeshan motive","why does keeshan need rescue"},it="motive",add="64cb6fe2"},{q="Why can't Keeshan escape on his own or wait for the Lakeshire guard?",a="Keeshan is severely injured and needs help fighting his way past the Blackrock raiders. Meanwhile, Lakeshire's defenders are stretched to their limits just trying to hold the town against gnolls and orcs, leaving no forces to spare for a deep search-and-rescue mission. When you stumble upon his cell, you are literally the only hope he has of making it back alive.",al={"why cant keeshan escape alone","why does keeshan need me","why no town guards"},it="why_me",add="1d637b84"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance soldier, every rescued fighter matters to Lakeshire's strained garrison as it defends the Kingdom against the Blackrock clan.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you hold the frontline against waves of Blackrock attackers while protecting the concussed Keeshan during his escape from their armed camp."},kw={"blackrock orcs","corporal keeshan","escort","keeshan","lakeshire","marshal marris","missing in action","redridge"},rel={"npc:marshal-marris","zone:redridge","topic:alliance"},m={start="Corporal Keeshan",["end"]="Marshal Marris",level="25",faction="Alliance",id=219},src={"Missing In Action"}}
E["quest:2282"] = {t="quest",n="Alther's Mill",z="redridge",s="At Alther's Mill, Lucius tests Alliance rogues with a locked chest and thieves' tools. The mill lies northeast along the road from Lakeshire, where Blackrock orcs now draw near.",h="At Alther's Mill, Lucius tests Alliance rogues with a locked chest and thieves' tools.",sec={{t="A Test of Grace and Finesse",b="Lucius sends you northeast along the road from Lakeshire to Alther's Mill, with your first set of thieves' tools. There, you face a locked chest and a test of skill. Open Lucius's personal lockbox and bring back the token inside to earn your Certificate of Thievery.",sp=0},{t="Shadows Around the Saws",b="Alther's Mill once served as a lumber outpost, but Blackrock orcs now encroach on Redridge and have drawn near. Lucius treats their presence as an added trial. SI:7 expects its agents to pick locks undetected while moving through enemy-held territory.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the mission to Alther's Mill?",a="Lucius tests your lockpicking in the field. He gives you thieves' tools and asks you to retrieve a token from a locked chest as proof of your skill.",al={"why go to althers mill","quest purpose","what does this quest do"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Lucius?",a="Lucius trains rogues in Lakeshire, in the Redridge Mountains. He schools recruits sent by contacts throughout the Alliance, testing their stealth and manual skill.",al={"who is lucius","lucius lakeshire","who gives this quest"},it="identity"},{q="Where is Alther's Mill located?",a="Alther's Mill lies just off the road northeast and east of Lakeshire, against the foothills before the higher mountain passes.",al={"where is the mill","althers mill location","how do i find althers mill"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why are there orcs around Alther's Mill?",a="Blackrock clan orcs have come down from Stonewatch and the burning ridges above. They raid human settlements and establish forward footholds throughout Redridge, including around the abandoned mill.",al={"why are orcs here","blackrock orcs redridge","who controls althers mill"},it="threat"},{q="What reward does Lucius grant upon completing the task?",a="Lucius awards you the Certificate of Thievery, recognizing your grasp of tumblers and lockpicks and your readiness to serve as a certified field rogue.",al={"what is the reward","certificate of thievery","quest completion reward"},gp=true},{q="How does this quest fit into rogue training across the Alliance?",a="Rogues across Alliance lands are directed by contacts such as Mathias Shaw's SI:7 handlers in Stormwind to meet Lucius in Lakeshire. The test at Alther's Mill is the final practical trial in their basic field training.",al={"rogue quest chain","si7 connection","redridge rendezvous followup"},it="history"},{q="Why does Lucius send you to Alther's Mill?",a="Lucius trains burgeoning scoundrels for the Alliance and wants to test your practical finesse under pressure. Placing a locked chest right near Alther's Mill—an area encroached upon by Blackrock orcs—forces you to demonstrate real lockpicking skill in a hostile environment rather than in a cozy classroom.",al={"lucius motive","why does lucius want this done","why send me to althers mill"},it="motive",add="bca91f0e"},{q="What is the Token of Thievery for?",a="The Token of Thievery is proof of your handiwork. Locked securely inside Lucius's chest, it serves as physical evidence that you managed to infiltrate Alther's Mill, crack the lock, and slip away undetected. Returning it earns you Lucius's official Certificate of Thievery.",al={"token of thievery use","what is token of thievery","purpose of token of thievery"},it="item",add="7e02fd2a"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you receive your lockpicking tools and field credentials while testing your patience and stealth near Blackrock orcs.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you help train thieves and infiltrators near Lakeshire while watching Blackrock movements."},kw={"alther's mill","blackrock orcs","lakeshire","lockpicking","lucius","redridge mountains","si:7","thieves tools","token of thievery"},rel={"npc:lucius","quest:2281","quest:2300","subzone:lakeshire","zone:redridge"},m={start="Lucius",level="20",faction="Alliance",id=2282,ri={"Token of Thievery"}},src={"Alther's Mill (quest)"}}
E["quest:244"] = {t="quest",n="Encroaching Gnolls",z="redridge",s="Gnolls have reached the western road into Redridge, and Lakeshire fears being cut off. Guard Parker spots camps near the border and sends word to Deputy Feldon. The warning confirms the town’s fear that the beastmen may isolate Redridge.",h="Gnolls have reached the western road into Redridge, and Lakeshire fears being cut off.",sec={{t="Eyes on the Border",b="Guard Parker watches the western border trail, where the road runs from Elwynn Forest into Redridge Mountains. Stormwind’s forces have thinned, leaving the route with few defenders. Parker keeps the gravel road open for supply wagons, but his scouts find gnoll warbands advancing from the crags to the north and east. Their camps lie alarmingly close to the road.",sp=0},{t="A Town Under Siege",b="Deputy Feldon receives the warning near the Lakeshire bridge and sees how much danger the town faces. Redridge gnolls are raiding near Lakeshire, and their camps near the Elwynn border could let them encircle the town and push into the kingdom’s heartland. Stormwind has ignored pleas for reinforcements, leaving Lakeshire’s watch unready for threats from both sides.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who starts this quest?",a="Guard Parker gives you the warning along the road in western Redridge Mountains, near the Elwynn Forest border crossing.",al={"quest giver","where to start","guard parker location"},gp=true},{q="Where can I find Deputy Feldon?",a="Deputy Feldon is in Lakeshire, patrolling the grounds just south of the town’s large stone bridge.",al={"feldon location","who is deputy feldon","turn in location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why are the gnolls an issue on the road?",a="The road to Elwynn Forest is Lakeshire’s only safe land route to the rest of the kingdom. If gnolls take the western slopes, the town could lose its supplies and its way out.",al={"why gnolls matter","redridge gnoll problem","road danger"},it="threat"},{q="Why doesn't Stormwind send help to Lakeshire?",a="With King Varian Wrynn missing and unrest straining the realm, Highlord Bolvar and the court have refused to send royal troops to Redridge. Lakeshire must rely on local deputies and volunteers for its defense.",al={"where are stormwind guards","no reinforcements","lakeshire defense"},it="conflict"},{q="What happens after reporting the gnolls?",a="Deputy Feldon asks you to scout the gnoll camps more closely in Assessing the Threat, to learn how many gnolls have gathered.",al={"next quest","chain follow up"},it="next_step"},{q="Which gnoll packs are encroaching here?",a="Redridge gnolls gather in the hills as the Redridge Gnoll Pack. As human control of the region weakens, they have grown bolder and more coordinated.",al={"which gnolls","redridge gnoll clans"},it="threat"},{q="Why does Guard Parker want this done?",a="Guard Parker is charged with securing this stretch of road leading into the Redridge Mountains, but he has spotted hostile gnoll encampments amassing just to the north and east. Fearing an imminent push that could overwhelm his patrol and cut off the pass, he urgently needs the authorities in Lakeshire informed before the gnolls strike the road or press toward Elwynn.",al={"guard parker motive","why warn lakeshire","why does parker send you"},it="motive",add="e50462f9"},{q="Why does Guard Parker send you instead of going himself?",a="Parker is under strict orders to stand watch and defend the road between Elwynn Forest and Redridge. If he abandons his post to run back to town, the border is left completely unguarded against the lurking packs. An able-bodied traveler heading toward Lakeshire is his best chance to deliver the warning swiftly without abandoning his duty.",al={"why send me","why doesnt parker go","why cant guard parker report"},it="why_me",add="be5d12a2"}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human, you can see how the beastmen’s advance near Elwynn Forest leaves the kingdom’s heart vulnerable while the king is missing.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you know Lakeshire’s isolation threatens the eastern front, making border intelligence vital for travelers and supply convoys."},kw={"assessing the threat","deputy feldon","elwynn border","encroaching gnolls","guard parker","lakeshire","redridge"},rel={"quest:246","npc:deputy-feldon","subzone:lakeshire","topic:gnoll","zone:redridge"},m={start="Guard Parker",["end"]="Deputy Feldon",level="16",faction="Alliance",id=244},src={"Encroaching Gnolls"}}
E["quest:246"] = {t="quest",n="Assessing the Threat",z="redridge",s="Deputy Feldon needs a measure of the gnoll threat near Lakeshire. With the garrison stretched thin and Stormwind withholding reinforcements, he hires travelers to thin the packs and learn their strength.",h="Deputy Feldon needs a measure of the gnoll threat near Lakeshire.",sec={{t="A Strained Frontier",b="Lakeshire faces Blackrock orc warbands from the heights and aggressive gnoll packs in the valleys. Its defenders are too few for ordinary scouting patrols. When reports confirmed gnolls pressing toward the border, Deputy Feldon sought help from travelers. He pays champions to test the enemy in the wild, rather than send guards the town cannot spare.",sp=0},{t="Reconnaissance by Force",b="You scout along Redridge's southern road, striking the camps of Redridge Mongrels and Poachers. Each fight thins the gnolls' forward scouts and disrupts their supply lines. It also reveals whether the packs are roaming scavengers or an organized force threatening Lakeshire. The fighting gives Feldon numbers he can use to plan the town's strained defense.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Deputy Feldon send adventurers instead of town guards?",a="Lakeshire's garrison is badly undermanned. Stormwind City sends no reinforcements, and hostile forces press from several directions, leaving the guards unable to spare soldiers for long patrols along the southern road.",al={"why hire adventurers","where are the guards","lakeshire guard shortage"},it="why_me"},{q="Where are the gnolls located for this mission?",a="The Redridge Mongrels and Poachers camp along the southern road and in the low foothills of the Redridge Mountains, south of Lakeshire and near the border passes.",al={"where are redridge mongrels","gnoll locations redridge","southern road gnolls"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the strategic purpose of culling these gnolls?",a="The fighting pushes back gnolls pressing toward the road, disrupts their supply lines, and gives Feldon firsthand intelligence about the packs' size, weapons, and discipline.",al={"why kill gnolls","threat assessment goal","lakeshire defense"},it="motive"},{q="Does Stormwind City help with the gnoll threat?",a="No. Stormwind's House of Nobles and regency council withhold regular military support from outlying regions such as Redridge. Local leaders, including Magistrate Solomon and Deputy Feldon, must rely on paid mercenaries.",al={"stormwind reinforcements","why won't stormwind help","stormwind army lakeshire"},it="allies"},{q="What does Deputy Feldon do with your report?",a="Deputy Feldon weighs the packs' strength and tenacity, confirming that the southern gnolls pose a serious military danger rather than being isolated beasts. He directs you to help other town leaders shore up their defenses.",al={"feldon's reaction","what happens after assessing threat","turn in report"},it="next_step"},{q="How does this task connect to the prior quest?",a="This follows Encroaching Gnolls. After you alerted the garrison to the gnoll movement, Feldon sent you on a combat patrol to learn how serious the incursion is.",al={"quest line connection","encroaching gnolls followup","prerequisite quest"},it="history"},{q="Who are the Redridge gnolls you are sent to cull?",a="You are dispatched against the Redridge Mongrels and Poachers encamped along the southern road. These savage gnolls are massing right along the town's lifeline, harassing travelers, choking supply routes, and creeping perilously close to Lakeshire itself while the town's defenses are stretched to their limits.",al={"redridge mongrels poachers","who are the gnolls in redridge","redridge gnoll threat"},it="target",add="6de7b21c"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Redridge shows the strain on the Alliance's heartland: neglected border settlements hire champions to survive while the capital looks away.",["race:Human"]="As a human defender, protecting Lakeshire is personal. Frontier families bear the cost of political paralysis in Stormwind Keep.",["class:Warrior"]="Deputy Feldon calls for armed reconnaissance. As a warrior, you wade into fortified camps and break the gnolls' vanguard."},kw={"assessing","feldon","gnolls","lakeshire","mongrel","poacher","reconnaissance","redridge","threat"},rel={"quest:244","npc:deputy-feldon","subzone:lakeshire","zone:redridge","topic:gnoll","topic:stormwind-army","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={level="17",faction="Alliance",id=246},src={"Assessing the Threat"}}
E["quest:249"] = {t="quest",n="Morganth",z="redridge",s="Across Redridge, Theocritus watches Morganth hunt an ancient relic.",h="Across Redridge, Theocritus watches Morganth hunt an ancient relic.",sec={{t="A Watcher Across the Border",b="From the Tower of Azora in eastern Elwynn Forest, Theocritus watches the crags of Redridge through his scrying spells. He sees Morganth, a warlock in the Tower of Ilgalar, searching for the Scythe of Elune. Fearing Morganth is close to claiming it, Theocritus asks Alliance champions to stop him before Stormwind is threatened.",sp=0},{t="Storming the Spire",b="The Tower of Ilgalar rises above the Redridge basin, where gnolls and twisted arcane energies fill its halls. Morganth waits at the summit, wielding shadow magic and guarding his research. To reach him, you climb through hostile ground and face the warlock directly. His Pendant of Shadow can be brought back as proof that the tower has fallen and the threat is broken.",sp=0},{t="The Scythe's Lingering Shadow",b="Morganth's defeat removes an immediate threat to Stormwind, but his search for the Scythe of Elune shows how far the artifact's dark legend reaches. Theocritus is relieved when he receives the Pendant of Shadow. The ancient scythe's whereabouts and the havoc it might bring remain unknown across the surrounding provinces.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Morganth?",a="Morganth is a powerful rogue warlock who lives at the summit of the Tower of Ilgalar in the Redridge Mountains. He studies the dark arts and seeks the Scythe of Elune, an artifact capable of wielding disastrous magic.",al={"morganth identity","who is morganth","morganth backstory"},it="target"},{q="Where is the Tower of Ilgalar?",a="The Tower of Ilgalar stands in the eastern Redridge Mountains, beyond Stonewatch Keep, with Shadowhide gnolls camped around its base.",al={"tower of ilgalar location","where is morganth tower","redridge tower"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Theocritus want Morganth dead?",a="Through scrying spells, Theocritus learned that Morganth was hunting the Scythe of Elune and feared he was close to finding it. The power Morganth sought threatened Redridge and the neighboring kingdom of Stormwind.",al={"theocritus motive","why kill morganth","theocritus quest reason"},it="motive"},{q="What is the Scythe of Elune?",a="The Scythe of Elune is an artifact shrouded in mystery. Theocritus does not explain its powers, but fears that if Morganth finds it, Redridge and Stormwind will feel the warlock's dark might.",al={"scythe of elune lore","what is the scythe","why is the scythe dangerous"},it="threat"},{q="What is the Pendant of Shadow?",a="The Pendant of Shadow is Morganth's magical talisman. It focuses his dark arts and, when brought to Theocritus at the Tower of Azora, proves Morganth has been defeated.",al={"pendant of shadow","morganth pendant","proof of morganth death"},it="item"},{q="What quest chain leads up to this?",a="The chain begins with 'Theocritus' Retrieval' in Elwynn Forest, followed by 'A Watchful Eye' and 'Looking Further'. Those steps recover tools and set up scrying to watch Morganth's tower. This is the chain's final part.",al={"morganth quest chain","morganth prerequisites","how to unlock morganth"},it="history",gp=true},{q="Why does Theocritus send you to face Morganth instead of going himself?",a="Theocritus admits quite plainly that he is not prepared to pit his own magical might directly against Morganth. While he watches over the borders from the Tower of Azora and coordinates defenses against shadow magic, an assault on the Tower of Ilgalar itself demands a bold, capable adventurer willing to breach the warlock's stronghold before Morganth's dark ambitions can threaten all of Stormwind.",al={"why send me","why doesnt theocritus fight morganth","why not theocritus"},it="why_me",add="23819dbd"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you see Theocritus's diligent, scholarly tradition: human mages watch from high towers to guard the realm from rogue spellcasters.",["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you see the danger of unchecked fel and shadow ambitions. Reaching for relics like the Scythe of Elune invites swift destruction.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, whispers of the Scythe of Elune in human hands should alarm you. Its name touches sacred and volatile mysteries for the kaldorei.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you help protect Stormwind's exposed eastern borders. Defeating Morganth keeps Redridge from falling to dark sorcery."},kw={"elwynn","morganth","pendant of shadow","redridge","scythe of elune","theocritus","tower of azora","tower of ilgalar"},rel={"quest:248","quest:94","quest:178","npc:theocritus","subzone:tower-of-ilgalar","subzone:tower-of-azora","quest:1043","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Old Lion Statue / Theocritus",["end"]="Theocritus",level="26",faction="Alliance",id=249,ri={"Pendant of Shadow"}},src={"Morganth (quest)"}}
E["quest:3741"] = {t="quest",n="Hilary's Necklace",z="redridge",s="On the docks at Lakeshire, Hilary loses the necklace her father gave her while fishing. Her friend Shawn asks travelers to retrieve it from Lake Everstill, where their parents forbid them to swim.",h="On the docks at Lakeshire, Hilary loses the necklace her father gave her while fishing.",sec={{t="A Day at the Docks",b="Hilary and Shawn spend the day fishing along Lakeshire's docks, trying to enjoy an ordinary childhood amid the threats around the Redridge Mountains. Hilary drops her treasured necklace into Lake Everstill. After searching the piers and shore without finding it, Shawn asks travelers for help.",sp=0},{t="Perils of Lake Everstill",b="Hilary and Shawn's parents forbid them to swim in Lake Everstill. Aggressive murlocs and hungry threshedons lurk beneath the surface. The children cannot reach the necklace in the glinting mud at the lake bottom, so Shawn turns to travelers for help recovering the gift.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who lost the necklace?",a="Hilary, a young girl in Lakeshire, lost the necklace her father gave her. It matters deeply to her because it was his gift.",al={"who is nida","who lost it","necklace owner","who is hilary"},it="identity"},{q="Why can't Shawn or Hilary swim down and get it themselves?",a="Their parents forbid them to swim in Lake Everstill because aggressive murlocs and predatory threshedons lurk beneath the surface.",al={"why not get it themselves","why kids not swimming"},it="why_me"},{q="Where did the necklace end up?",a="The necklace slipped off the docks and settled into a mound of glinting mud on Lake Everstill's western lake bed.",al={"necklace location","where is necklace","where did it fall"},gp=true},{q="Who is Effsee?",a="Effsee is Hilary's pet kitten in Lakeshire. She keeps Hilary company and joins her in thanking travelers who recover the necklace.",al={"effsee","nida cat","hilary cat"},it="identity"},{q="Who starts the request to find the necklace?",a="Shawn, Hilary's friend, was fishing with her on the docks. He asks travelers to help because he knows how much her father's gift means to her.",al={"who gives quest","shawn role"},it="origin"},{q="Why does this task matter to Lakeshire?",a="Recovering a lost keepsake offers comfort and normalcy to Lakeshire's families, who struggle to live peacefully under constant threat.",al={"lakeshire importance","why help kids"},it="purpose"},{q="Why does Shawn want you to find the necklace?",a="Shawn is just trying to look out for his friend. The two of them spent the entire day fishing along the docks, and Hilary was devastated when her prized trinket went missing. Seeing her distress, Shawn searched everywhere on dry land before realizing it must have tumbled into Lake Everstill.",al={"why does shawn care","shawn motive necklace","why help hilary"},it="motive",add="ce1ad253"},{q="What is Hilary's necklace?",a="It is a cherished personal keepsake given to young Hilary by her father. While it holds little material value to an adventurer, it means the world to a frightened child whose family is enduring the mounting tensions gripping Lakeshire.",al={"what is the necklace","hilarys necklace significance","who gave hilary the necklace"},it="item",add="186564aa"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, helping Lakeshire's beleaguered citizens with personal hardships shows your commitment to protecting everyday townsfolk as well as confronting larger threats."},kw={"effsee","glinting mud","hilary","lake everstill","lakeshire","necklace","nida","redridge","shawn"},rel={"npc:nida","subzone:lakeshire","zone:redridge"},m={start="Shawn",["end"]="Hilary",faction="Alliance",id=3741,ri={"Nida's Necklace"}},src={"Nida's Necklace (quest)"}}
E["quest:89"] = {t="quest",n="The Everstill Bridge",z="redridge",s="In Lakeshire, The Everstill Bridge still waits for repairs. Iron meant for the work went into weapons during the last orc invasion, and Redridge gnolls ambushed the replacement caravan from Stormwind.",h="In Lakeshire, The Everstill Bridge still waits for repairs.",sec={{t="A Town Cut Off",b="You find Lakeshire's stone bridge across Lake Everstill unfinished. It links the western roads toward Elwynn Forest with the far bank and the northern passes. Recent orc incursions brought the town close to ruin. To survive, Lakeshire melted its structural iron into munitions, blades, and plate armor to repel the Blackrock invaders. The bridge was left incomplete and vulnerable.",sp=0},{t="Stolen Shipments",b="Foreman Oslow asked the House of Nobles and Stormwind for fresh materials to finish the repairs. A caravan carrying iron set out, but Redridge gnolls ambushed it on the road. They took iron pikes and rivets to their camps in the northern hills. You can help recover the stolen supplies; without them, the bridge work remains stalled as gnolls and orcs tighten their hold on the mountains.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is the Everstill Bridge unfinished?",a="Lakeshire melted its construction iron into weapons, bullets, and armor to survive the recent orc invasion. Then Redridge gnolls ambushed the replacement shipment from Stormwind, leaving Foreman Oslow without the materials to finish the bridge.",al={"why broken bridge","who broke everstill bridge","lakeshire bridge broken"},it="ruin"},{q="Who is Foreman Oslow?",a="Foreman Oslow supervises the rebuilding of the bridge across Lake Everstill. Without support or supplies from the capital, he depends on travelers to recover building materials stolen from the hills.",al={"foreman oslow","who is oslow"},it="identity"},{q="Who stole the bridge supplies?",a="Redridge gnolls ambushed the caravan from Stormwind and carried the iron pikes and rivets to their camps in the hills behind Lakeshire.",al={"who stole iron rivets","who took the bridge iron"},it="conflict"},{q="Why didn't Stormwind send guards to protect the caravan?",a="With King Varian Wrynn missing, the Stormwind House of Nobles has largely withheld military aid from outlying territories. Redridge Mountains must face gnolls and Blackrock orcs with little support beyond its town militias.",al={"stormwind help lakeshire","why no guards"},it="why_here"},{q="Why did Lakeshire melt down their iron?",a="During the last orc invasion, Lakeshire's defenders ran short of war supplies. The town melted its construction iron into armor, swords, and ammunition to survive the assault.",al={"why melt iron","orc invasion redridge"},it="history"},{q="What supplies are needed to repair the bridge?",a="Foreman Oslow needs heavy iron pikes and iron rivets to secure and anchor the bridge spans across Lake Everstill.",al={"bridge materials","what does oslow need"},it="purpose"},{q="Why does Foreman Oslow need the Everstill Bridge rebuilt?",a="Foreman Oslow is charged with restoring Lakeshire's vital link across Lake Everstill. The bridge connects the town to the surrounding roads and southern Redridge, but previous warfare forced the town to melt its structural iron into weapons and armor. Without bridge supplies, the town remains vulnerable, divided, and unable to support normal transit or defenses.",al={"foreman oslow motive","why rebuild the bridge","why does oslow care"},it="motive",add="f119d943"},{q="What are the Iron Pikes and Iron Rivets for?",a="The iron pikes and rivets are structural hardware meant to reinforce and shore up the wooden scaffolding and stone spans of the Everstill Bridge. They were originally shipped from Stormwind before Redridge gnolls hijacked the supply caravan, leaving Oslow's crew completely halted without metal fastenings.",al={"what are the iron pikes for","iron rivets use","why does oslow need pikes and rivets"},it="item",add="f9ba0cdb"},{q="Why do the Redridge gnolls have the bridge materials?",a="A marauding band of Redridge gnolls ambushed and plundered the caravan traveling from Stormwind, hauling the iron pikes and rivets into the hills north of Lakeshire. The gnolls opportunistically pillage supplies along the roadways, exploiting Lakeshire's isolated state and lack of military protection.",al={"who stole the rivets","why gnolls have iron","redridge gnolls target"},it="target",add="9c1de71f"},{q="Why does Foreman Oslow ask you instead of the town guard?",a="Lakeshire's local garrison is stretched to its absolute limit defending the town perimeter from invading Blackrock orcs and aggressive gnoll packs. With Stormwind offering virtually no military reinforcements, the town watch cannot spare men to scour the hills for stolen building supplies, forcing Oslow to rely on passing adventurers.",al={"why not lakeshire guards","why me everstill bridge","why doesn't the guard get the supplies"},it="why_me",add="ecd0e353"}},ang={["profession:Blacksmithing"]="Lakeshire's defenders were so desperate that they forged weapons from structural pikes and rivets. That effort saved lives but left vital infrastructure unfinished.",["faction:Alliance"]="Lakeshire's supply lines show how Stormwind neglects its outer territories. Local foremen must rely on hired blades to protect trade on the roads."},kw={"everstill bridge","foreman oslow","iron pikes","iron rivets","lakeshire","redridge","redridge gnolls"},rel={"npc:foreman-oslow","subzone:lakeshire","zone:redridge","quest:124","topic:gnoll","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Foreman Oslow",level="20",faction="Alliance",id=89,ri={"Iron Pike","Iron Rivet"}},src={"The Everstill Bridge"}}
E["quest:91"] = {t="quest",n="Solomon's Law",z="redridge",s="In Lakeshire, Solomon's Law puts the Shadowhide gnolls under sentence of death for aiding Morganth, an enemy of Stormwind. Bailiff Conacher issues the decree from the town hall and seeks proof that the sentence has been carried out.",h="In Lakeshire, Solomon's Law puts the Shadowhide gnolls under sentence of death for aiding Morganth, an enemy...",sec={{t="Frontier Justice in Lakeshire",b="Lakeshire governs Redridge with little military help from Stormwind. Magistrate Solomon and the town officials rely on strict frontier authority to keep order. Bailiff Conacher works from the town hall as the magistrate court's arm. When threats reach the township, the court places bounties on offenders and depends on hired mercenaries and traveling defenders to uphold the kingdom's laws.",sp=0},{t="Aiding an Enemy of the Crown",b="The Shadowhide clan faces execution for aiding Morganth, a rogue spellcaster in the eastern hills. Lakeshire and Stormwind law calls for death when someone directly helps a declared enemy of the realm. The gnolls carry out Morganth's bidding, so the court treats them as treasonous fighters rather than wild scavengers.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Solomon and what is his law?",a="Solomon is Magistrate Solomon, Lakeshire's civilian leader. His local decrees and Stormwind's statutes make aiding a declared enemy of the kingdom treason, punishable by death.",al={"who is solomon","solomon law meaning","what is solomons law"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Morganth and why does Lakeshire care about him?",a="Morganth is a rogue practitioner of the Arcane who lives in Redridge's eastern foothills. Stormwind has branded him an enemy, and he uses foul magic to terrorize townsfolk and bend the Shadowhide gnolls to his will.",al={"who is morganth","morganth backstory","why morganth dangerous"},it="threat"},{q="Why are the Shadowhide gnolls being hunted specifically?",a="The Shadowhide gnolls are hunted because they serve Morganth, the dark wizard. Their alliance makes them lawful targets for execution under the town decree.",al={"why kill shadowhides","shadowhide gnolls redridge","why gnolls targeted"},it="target"},{q="What are the pendants for?",a="The Shadowhide gnolls' pendants prove their deaths. Bailiff Conacher requires ten before the court certifies the sentence has been carried out and grants a bounty.",al={"why shadowhide pendants","purpose of pendants","pendants proof"},it="item"},{q="Where does Bailiff Conacher conduct his business?",a="Bailiff Conacher works inside Lakeshire Town Hall with Magistrate Solomon and the other civil officials who manage Redridge.",al={"conacher location","where is bailiff conacher","lakeshire court"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why doesn't Stormwind send royal soldiers to deal with this?",a="Stormwind's kingdom is stretched thin and troubled by political paralysis and unrest across its territories. Lakeshire's requests for soldiers have repeatedly gone unanswered, leaving Magistrate Solomon to hire adventurers.",al={"where is stormwind army","why no guards for gnolls","lakeshire abandoned by stormwind"},it="why_me"},{q="Why does Bailiff Conacher want the Shadowhide gnolls killed?",a="As the magistrate's officer in Lakeshire, Bailiff Conacher is tasked with upholding the laws of the realm. A rogue sorcerer named Morganth has entrenched himself in the eastern foothills and turned the Shadowhide gnoll pack into his personal vanguard. Conacher views their allegiance to a declared enemy of Stormwind as high treason. To him, executing these gnolls is not just about thinning a local nuisance—it is about enforcing the magistrate's legal death sentence upon those who abet criminals of the crown.",al={"conacher motive","why kill shadowhide gnolls","bailiff conacher reason"},it="motive",add="0a2e314c"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Upholding Solomon's decree supports the law on the eastern frontier, where Stormwind's regular forces are conspicuously absent.",["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you bring holy justice and protection to besieged frontier towns by punishing gnolls who willingly serve a dark sorcerer.",["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you face Morganth's agents as a priority, for he has turned Arcane knowledge toward dark terror."},kw={"conacher","gnolls","lakeshire","morganth","pendants","redridge","shadowhide","solomon","town hall"},rel={"npc:bailiff-conacher","subzone:lakeshire-town-hall","subzone:lakeshire","quest:249","topic:gnoll","zone:redridge","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Bailiff Conacher",level="23",faction="Alliance",id=91,ri={"Shadowhide Pendant"}},src={"Solomon's Law"}}
E["quest:92"] = {t="quest",n="Redridge Goulash",z="redridge",s="In Lakeshire, Redridge Goulash helps feed a town under strain. Chef Breanna fed the active Stormwind garrison during the recent Blackrock orc uprising, emptying her pantry and leaving her to seek hearty ingredients from the mountains.",h="In Lakeshire, Redridge Goulash helps feed a town under strain.",sec={{t="A Bare Mountain Pantry",b="Lakeshire remains under siege from Blackrock orcs, gnolls, and ferocious wild beasts. When the recent orc uprising began along the ridges, Chef Breanna took on feeding the entire brigade of Stormwind troops stationed in town. Keeping the active garrison fed quickly emptied her cupboards, though the town still had plenty of hungry mouths.",sp=0},{t="Mountain Bounty",b="With her cupboards bare, Chef Breanna looks to the dangerous wilderness beyond Lakeshire's gates. Her signature goulash calls for tough mountain condor meat, seasoned snouts from formidable Great Goretusks, and crisp leg meat from giant tarantulas that prowl the hills.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is Chef Breanna out of food supplies?",a="During the recent Blackrock orc uprising, Chef Breanna fed the entire brigade of Stormwind troops stationed to defend Lakeshire. Keeping the active garrison supplied emptied her cupboards.",al={"why empty pantry","breanna pantry","why no food"},it="motive"},{q="What ingredients are used to make Redridge Goulash?",a="Redridge Goulash calls for five pieces of Tough Condor Meat, five Great Goretusk Snouts, and five helpings of Crisp Spider Meat, gathered from creatures in the surrounding mountains.",al={"goulash ingredients","what is in redridge goulash","goulash meat"},it="item"},{q="Where is Chef Breanna located?",a="Chef Breanna tends her hearth and cooking kettles in Lakeshire, along the northern shores of Lake Everstill in the Redridge Mountains.",al={"breanna location","where is chef breanna","lakeshire chef"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why doesn't Lakeshire just import food from Stormwind City?",a="Orcs, Blackrock raiders, and gnolls choke the mountain passes, while Stormwind's resources are stretched thin. Lakeshire often depends on local wildlife and visiting adventurers for food.",al={"stormwind supplies","why not trade with stormwind","lakeshire food shortage"},it="conflict"},{q="Is Redridge Goulash considered a delicacy?",a="Chef Breanna and Lakeshire's frontier folk consider the finished dish a hearty mountain delicacy, though its spider meat, boar snouts, and leathery condor flesh may sound harsh to outsiders.",al={"is goulash good","tasty goulash","redridge delicacy"},it="fame"},{q="What brigade did Breanna have to feed?",a="Chef Breanna cooked for the Stormwind soldiers stationed in Lakeshire to push back the Blackrock orc forces pressing down from the northern ridges.",al={"stormwind brigade","who defended lakeshire","troops in lakeshire"},it="history"},{q="What is the Great Goretusk Snout for?",a="Chef Breanna uses Great Goretusk Snouts as one of the hearty, flavorful meat bases simmered into Redridge Goulash. The local goretusks roaming Redridge Mountains provide thick, fatty cuts that help give the stew its rich body, especially now that her regular pantry supplies have been emptied.",al={"great goretusk snout use","why get goretusk snouts","breanna goretusk snout"},it="item",add="4a7f1419"},{q="What is the Tough Condor Meat for?",a="Tough Condor Meat is one of the essential game ingredients Chef Breanna requires for Redridge Goulash. While lean and fibrous on its own, slow-cooking condor meat over a fire tenderizes the flesh and imparts the deep, savory flavor traditional to this regional dish.",al={"tough condor meat use","why get condor meat","breanna condor meat"},it="item",add="147c758b"},{q="What is the Crisp Spider Meat for?",a="Crisp Spider Meat serves as a key protein in Chef Breanna's Redridge Goulash. Harvested from the giant arachnids of the Redridge hills, the meat adds a distinct texture and earthy flavor to round out the stew alongside the condor fowl and goretusk pork.",al={"crisp spider meat use","why get spider meat","breanna spider meat"},it="item",add="bcb0ca74"},{q="Why does Chef Breanna need an adventurer to gather ingredients?",a="Lakeshire's defenders are stretched to their limits guarding the town from Blackrock orcs and gnolls, leaving neither guards nor Breanna free to forage the dangerous wilderness. With her kitchen depleted after feeding the Stormwind troops, Breanna must rely on capable traveling adventurers to brave the predators in the surrounding hills and restock her larder.",al={"why can't breanna hunt","why doesn't the guard get meat","why me redridge goulash"},it="why_me",add="bc77dafb"}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="As a cook exploring the Eastern Kingdoms, you can see how Chef Breanna turns fierce mountain beasts into sustaining, savory fare.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can see how the Blackrock orc invasion has strained Lakeshire's stores, garrisons, and civilian life."},kw={"blackrock orcs","chef breanna","condor meat","goretusk snout","lakeshire","redridge goulash","redridge mountains","spider meat"},rel={"npc:chef-breanna","subzone:lakeshire","zone:redridge","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Chef Breanna",level="18",faction="Alliance",id=92,ri={"Crisp Spider Meat","Great Goretusk Snout","Tough Condor Meat"}},src={"Redridge Goulash (quest)"}}
E["quest:95999"] = {t="quest",n="WANTED: Incinerator Gar'im",z="redridge",s="In Lakeshire, a handsome bounty calls for the death of Incinerator Gar'im. The hostile orc commander is entrenched in Render's Valley, where he leads shadowcasters and is said to work with the Blackrock clan at Stonewatch Keep. Magistrate Solomon offers the bounty for proof of Gar'im's demise.",h="In Lakeshire, a handsome bounty calls for the death of Incinerator Gar'im.",sec={{t="A Fire in Render's Valley",b="Blackrock orcs are pressing out from their mountain strongholds, making the Redridge Mountains more dangerous. In Render's Valley, Gar'im leads an incursion with loyal shadowcasters and dark sorcery. Lakeshire's guard is stretched thin, and the crown's armies are largely absent. Magistrate Solomon has called on independent fighters to eliminate Gar'im, who is said to work with the Blackrock at Stonewatch Keep.",sp=0},{t="Proof of Demise",b="Gar'im is known for destructive magic and command over shadow-weaving casters. To claim the township's reward, hunters must enter enemy-held territory, defeat him, and return his shattered staff to Lakeshire's town hall as proof that the threat has ended.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Incinerator Gar'im?",a="Incinerator Gar'im is an orc warlord and spellcaster leading an incursion in Render's Valley. He is said to work with the Blackrock orcs of Stonewatch Keep and commands dangerous shadowcasters.",al={"who is gar'im","garim","incinerator garim"}},{q="Where can Incinerator Gar'im be found?",a="Gar'im camps among hostile orc forces in Render's Valley, in the southeastern Redridge Mountains.",al={"gar'im location","where is garim","render's valley location"}},{q="Who posted the bounty for Gar'im?",a="Magistrate Solomon posted the bounty on Lakeshire's behalf, hoping to stem the orc incursions bearing down on the embattled town.",al={"who gave the bounty","solomon bounty"}},{q="What proof is required to claim the bounty?",a="Magistrate Solomon requires the Broken Staff of Incinerator Gar'im as proof of the spellcaster's death before paying the reward.",al={"garim proof","broken staff quest item"}},{q="What threat do Gar'im and his followers pose?",a="Gar'im wields lethal destructive magic and is flanked by shadowcasters. Together, they strengthen the Blackrock clan's hold in Redridge and threaten to overwhelm Lakeshire if left unchecked.",al={"gar'im abilities","shadowcasters redridge"}},{q="Why is Lakeshire relying on bounties rather than the Stormwind army?",a="Stormwind has left Redridge largely to defend itself amid political strife and troop shortages. Magistrate Solomon has had to hire willing fighters to kill enemy leaders.",al={"why bounties lakeshire","where is stormwind army"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Defeating Incinerator Gar'im protects Lakeshire's vulnerable citizens from the leader of an orc incursion and his dangerous shadowcasters.",["class:Mage"]="Gar'im and his shadowcasters wield a corrupted form of offensive arcana and shadow magic, calling for a swift response with counter-spellcraft."},kw={"blackrock","bounty","gar'im","incinerator","lakeshire","render's valley","shadowcaster","solomon"},rel={"npc:magistrate-solomon","subzone:render-s-valley","subzone:lakeshire","subzone:stonewatch-keep","subzone:stonewatch","zone:redridge"},m={level="25",id=95999},src={"In-game quest text: WANTED: Incinerator Gar'im"},fv=true}
E["quest:98247"] = {t="quest",n="Shipping Label",z="redridge",s="A damaged Shipping Label points toward the Azeroth Commerce Authority's trade hub at Three Corners in the Redridge Mountains. It marks a supply crate as the authority's property and shows travelers where to report it.",h="A damaged Shipping Label points toward the Azeroth Commerce Authority's trade hub at Three Corners in the...",sec={{t="A Stray Delivery",b="A damaged label marks a stocked supply crate as freight belonging to the Azeroth Commerce Authority. The destination and recipient have been torn away, but the label tells anyone who finds the cargo to return it or report to the authority's trade outpost in the Redridge Mountains. Beside the formal text, a rough map sketches the roads toward the Three Corners intersection.",sp=0},{t="The Commerce Authority's Hub",b="At Three Corners, representatives of the Azeroth Commerce Authority enlist travelers as independent couriers. The authority does not bind haulers to strict merchant contracts. Instead, it runs an informal network that compensates them with Merchant's Favor for recovering missing cargo and completing abandoned deliveries along the highway.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Shipping Label?",a="The Shipping Label is a damaged freight marker attached to a supply crate owned by the Azeroth Commerce Authority. The recipient's name is missing, but the label directs whoever finds the crate to report to the authority's hub at Three Corners.",al={"what is shipping label","shipping label quest","torn shipping label"}},{q="What is the Azeroth Commerce Authority?",a="The Azeroth Commerce Authority organizes logistics, trade, and freight across the region. It keeps local trade hubs to recover lost shipments and employs roving couriers without long-term contracts.",al={"who is aca","azeroth commerce authority","what is the azeroth commerce authority"}},{q="Where is the Azeroth Commerce Authority trade hub located?",a="The Azeroth Commerce Authority's trade hub is at the Three Corners crossroads in the Redridge Mountains, along the roads linking Elwynn Forest, Duskwood, and Lakeshire.",al={"where is aca trade hub","three corners hub","where to turn in shipping label"}},{q="What is Merchant's Favor?",a="Merchant's Favor is scrip or credit the Azeroth Commerce Authority grants to independent couriers. Affiliates can use it to buy trade goods and logistical services at the authority's posts.",al={"what is merchants favor","merchants favor","aca compensation"}},{q="How do you become an affiliate of the Azeroth Commerce Authority?",a="To become an affiliate, you need no formal contract, paperwork, or long-term commitment. The Azeroth Commerce Authority asks couriers to help return or complete misplaced deliveries they encounter on the road.",al={"how to become aca affiliate","joining aca","do i need a contract"}},{q="What happens to the crate after delivering the label?",a="After you deliver the label, representatives at the trade hub ask about the crate it came from. Returning empty or fulfilled shipping containers remains vital to their trade operations.",al={"what happens to the crate","missing crate","do they want the crate"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler in the southern territories, you can help the Azeroth Commerce Authority recover stray cargo and secure overland transport routes from its hub at Three Corners."},kw={"azeroth commerce authority","crate","delivery","merchants favor","redridge mountains","shipping label","three corners"},rel={"subzone:three-corners","zone:redridge"},m={id=98247},src={"In-game quest text: Shipping Label"},fv=true}
E["quest:98386"] = {t="quest",n="Alther's Mill",z="redridge",s="Workers at Alther's Mill cannot send timber to Lakeshire while giant spiders overrun the eastern lumberyard. Foreman Oslow needs the wood to finish the town bridge.",h="Workers at Alther's Mill cannot send timber to Lakeshire while giant spiders overrun the eastern lumberyard.",sec={{t="A Bottleneck in Lumber",b="Foreman Oslow is trying to keep bridge repairs on schedule in Lakeshire. Blackrock orcs, gnoll packs, and murlocs along Lake Everstill already strain his workforce. Now giant tarantulas have overrun Alther's Mill to the east, stopping the timber shipments the bridge needs.",sp=0},{t="Clearing the Infestation",b="Spiders lurk among the timber stacks, leaving the mill useless. Foreman Oslow cannot risk sending laborers into a nest of greater tarantulas, so he hires capable adventurers to clear the spiders and destroy their egg clutches. He is irritated that Alther let the mill fall into disarray, but Lakeshire needs the lumber before the bridge work can continue.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Foreman Oslow?",a="Foreman Oslow is the stonemason overseeing repairs and rebuilding of the bridge in Lakeshire. Local threats keep delaying his work.",al={"who is foreman oslow","foreman oslow redridge"}},{q="What is Alther's Mill?",a="Alther's Mill is a lumber mill east of Lakeshire in the Redridge Mountains. Its timber shipments supply construction around Lakeshire, including the bridge.",al={"what is althers mill","where is althers mill"}},{q="Who is Alther?",a="Alther operates the lumber mill east of Lakeshire. Foreman Oslow holds him responsible for managing the site, now overrun by spiders.",al={"who is alther","where is ol alther"}},{q="Why does Foreman Oslow need Alther's Mill cleared?",a="Foreman Oslow cannot safely send workers to gather lumber while tarantulas infest the mill. Clearing the spiders and destroying their eggs lets timber deliveries for the bridge resume safely.",al={"why clear althers mill","why kill spiders redridge"}},{q="What is infesting Alther's Mill?",a="Greater tarantulas and clutches of spider eggs infest the mill, threatening any workers sent to collect lumber.",al={"what spiders at althers mill","redridge spiders"}},{q="What bridge is Foreman Oslow trying to build?",a="Foreman Oslow is rebuilding the bridge in Lakeshire. Hostile orcs, gnolls, murlocs, and local pests that threaten lumber supplies keep delaying the work.",al={"what bridge in redridge","lakeshire bridge"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you know Lakeshire needs its bridge rebuilt, but constant threats keep drawing resources away from the work."},kw={"alther's mill","bridge","foreman oslow","lakeshire","lumber mill","redridge mountains","tarantula"},rel={"quest:2282","npc:foreman-oslow","zone:redridge","topic:gnoll","topic:murloc"},m={id=98386},src={"In-game quest text: Alther's Mill"},fv=true}
E["quest:98387"] = {t="quest",n="Blackrock Blockade",z="redridge",s="Marshal Marris is pressing the Blackrock Blockade east of Lake Everstill. Lakeshire's guard aims to starve out the Blackrock orcs and take their weapons.",h="Marshal Marris is pressing the Blackrock Blockade east of Lake Everstill.",sec={{t="A War of Attrition",b="Blackrock raiders in Redridge are pushing Alliance forces to their limits. Cut off from regular supply trains, their forward parties live off the hills. Marshal Marris knows even fierce orcs cannot keep fighting without food and steel.",sp=0},{t="Severing the Forward Camps",b="South of Stonewatch Keep, Blackrock camps lead the clan's advance. Lakeshire's defenders strike those camps to seize supplies and stolen weapons, weakening the orcs' fighting strength and morale.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the goal of the Blackrock Blockade?",a="Lakeshire's guard aims to weaken the Blackrock camps south of Stonewatch Keep. By taking their food and weapons, the defenders hope to starve the orcs and blunt their advance into Redridge.",al={"what is blackrock blockade","blackrock blockade goal","blockade purpose"}},{q="Who issues this assignment?",a="Marshal Marris, who commands Lakeshire's town guard, directs the effort to disrupt Blackrock supplies and defend Redridge.",al={"who gives blackrock blockade","quest giver","marshal marris quest"}},{q="Where are these Blackrock encampments located?",a="The Blackrock camps lie in the eastern hills of Redridge Mountains, south of Stonewatch Keep and across the river from Lakeshire.",al={"where are the orcs","blackrock camp location","where is stonewatch camp"}},{q="Why is Lakeshire relying on attrition rather than a direct assault?",a="Lakeshire's guard has too few soldiers and little help from Stormwind. The Blackrock orcs have pushed into Alliance lands and now lack supplies, so the guard seeks to wear them down rather than attack head-on.",al={"why starve the orcs","why not attack stonewatch directly","lakeshire strategy"}},{q="What weapons are being confiscated from the orcs?",a="Marshal Marris wants the weapons and supplies stored in the Blackrock camps seized, leaving the orcs without their tools of war.",al={"what items needed","what axes","battleworn axes lore"}},{q="Are these orcs affiliated with Thrall's Horde?",a="No. The Blackrock orcs in Redridge belong to the renegade Dark Horde based at Blackrock Mountain. They reject Thrall's leadership and remain hostile to both the Alliance and the new Horde.",al={"are these horde orcs","is blackrock horde","thrall blackrock clan"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Every weapon taken from the Blackrock vanguard buys Lakeshire time as it faces hostile armies with little aid from Stormwind.",["class:Warrior"]="In close fights with rugged Blackrock orcs, taking away their heavy cleavers and supplies is a basic part of frontier warfare."},kw={"battleworn axe","blackrock blockade","blackrock clan","lakeshire","marshal marris","redridge mountains","stonewatch keep"},rel={"npc:marshal-marris","subzone:lakeshire","subzone:stonewatch-keep","subzone:stonewatch","item:battleworn-axe","zone:redridge","topic:alliance"},m={level="21",id=98387},src={"In-game quest text: Blackrock Blockade"},fv=true}
E["quest:98407"] = {t="quest",n="Show of Force",z="redridge",s="Deputy Feldon sends you to drive gnoll packs back from Lakeshire. The Redridge guards need proof that the thrashers have been beaten.",h="Deputy Feldon sends you to drive gnoll packs back from Lakeshire.",sec={{t="A Bold Encroachment",b="Gnoll packs have grown bolder in the Redridge Mountains. Their camps now lie close to Lakeshire and the human homesteads beyond it. Stormwind has too few soldiers to spare for the borderlands, so local authorities depend on travelers to hold the perimeter. The gnolls have not yet struck the town, but their camps bring them within reach of its homes.",sp=0},{t="Speaking Their Language",b="Deputy Feldon knows the gnolls respect strength above all. He wants you to hunt their fiercest fighters, the gnoll thrashers, and bring back their spiked collars as proof of defeat. By breaking the front line and showing the trophies, Lakeshire's defenders hope to frighten the surviving packs into retreating to the highlands.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who offers this quest and where are they located?",a="Deputy Feldon offers this work from the town guard perimeter near Lakeshire in the Redridge Mountains.",al={"quest giver","deputy feldon location","who gives show of force"}},{q="Why are the gnolls pushing so close to Lakeshire?",a="The gnolls have grown bold while Lakeshire's defenses are stretched and Stormwind sends little military aid. They have established hunting camps close to human settlements.",al={"why are gnolls attacking","gnoll threat redridge","why gnolls close"}},{q="What enemies need to be defeated for this mission?",a="You are sent after gnoll thrashers, the more dangerous fighters in the local packs, who wear spiked collars.",al={"which gnolls","what mobs to kill","gnoll thrashers"}},{q="Why does Deputy Feldon want spiked collars specifically?",a="Deputy Feldon wants the thrashers' collars as a show of strength, to frighten the other gnolls into retreating to the hills.",al={"why spiked collars","collar purpose","why take collars"}},{q="Can Stormwind provide soldiers to deal with the gnolls?",a="Stormwind has sent almost no reinforcements, leaving Redridge to defend itself amid instability and troop shortages across the kingdom.",al={"stormwind help redridge","why no stormwind army","where are the guards"}},{q="Where are the gnolls typically encamped in Redridge?",a="Gnoll camps lie across the hills and low ridges by Lake Everstill and along the roads east toward Stonewatch.",al={"gnoll camps","where to find gnolls","gnoll locations redridge"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Lakeshire is one of the Alliance's easternmost strongholds in the southern Eastern Kingdoms. Its borders must hold against attacks by wild beasts.",["race:Human"]="As a human, Redridge's settlers and townsfolk are your fellow subjects of Stormwind. They are left exposed to marauders and rely on their own people to drive them back.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you meet the gnolls with direct force. They yield only to strength, so disciplined fighting at the front can break their ranks."},kw={"deputy feldon","gnoll thrasher","gnolls","lakeshire","redridge mountains","show of force","spiked collar"},rel={"npc:deputy-feldon","subzone:lakeshire","zone:redridge","topic:gnoll","topic:alliance","topic:human"},m={level="17",id=98407},src={"In-game quest text: Show of Force"},fv=true}
E["subzone:alther-s-mill"] = {t="subzone",n="Alther's Mill",z="redridge",s="In the Redridge Mountains, Alther's Mill lies in ruins northeast of Lakeshire. Once it supplied timber to local builders, but now scavengers and predators haunt its grounds. Travelers heading east toward Stonewatch pass this grim mark of the frontier.",h="In the Redridge Mountains, Alther's Mill lies in ruins northeast of Lakeshire.",sec={{t="An Abandoned Frontier Mill",b="Alther's Mill once supplied timber for Lakeshire and the nearby settlements. The clearing northeast of Lake Everstill gave millers access to timber in the mountains. Trouble spread across Stormwind's kingdom, and the Blackrock clan came down from the heights of Stonewatch. The millers abandoned their work, leaving the timber buildings and wheel to decay.",sp=0},{t="Shadows and Scrap",b="With the workers gone, monstrous tarantulas, carrion vultures, and raiders took over the mill. Travelers on the path to the eastern passes must skirt its shadowed grounds carefully. Shadowy operatives and thieves also use the abandoned compound. Its discarded storage boxes and hidden corners let them practice lockpicking and carry out covert trades beyond the Lakeshire Town Watch's gaze.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Alther's Mill?",a="Alther's Mill lies northeast of Lakeshire in the Redridge Mountains. It once harvested and processed timber for nearby settlements, until dangers in the wilderness forced the millers to leave.",al={"alther's mill","althers mill","what is this place","what was alther's mill"},it="place"},{q="Why is the mill abandoned?",a="The mill was abandoned as regional defenses weakened after the First and Second Wars. Giant spiders and Blackrock orcs made the frontier too dangerous for ordinary laborers without royal military protection.",al={"why abandoned","who abandoned althers mill","what happened to the millers"},it="ruin"},{q="What creatures roam around the mill?",a="Giant mountain tarantulas, scavenger buzzards, and roving predators overrun the mill grounds and nearby scrublands. Stray marauders also travel between Stonewatch and Lake Everstill.",al={"enemies at althers mill","creatures at mill","what lives here"},it="danger"},{q="Why do rogues visit Alther's Mill?",a="Alliance rogues visit Alther's Mill to practice picking locked footlockers. Their trainers send them to the isolated, debris-strewn grounds to earn valuable thieving certifications.",al={"rogue quest mill","althers mill lockpicking","thieving certificate"},gp=true},{q="What happened to Alther's Mill?",a="Alther's Mill was once an active lumber mill serving the kingdom of Stormwind and the people of Redridge. As the region grew increasingly isolated and threatened by hostile wildlife and invading orcs from the mountains, the mill fell out of human hands. Abandoned by its workers, the site was eventually overrun by wild beasts, wandering scavengers, and stray orcs passing through toward Stonewatch Keep.",al={"alther's mill history","what happened at althers mill","history of alther mill"},it="history",add="f58217b4"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue of the Alliance, you know Alther's Mill as a quiet place to practice lockpicking. Thieves' syndicates use its scattered lockboxes and secluded grounds for training.",["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, Alther's Mill recalls Stormwind's strained frontier garrisons. Valuable industry lies broken and abandoned within sight of Lakeshire."},kw={"alther's mill","althers mill","lakeshire","lockpicking","lumber mill","redridge","spiders","stonewatch"},rel={"zone:redridge","subzone:lakeshire","subzone:stonewatch","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:alliance","subzone:stonewatch-keep"},src={"Alther's Mill"}}
E["subzone:galardell-valley"] = {t="subzone",n="Galardell Valley",z="redridge",s="Gnolls prowl Galardell Valley beneath the Tower of Ilgalar in northeastern Redridge. The canyon is a danger to the settlements nearby.",h="Gnolls prowl Galardell Valley beneath the Tower of Ilgalar in northeastern Redridge.",sec={{t="A Den of Beasts and Shadow",b="Redridge gnolls prowl Galardell Valley, beyond the reach of Lakeshire's defenders. They roam the lowlands and camp along the canyon floor under brutal pack leaders such as Lieutenant Fangore. Above the ravines rises the Tower of Ilgalar, stronghold of the renegade mage Morganth. The gnolls and the tower keep the valley a source of dread for nearby settlements.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Galardell Valley located?",a="Galardell Valley lies in the far northeastern corner of the Redridge Mountains, behind the high crags beyond the roads leading north from Lake Everstill.",al={"galardell valley location","where is galardell valley","how to find galardell valley"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What creatures live in the valley?",a="Bloodthirsty gnoll packs roam the valley trails in dense groups, led by dangerous brutes such as Lieutenant Fangore.",al={"mobs in galardell valley","who lives in galardell valley","galardell enemies"},it="residents"},{q="What is the dark tower overlooking the valley?",a="The Tower of Ilgalar is the stone stronghold of the rogue sorcerer Morganth, overlooking the valley.",al={"galardell valley tower","spire above galardell","tower near gnolls redridge"}},{q="Who is Lieutenant Fangore?",a="Lieutenant Fangore is a formidable gnoll leader in the valley. Cunning and fierce, he howls for aid from nearby gnoll packs when challenged, and they can quickly overwhelm unwary travelers.",al={"fangore","lieutenant fangore","galardell valley boss"},it="leader"},{q="What is Galardell Valley?",a="Galardell Valley is a rugged basin tucked into the northeastern reaches of the Redridge Mountains. Dominated by the looming silhouette of the Tower of Ilgalar, the valley has fallen into hostile hands, completely overrun by packs of aggressive gnolls and shrouded in dark magic.",al={"what is galardell valley","galardell valley lore","tell me about galardell valley"},it="place",add="3f06acf8"},{q="How dangerous is Galardell Valley?",a="It is extremely hazardous. Fierce gnoll packs patrol the crags and dense brush, working together to swarm intruders. Worse still, their chieftain, Lieutenant Fangore, can quickly summon nearby reinforcements to overwhelm unwary travelers, all beneath the watchful gaze of the dark sorcerer Morganth.",al={"is galardell valley dangerous","galardell valley danger","is it safe here"},it="danger",add="eb0794a1"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Lakeshire's overwhelmed town guard cannot secure the northeast road while gnoll packs and Morganth's dark presence hold Galardell Valley."},kw={"fangore","galardell valley","gnolls","morganth","redridge","tower of ilgalar"},rel={"subzone:tower-of-ilgalar","zone:redridge","quest:249","topic:gnoll"},src={"Galardell Valley"}}
E["subzone:lake-everstill"] = {t="subzone",n="Lake Everstill",z="redridge",s="Murlocs and lake beasts now make Lake Everstill dangerous beside Lakeshire. Once known for calm fishing and clear mountain runoff, its waters and shores have grown perilous.",h="Murlocs and lake beasts now make Lake Everstill dangerous beside Lakeshire.",sec={{t="Heart of the Valley",b="Lake Everstill fills Redridge's central basin beside Lakeshire. Its clear waters run east toward Stonewatch, and a bridge crosses the lake at the heart of town. The lake has long supported local trade and drawn anglers seeking quiet. Now, wilderness threats have broken that calm along the shore.",sp=0},{t="Trouble in the Depths",b="Hostile murlocs have made camps along the northern and eastern shallows, disrupting trade and harrying fishermen. Dangerous threshers patrol the deeper waters below.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What dangerous creatures live in Lake Everstill?",a="Hostile murloc tribes crowd the shallows, including scouts, tidecallers, and flesheaters. Giant threshers and aggressive muckdwellers patrol beneath the surface.",al={"what is in the lake","lake everstill monsters","redridge lake mobs"},it="danger"},{q="Where does the water from Lake Everstill flow?",a="An eastern river carries Lake Everstill's water past the slopes below Stonewatch, a stronghold held by Blackrock.",al={"lake everstill river","where does the lake go"},it="place"},{q="Can you fish safely in Lake Everstill?",a="Catfish and sagefish fill the lake, but fishing has become dangerous. Murloc raiding parties camp along the water's edge, and large threshers attack anyone who ventures too far into the deep.",al={"fishing lake everstill","is it safe to fish lakeshire"},gp=true},{q="What is Lake Everstill?",a="Lake Everstill is the large, azure body of water sitting at the heart of the Redridge Mountains. Its crystal-clear waters frame the town of Lakeshire, which rests along its northern banks and connects to the eastern shore via the Everstill Bridge. Fed by mountain streams, its waters eventually drain eastward near Stonewatch Keep.",al={"lake everstill overview","what is this lake","about lake everstill"},it="place",add="f0f5bd2b"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage passing through Lakeshire, you will find the lake's dangers mundane rather than arcane. Murloc camps crowd the shallows, while threshers patrol deeper waters.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you know that control of the lake and its crossings is vital to Lakeshire's survival against coordinated incursions by Redridge murlocs and nearby Blackrock orcs."},kw={"everstill bridge","lake everstill","lakeshire","murlocs","redridge"},rel={"subzone:lakeshire","zone:redridge","topic:murloc","subzone:stonewatch"},src={"Lake Everstill"}}
E["subzone:lakeridge-highway"] = {t="subzone",n="Lakeridge Highway",z="redridge",s="Travelers on Lakeridge Highway face ruin and danger along Lake Everstill's southern shore. Before the First War, this vital, heavily traveled road carried trade through Redridge; now gnolls and Blackrock orcs make passage perilous.",h="Travelers on Lakeridge Highway face ruin and danger along Lake Everstill's southern shore.",sec={{t="A Fallen Artery",b="Before the First War, Lakeridge Highway carried goods and travelers through Redridge as a busy trade route along Lake Everstill's southern shore. In those peaceful days, travelers crossed between the valley settlements and the eastern heights under Stormwind's protection. The Horde's march shattered that safety, leaving eastern Redridge contested and desolate.",sp=0},{t="Peril on the Road",b="After Blackrock orcs seized Stonewatch Keep, regular road repairs and patrols stopped. Lakeridge Highway soon crumbled into an overgrown track, contested by savage gnoll packs. Stormwind's forces are spread thin and cannot reinforce Lakeshire, leaving the highway officially unsafe. Travelers bound for the eastern ridges must face gnoll ambushes along the way.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does the Lakeridge Highway lead?",a="Lakeridge Highway follows Lake Everstill's southern shore east from Lakeshire toward the foothills around Stonewatch Keep and the eastern mountains of Redridge.",al={"where does lakeridge highway go","lakeridge highway path","where is lakeridge highway"},it="place"},{q="Why is the highway abandoned?",a="Lakeridge Highway fell into disuse after the First War, especially when Blackrock orcs fortified Stonewatch Keep. Stormwind lacked the forces to secure and maintain the road, leaving hostile gnolls free to move in and choking off civilian travel.",al={"why is it abandoned","why is lakeridge highway empty","lakeridge highway fallen into disuse"},it="ruin"},{q="What threats wander the road today?",a="Aggressive gnolls ambush travelers who stray from Lakeshire, while Blackrock orc scouts still operate from the eastern strongholds.",al={"dangers on lakeridge highway","mobs on lakeridge highway","who controls lakeridge highway"},it="danger"},{q="Was the highway always dangerous?",a="No. Before the First War, Lakeridge Highway was a well-kept, heavily traveled route that safely linked Redridge's heartland with its eastern outposts.",al={"lakeridge highway history","highway before the war"},it="history"},{q="What is the Lakeridge Highway?",a="The Lakeridge Highway is an old thoroughfare running along the southern shore of Lake Everstill in the Redridge Mountains. In the peaceful days before the First War, it served as a vital, heavily traveled route connecting the settlements of the region. Today, it lies neglected and contested, linking the beleaguered town of Lakeshire to the dangerous eastern heights.",al={"what is lakeridge highway","lakeridge highway lore","lakeridge road"},it="place",add="d838b935"},{q="Why is it called Lakeridge Highway?",a="The highway takes its name directly from its geography: it traces the high ridges overlooking the southern waters of Lake Everstill in the Redridge Mountains, carving a path between the lake's banks and the rising southern cliffs.",al={"lakeridge highway name meaning","why lakeridge highway","lakeridge name origin"},it="name",add="79cf79b5"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, Lakeridge Highway shows how far Stormwind's neglected frontier reaches: roads just beyond Lakeshire have been left to gnolls and orcs for lack of reinforcements."},kw={"gnolls","highway","lake everstill","lakeridge","redridge","road","stonewatch"},rel={"zone:redridge","subzone:lake-everstill","subzone:lakeshire","subzone:stonewatch-keep","subzone:stonewatch","topic:gnoll","topic:first-war"},src={"Lakeridge Highway"}}
E["subzone:lakeshire"] = {t="subzone",n="Lakeshire",z="redridge",s="Lakeshire's defenders face attacks from orcs, gnolls, and murlocs along Lake Everstill. Magistrate Solomon leads the town, while Marshal Marris commands its guard.",h="Lakeshire's defenders face attacks from orcs, gnolls, and murlocs along Lake Everstill.",sec={{t="A Town Under Siege",b="Lakeshire once offered peace in the foothills east of Stormwind. Now it is the kingdom's hardest-pressed frontier. Blackrock clan orcs swept down from the north and overran the garrison at Stonewatch Keep. Dark wizardry stirred Shadowhide gnolls into organized raiding parties. Blackrock saboteurs also broke parts of the Everstill Bridge. Foreman Oslow and his crew struggle to mend the span under threat of attack. Murlocs crowd the lake's shores, while gnolls stalk the high passes. Lakeshire's defenders are close to breaking.",sp=0},{t="Abandoned by the Crown",b="Magistrate Solomon sent repeated pleas for help across the mountains, but Stormwind City provided almost no soldiers. The kingdom's resources were drained by internal strife, and royal councilors dismissed Redridge's danger as exaggerated border skirmishes. Dwarven reinforcements sent from Ironforge were ambushed and vanished in the Burning Steppes. Marshal Marris and his few remaining guards held the barricades alone. Lakeshire depended on the courage of roaming mercenaries and freelance adventurers hired from the town hall.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who governs Lakeshire?",a="Magistrate Solomon governs Lakeshire from the town hall. Marshal Marris leads local defense and policing with the battered remains of the town guard.",al={"lakeshire leader","who is in charge of lakeshire","magistrate of lakeshire"},it="residents"},{q="Why won't Stormwind send soldiers to help Lakeshire?",a="Stormwind's forces are stretched thin by unrest across the region. Royal councilors, especially Lady Katrana Prestor, persuaded Highlord Bolvar Fordragon not to send standing troops to Redridge, so the Crown relied on deputized adventurers.",al={"why no stormwind reinforcements","stormwind army lakeshire","why is lakeshire abandoned"},sp=1,it="conflict"},{q="What happened to the Everstill Bridge?",a="Blackrock orcs damaged the stone bridge during their raids across the lake, disrupting trade and transport. Foreman Oslow oversees repairs, but missing tools and continuing attacks have slowed the work.",al={"broken bridge redridge","who broke everstill bridge","foreman oslow bridge"},it="place"},{q="What threats currently surround the town?",a="Blackrock orcs hold Stonewatch Keep to the east, Shadowhide gnolls under rogue sorcerer Morganth strike from the northern hills, and aggressive murlocs infest Lake Everstill's waters and banks.",al={"who is attacking lakeshire","redridge threats","lakeshire enemies"},it="threat"},{q="What is Lakeshire?",a="Lakeshire is the primary human settlement in the Redridge Mountains, built along the scenic shores of Lake Everstill. Serving as an outpost of the Kingdom of Stormwind, it provides a community for local tradesfolk, fishermen, and laborers. The town features a civic town hall, an inn for travelers, stables, and a prominent stone bridge spanning the lake, acting as the vital hub of civilization in an increasingly beleaguered region.",al={"what is lakeshire","where is lakeshire","lakeshire town"},it="place",add="4f49b93e"},{q="What happened at Lakeshire?",a="Lakeshire suffered in the wars against the Horde and was rebuilt in the years that followed. In recent days, the town has come under relentless siege once more from Blackrock orcs, Shadowhide gnolls, and hostile murlocs along the lake.",al={"lakeshire history","first war lakeshire","what happened to lakeshire"},it="history",add="cfd70950"},{q="Is Lakeshire dangerous?",a="While the town center remains guarded by Marshal Marris and the local Stormwind Guard, the surrounding area is exceptionally perilous. Blackrock orcs launch frequent raids, having overrun Stonewatch Keep and broken the Everstill Bridge. Just beyond the perimeter, savage Redridge gnolls, dark-magic-infused Shadowhide gnolls, and aggressive murlocs on the lake shore constantly threaten to overwhelm the defenders.",al={"how dangerous is lakeshire","is it safe in lakeshire","lakeshire danger"},it="danger",add="7f095f38"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Lakeshire guards Stormwind's eastern border. If the Blackrock clan takes the town, orcs could reach Elwynn's heartlands directly.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you can see Lakeshire's hard-won resilience. Rebuilt after the wars against the Horde, it gives Stormwind refugees who refuse to flee their homeland again a place to stand."},kw={"blackrock orcs","everstill bridge","lake everstill","lakeshire","magistrate solomon","marshal marris","redridge","stonewatch"},rel={"zone:redridge","subzone:lake-everstill","npc:magistrate-solomon","npc:marshal-marris","npc:foreman-oslow","quest:89","subzone:stonewatch","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Lakeshire"}}
E["subzone:lakeshire-inn"] = {t="subzone",n="Lakeshire Inn",z="redridge",s="At Lakeshire Inn, travelers and townsfolk seek shelter as danger closes around Lakeshire. On Lake Everstill, the inn offers food, drink, and a place to hear news amid the town’s troubles.",h="At Lakeshire Inn, travelers and townsfolk seek shelter as danger closes around Lakeshire.",sec={{t="A Beacon of Warmth",b="On the shore of Lake Everstill, Lakeshire Inn offers a short rest from the gnoll bands and Blackrock orcs pressing against the town. Though Lakeshire’s military position grows more desperate, the tavern remains warm and welcoming. Barkeep Daniels and Innkeeper Brianna serve ale, wine, and hot meals to locals and travelers. Townspeople gather to trade news, ease their sorrows, and seek hired blades to defend the kingdom’s eastern border.",sp=0},{t="Patrons and Whispers",b="Wiley the Black watches the room from a table, keeping his thoughts to himself and an eye on dangers in the region. Traveling brewers such as Yorus Barleybrew stop at the inn, and Darcy Parker and other townsfolk visit the common room. For those bound for the jagged peaks or south toward Duskwood, Lakeshire Inn is the last safe haven before the contested wilderness.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What services does the Lakeshire Inn provide?",a="Innkeeper Brianna binds hearthstones and rents rooms, while Barkeep Daniels provides food, drink, and refreshments for the road.",al={"lakeshire inn services","what can I do at lakeshire inn","innkeeper lakeshire"},it="purpose"},{q="Why is the inn so crowded despite the nearby attacks?",a="Blackrock orcs descend from the northern crags, and gnolls raid local farms, driving townspeople and displaced settlers toward safety in the town center. The tavern offers shelter and a place to share news of the defense.",al={"why is lakeshire inn full","lakeshire refugees inn","redridge tavern crowd"},it="conflict"},{q="Who is Wiley the Black?",a="Wiley the Black is a human rogue who keeps to himself inside the inn. Gryan Stoutmantle of Westfall once saved his life, and Wiley repays him by sharing what he knows about the Defias Brotherhood with adventurers Gryan sends his way.",al={"wiley the black","guy in lakeshire tavern","wiley npc"},it="people"},{q="Where is the inn located within Lakeshire?",a="The inn sits near Lakeshire’s western entrance, on the northern bank of Lake Everstill and just off the main road from Elwynn Forest.",al={"where is lakeshire inn","lakeshire tavern location","find lakeshire inn"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is Lakeshire Inn?",a="The Lakeshire Inn is the social heart and refuge of Lakeshire in the Redridge Mountains. Despite the ongoing incursions of Blackrock orcs and gnolls pressing into the region, the establishment maintains a warm and lively atmosphere. It serves as a central tavern and shelter where travelers, locals, and weary defenders gather to share news, drink ale and wine, and secure a safe bed.",al={"what is lakeshire inn","lakeshire inn","about lakeshire inn"},it="place",add="4b6fa18d"},{q="Who runs the Lakeshire Inn?",a="Innkeeper Brianna oversees the day-to-day hospitality and accommodations of the inn, while Barkeep Daniels and Bartender Wental attend the tavern counters, pouring wine and ale for patrons. The common room is typically populated by local townspeople, travelers, and notable regulars such as Wiley the Black.",al={"who runs lakeshire inn","lakeshire innkeeper","who works at lakeshire inn"},it="residents",add="13161e3b"},{q="Is Lakeshire Inn dangerous?",a="Within its walls, the inn offers shelter and bedrest to travelers. The surrounding town of Lakeshire remains under persistent threat from gnolls and Blackrock orc warbands.",al={"is lakeshire inn safe","danger at lakeshire inn","lakeshire inn danger"},it="danger",add="583be7e3"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you can use Lakeshire Inn as a base while helping defend Stormwind’s vulnerable eastern flank.",["profession:Cooking"]="You can find cooking staples, local recipes, and fresh drink from Barkeep Daniels in the common room."},kw={"barkeep daniels","darcy parker","innkeeper brianna","lake everstill","lakeshire inn","redridge inn","wiley the black","yorus barleybrew"},rel={"subzone:lakeshire","zone:redridge","npc:wiley-the-black","npc:barkeep-daniels","npc:darcy-parker","quest:1698","subzone:three-corners"},src={"Lakeshire Inn"}}
E["subzone:lakeshire-town-hall"] = {t="subzone",n="Lakeshire Town Hall",z="redridge",s="At Lakeshire Town Hall, Magistrate Solomon directs Redridge's affairs from the heart of Lakeshire. Blackrock orcs and gnolls bring relentless threats to the lakeside settlement.",h="At Lakeshire Town Hall, Magistrate Solomon directs Redridge's affairs from the heart of Lakeshire.",sec={{t="Seat of Redridge Governance",b="Lakeshire Town Hall, an aging stone building, has been refurbished many times over the years. It stands prominently in Lakeshire and houses Magistrate Solomon, a kind and dedicated civil leader who maintains order in the eastern reaches of the Kingdom of Stormwind. Stormwind's military is stretched thin, and royal aid is scarce. The hall has changed from a quiet administrative office into an active command center, where desperate appeals for volunteer defenders and mercenaries are processed daily.",sp=0},{t="Under Siege and Overwhelmed",b="Gnoll incursions and the encroaching Blackrock orcs have driven Magistrate Solomon to desperation. With aid scarce, he readily accepts help from independent adventurers who come through the town hall doors.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is in charge at Lakeshire Town Hall?",a="Magistrate Solomon oversees Lakeshire Town Hall. He is a kind, well-meaning administrator who governs Lakeshire and the surrounding Redridge valley.",al={"who leads lakeshire","magistrate solomon","who is in town hall"},it="in_charge"},{q="Why is the town hall seeking so much outside help?",a="Lakeshire faces severe, mounting threats from local gnoll packs and hostile Blackrock orc warbands. Stormwind has provided minimal military reinforcements, so Magistrate Solomon must hire passing adventurers to defend the region.",al={"why does solomon need help","lakeshire problems","why are there so many quests here"},it="motive"},{q="Why does Solomon accept help from travelers?",a="Gnoll incursions and the encroaching Blackrock orcs have left Magistrate Solomon desperate. He readily accepts help from independent adventurers who come through the town hall doors.",al={"why does solomon accept aid","lakeshire adventurers","town hall help"}},{q="Has Lakeshire Town Hall stood for a long time?",a="Yes. The aging building has survived turbulent decades and undergone diligent repairs and refurbishments to keep it functioning as Redridge's civic center.",al={"town hall age","how old is lakeshire town hall","town hall history"},it="history"},{q="What is Lakeshire Town Hall?",a="Lakeshire Town Hall is the seat of local governance for the town of Lakeshire and the surrounding Redridge Mountains. It serves as both the administrative center of the settlement and the official residence and office of Magistrate Solomon, where civic matters are managed and beleaguered citizens bring their grievances.",al={"what is lakeshire town hall","town hall lakeshire purpose","about lakeshire town hall"},it="place",add="21ea7658"},{q="Is Lakeshire Town Hall dangerous?",a="No, Lakeshire Town Hall is a safe haven for members of the Alliance. It sits securely within the heart of Lakeshire, guarded by local sentries while Magistrate Solomon and concerned townsfolk organize the defense of the region. However, Horde trespassers will find themselves attacked on sight by the town guards.",al={"is lakeshire town hall safe","is it dangerous in lakeshire town hall","lakeshire town hall danger"},it="danger",add="87431e4d"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, Lakeshire Town Hall marks the eastern frontier in Redridge, a beleaguered outpost holding the line without royal support from Stormwind.",["race:Human"]="As a human of Stormwind, you see in this refurbished hall the enduring spirit of rural settlements and the frustration regional administrators feel when the capital turns a blind eye."},kw={"blackrock","gnolls","lakeshire","magistrate solomon","redridge","redridge mountains","stormwind","town hall"},rel={"subzone:lakeshire","zone:redridge","topic:gnoll"},src={"Lakeshire Town Hall"}}
E["subzone:render-s-rock"] = {t="subzone",n="Render's Rock",z="redridge",s="Blackrock orcs hold Render's Rock above Redridge, near the pass to the Burning Steppes. From this cave, they prepare attacks on the valleys below.",h="Blackrock orcs hold Render's Rock above Redridge, near the pass to the Burning Steppes.",sec={{t="A Blackrock Bastion in the Heights",b="North of Lakeshire, Blackrock orcs guard a cave cut into the Redridge heights. The stronghold lies near the mountain pass leading to the Burning Steppes, where veteran orcs direct attacks against Redridge's defenders. Their guards make any attempt to enter perilous, whether to disrupt the orcs' supply lines or recover captives lost in the fighting.",sp=0},{t="A Hostage in the Shadows",b="Corporal Keeshan, a wounded Redridge soldier, is held inside Render's Rock. Isolated deep behind enemy lines, he is far from his companions. His captivity shows how boldly the Blackrock orcs press their attacks, and what the local garrison has paid to keep the mountain road open.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is Render's Rock located?",a="Render's Rock lies in the northwestern peaks of the Redridge Mountains, near the path north into the Burning Steppes.",al={"renders rock location","where is renders rock","find renders rock"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who controls Render's Rock?",a="Blackrock orcs control Render's Rock and use the crag as a redoubt to coordinate attacks and watch the mountain passes by the Burning Steppes.",al={"who lives in renders rock","renders rock enemies","who holds renders rock"},it="residents"},{q="Who is imprisoned inside the cave?",a="Corporal Keeshan, a wounded veteran of the Alliance garrison, is held captive inside Render's Rock and needs help escaping to Lakeshire.",al={"keeshan location","captive in renders rock","who is trapped in renders rock"}},{q="Why is this cave important to Lakeshire's defense?",a="Experienced Blackrock warriors hold Render's Rock above the Redridge valley, threatening Lakeshire and giving the orcs a foothold south of the Burning Steppes.",al={"why attack renders rock","renders rock threat","importance of renders rock"},it="purpose"},{q="What is Render's Rock?",a="Render's Rock is a vast, foreboding cavern carved into the craggy mountains of northwestern Redridge, right near the pass leading north toward the Burning Steppes. Rather than a mere natural den, it serves as a fortified stronghold and gathering point for the hostile Blackrock clan encroaching from the north.",al={"what is renders rock","renders rock cave","tell me about renders rock"},it="place",add="4e201338"},{q="Is Render's Rock dangerous?",a="It is exceptionally dangerous. The caverns crawl with hardened Blackrock orc veterans and raiders who have fortified deep within the stone. Unprepared travelers stepping inside risk being overwhelmed immediately by disciplined, battle-ready warriors defending their outpost.",al={"is renders rock safe","how dangerous is renders rock","renders rock threats"},it="danger",add="a0be54e2"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance fighter, you face one of Redridge's most entrenched Blackrock positions at Render's Rock. Clearing it can free Corporal Keeshan and protect Lakeshire."},kw={"blackrock orcs","burning steppes","corporal keeshan","keeshan","redridge","render's rock","renders rock"},rel={"zone:redridge","subzone:lakeshire","zone:burningsteppes"},src={"Render's Rock"}}
E["subzone:render-s-valley"] = {t="subzone",n="Render's Valley",z="redridge",s="Blackrock orcs hold a small camp in the southeastern Redridge Mountains at Render's Valley. It threatens nearby travelers and keeps captives taken from surrounding lands.",h="Blackrock orcs hold a small camp in the southeastern Redridge Mountains at Render's Valley.",sec={{t="A Foothold in the Southeast",b="Render's Valley lies among rocky ridges southeast of Lake Everstill, where Blackrock orcs keep an auxiliary camp for their operations in Redridge. Unlike the fortified keeps and stone towers on the northern cliffs, this camp gathers around war tents, banners, and sentry posts. Its warriors are smaller in number and less armed than the clan's core forces, but they still raid local roads and harass travelers. Captured prisoners remain in crude cages under guard.",sp=0},{t="Secret Paths and Captives",b="Scouts who reach Render's Valley find unexpected points of interest beyond the war parties roaming its dirt paths. Human prisoners have been seen in the camp, including a servant connected to the Tower of Azora who traded specialist goods under his captors' noses. Unmarked paths cross the high southern bluffs behind the valley, letting daring travelers slip into the murky bogs of the Swamp of Sorrows.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who controls Render's Valley?",a="The aggressive Blackrock clan occupies Render's Valley. Its orcs have pushed south from the Burning Steppes into Redridge to conquer territory and harass human settlements.",al={"who is in renders valley","renders valley orcs","what clan is in renders valley"},it="residents"},{q="Are the orcs here as dangerous as the ones at Stonewatch?",a="No. The Blackrock warriors in Render's Valley are generally younger or less formidable skirmishers than the hardened elite forces at Stonewatch Keep to the north.",al={"renders valley difficulty","how strong are the orcs here"},it="danger"},{q="Who is the prisoner kept in the camp?",a="A servant affiliated with the Tower of Azora in Elwynn Forest is held in a cage after being captured by the Blackrock clan. Those who reach him can acquire specialized tailoring supplies.",al={"renders valley captive","servant of azora redridge","renders valley tailor"}},{q="Can you reach the Swamp of Sorrows from here?",a="Yes. An unofficial mountain trail crosses the southern bluffs just past Render's Valley and leads into the northern marches of the Swamp of Sorrows.",al={"path to swamp of sorrows","renders valley mountain pass","redridge to swamp shortcut"},gp=true},{q="What is Render's Valley?",a="Render's Valley is a rugged ravine in the southeastern reaches of the Redridge Mountains. The Blackrock orcs have established an entrenched encampment here, extending their menacing reach across the eastern wilderness. While not as fortified as their stronghold at Stonewatch Keep further north, it serves as a critical foothold for the clan's operations against Lakeshire and the Kingdom of Stormwind.",al={"what is renders valley","renders valley lore","where is renders valley"},it="place",add="5cb67798"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Render's Valley is a secondary Blackrock raiding outpost threatening southern Redridge. Clearing it helps secure trade and travel in Lakeshire.",["profession:Tailoring"]="The Captured Servant of Azora offers unique tailoring patterns and materials. Craftsmen must fight through the sentries to reach him."},kw={"blackrock orcs","redridge","render's valley","renders valley","servant of azora","swamp of sorrows pass"},rel={"zone:redridge","zone:swampofsorrows"},src={"Render's Valley"}}
E["subzone:rethban-caverns"] = {t="subzone",n="Rethban Caverns",z="redridge",s="Rethban Caverns wind through the northwestern cliffs of the Redridge Mountains. Aggressive Redridge gnolls infest this extensive cave system, the only source of uncommon Rethban ore.",h="Rethban Caverns wind through the northwestern cliffs of the Redridge Mountains.",sec={{t="A Gnoll Warren",b="Deep in the northwestern mountains above Lake Everstill, Rethban Caverns shelter the local gnolls as a fortified redoubt. Their cunning leader, Ardo Dirtpaw, commands a pack that fiercely guards the twisting passages and chambers below. Wanderers who stray too close to the hillside entrance face attack.",sp=0},{t="The Veins of Rethban",b="Rethban ore is a distinct mineral found in these winding, dangerous tunnels and carried by the Dirtpaw pack. Blacksmiths and researchers in Lakeshire often send travelers into the caverns to recover samples of this rare mountain ore.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where are Rethban Caverns located?",a="Rethban Caverns lie along the jagged bluffs in northwestern Redridge, north of the main road toward Lakeshire.",al={"rethban caverns location","where is rethban","how to find rethban caverns"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What creatures dwell inside Rethban Caverns?",a="Redridge gnolls of the Dirtpaw clan dwell in the tunnels, led by their cunning chieftain, Ardo Dirtpaw.",al={"rethban mobs","who lives in rethban caverns","rethban enemies"},it="residents"},{q="Why do adventurers venture into the caverns?",a="Travelers and townsfolk from Lakeshire seek uncommon Rethban ore, a mineral vein deep in the caves and held by the gnolls who live there.",al={"rethban cavern quests","why go to rethban caverns","rethban ore quest"},it="purpose"},{q="What is Rethban Caverns?",a="Rethban Caverns is an extensive cave system winding deep into the northwestern mountains of Redridge. Though natural subterranean tunnels, they have become an entrenched den for local gnolls who mine and guard the rare Rethban ore found inside.",al={"what is rethban caverns","about rethban caverns","rethban cave lore"},it="place",add="b8930d83"},{q="Is Rethban Caverns dangerous?",a="Yes, it is extremely hazardous. The caves are tightly packed with aggressive gnolls under the command of their cunning leader, Ardo Dirtpaw. Anyone venturing into the subterranean depths risks being quickly swarmed and trapped in the dark.",al={"is rethban caverns dangerous","danger in rethban","how dangerous is rethban caverns"},it="danger",add="206356ed"}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="Rethban Caverns yield Rethban ore, a mineral deposit the local gnoll tribes fiercely contest.",["faction:Alliance"]="The aggressive gnoll pack entrenched in Rethban Caverns threatens travelers in northern Redridge, so Lakeshire's defenders must keep the bluffs secure."},kw={"ardo dirtpaw","dirtpaw","gnolls","lakeshire","redridge","rethban","rethban caverns","rethban ore"},rel={"quest:347","zone:redridge","topic:gnoll"},src={"Rethban Caverns"}}
E["subzone:stonewatch"] = {t="subzone",n="Stonewatch",z="redridge",s="Blackrock orcs hold Stonewatch above the approaches from the Burning Steppes, threatening Lakeshire. The fortress once guarded Redridge against northern invasions.",h="Blackrock orcs hold Stonewatch above the approaches from the Burning Steppes, threatening Lakeshire.",sec={{t="A Bastion Overrun",b="Stonewatch overlooks the cliffs near Stonewatch Falls, where its tower and keep guard the approaches from the Burning Steppes. Lakeshire's defenders first held the fortress. Then Morganth, a rogue warlock, allied with the Blackrock clan. Dark magic helped the orcs overwhelm the 12th Sabre Regiment and seize the keep. Morganth later turned against his allies and withdrew to the nearby Tower of Ilgalar with an army of Shadowhide gnolls. The Blackrock orcs kept their hold under Warlord Gath'Ilzogg and Lieutenant Tharil'zun.",sp=0},{t="The Threat to Lakeshire",b="Blackrock orcs hold Stonewatch, leaving Lakeshire exposed to conquest. Stormwind's House of Nobles has provided no substantial military reinforcements, whether through indifference or paralysis. Magistrate Solomon and Marshal Marris have had to hire mercenaries and call for volunteers. Their best hope of lifting the threat over the region is to strike at the fortress's leaders, Tharil'zun and Gath'Ilzogg.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who controls Stonewatch right now?",a="The Blackrock clan holds Stonewatch under Warlord Gath'Ilzogg and his lieutenant, Tharil'zun. They drove out the kingdom's garrison and use the stronghold to stage attacks across Redridge.",al={"who is in stonewatch","who holds stonewatch","stonewatch enemies"},it="in_charge"},{q="How did the humans lose Stonewatch?",a="Blackrock orcs, aided by the dark sorcery of the rogue human warlock Morganth, invaded and overwhelmed the 12th Sabre Regiment. The defenders fell, and the orcs took the fortress.",al={"fall of stonewatch","how did stonewatch fall","stonewatch backstory"},it="history"},{q="Why isn't Stormwind sending an army to take it back?",a="Stormwind has not sent enough troops to the border regions, leaving Magistrate Solomon and Marshal Marris to defend Redridge. Lakeshire depends on visiting adventurers and mercenaries for counterattacks against Stonewatch.",al={"why no stormwind help","lakeshire reinforcements"},it="conflict"},{q="What is the relationship between Stonewatch and the Tower of Ilgalar?",a="Morganth helped the Blackrock orcs seize Stonewatch, then betrayed them soon after their victory. He built the nearby Tower of Ilgalar and gathered magical thralls and Shadowhide gnolls there, attacking both orcs and humans.",al={"tower of ilgalar connection","morganth stonewatch"},it="ties"},{q="What is Stonewatch?",a="Stonewatch is a fortified military stronghold situated in central Redridge Mountains, built high above the cascading Stonewatch Falls. Constructed by the humans of Lakeshire to serve as a vital defensive bastion against orc incursions spilling from the Burning Steppes, it consists of both the formidable Stonewatch Keep and an armored watchtower overlooking the surrounding valleys.",al={"what is stonewatch","stonewatch keep overview","tell me about stonewatch"},it="place",add="5eefcf97"},{q="Is Stonewatch dangerous?",a="Stonewatch is one of the most perilous regions in Redridge. Heavily fortified and swarming with disciplined Blackrock orc invaders, it serves as a central staging ground for their raids on the surrounding valley. Intruders will face battle-hardened grunts, sentries, and warlocks loyal to Warlord Gath'Ilzogg, making any assault a deadly undertaking.",al={"how dangerous is stonewatch","stonewatch threat","is stonewatch safe"},it="danger",add="ae6d9597"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, Stonewatch is one of the most dangerous hostile orc positions inside Alliance lands. Taking it back is vital to Redridge's safety.",["race:Human"]="As a human, the slaughter of the 12th Sabre Regiment and the fall of Stonewatch show how vulnerable Lakeshire is and how little help Stormwind's leaders have given it."},kw={"blackrock orcs","gath'ilzogg","lakeshire","morganth","redridge","stonewatch","stonewatch keep","tharil'zun"},rel={"subzone:stonewatch-keep","subzone:stonewatch-tower","subzone:stonewatch-falls","subzone:lakeshire","zone:redridge","subzone:tower-of-ilgalar","quest:169","quest:19"},src={"Stonewatch"}}
E["subzone:stonewatch-falls"] = {t="subzone",n="Stonewatch Falls",z="redridge",s="At Stonewatch Falls, water pours from Lake Everstill into a pool claimed by murlocs. The falls lie beneath Stonewatch in the eastern Redridge Mountains.",h="At Stonewatch Falls, water pours from Lake Everstill into a pool claimed by murlocs.",sec={{t="A Perilous Mountain Basin",b="Stonewatch Falls rushes down the slope beneath Stonewatch, the Blackrock orc stronghold. Its water flows from Lake Everstill’s eastern river and gathers in a deep pool against the mountainside. Murlocs have claimed the shore, raising crude reed hovels and preying on travelers who come too close to the water.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does the water from Stonewatch Falls come from?",a="Stonewatch Falls begins at the river flowing from Lake Everstill’s eastern side, then tumbles downhill into a mountain basin beneath Stonewatch’s cliffs.",al={"where does stonewatch falls start","falls water source","stonewatch river source"}},{q="What creatures live around Stonewatch Falls?",a="A tribe of murlocs occupies the shore. They feed on fish from the deep pool and build rough shelters along its banks.",al={"what is at stonewatch falls","murlocs at stonewatch falls","mobs near falls"},it="residents"},{q="Is Stonewatch Falls connected to Stonewatch Keep?",a="Stonewatch Falls lies below Stonewatch and its ruined keep. Blackrock orcs hold the heights, while murlocs occupy the basin below.",al={"falls connection to keep","is stonewatch keep near the falls","stonewatch relationship"}},{q="What is Stonewatch Falls?",a="Stonewatch Falls is a scenic waterfall situated at the terminus of Lake Everstill's eastern river. Tumbling down the hills right beneath Stonewatch Keep, the cascading water gathers into a deep, secluded mountain lake nestled in the rocky eastern heights of Redridge.",al={"stonewatch falls lore","what is this place","where is stonewatch falls"},it="place",add="ffdc928b"},{q="Is Stonewatch Falls dangerous?",a="Yes, travelers should tread carefully. A hostile tribe of murlocs infests the pool and its banks, having built crude hovels along the shore. Between these territorial shore-crawlers and the shadow of the Blackrock orcs occupying Stonewatch Keep above, the waters are far from peaceful.",al={"stonewatch falls danger","is it safe here","threats at stonewatch falls"},it="danger",add="763cc7e3"},{q="Why is it called Stonewatch Falls?",a="The waterfall takes its name directly from Stonewatch Keep, the formidable fortress that looms on the heights just above it. The waters cascade straight down the hillside below the stronghold.",al={"stonewatch falls name origin","why is it named stonewatch falls"},it="name",add="7a8101a7"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, the murlocs at Stonewatch Falls are another danger to travelers in eastern Redridge, already troubled by threats."},kw={"lake everstill","murlocs","redridge","stonewatch","stonewatch falls","waterfall"},rel={"zone:redridge","subzone:lake-everstill","subzone:stonewatch","subzone:stonewatch-keep","topic:murloc"},src={"Stonewatch Falls"}}
E["subzone:stonewatch-keep"] = {t="subzone",n="Stonewatch Keep",z="redridge",s="Blackrock orcs hold Stonewatch Keep in eastern Redridge Mountains, turning it against Lakeshire. The Kingdom of Stormwind built and manned the fortress before the invaders seized it as a base for their warlords.",h="Blackrock orcs hold Stonewatch Keep in eastern Redridge Mountains, turning it against Lakeshire.",sec={{t="A Fallen Bastion",b="Stonewatch Keep once guarded the eastern ridges and the settlers of Lakeshire from hostile incursions. That changed when the renegade warlock Morganth allied with the Blackrock clan. Strengthened by dark magic, the orcs stormed the fortress and overcame its human defenders. After their victory, Morganth abandoned the Blackrock clan to raise the nearby Tower of Ilgalar and subjugate local gnolls. The invaders kept Stonewatch, turning a former Alliance bastion into a staging ground for assaults on the valley.",sp=0},{t="The Warlord's Seat",b="A heavy garrison of Blackrock warriors holds Stonewatch Keep under the command of the orc warlord Gath'Ilzogg and his lieutenant, Tharil'zun. From the ramparts, they direct raids across Redridge and take prisoners, including Stormwind's Corporal Keeshan. Stormwind's forces are spread thin, leaving the kingdom unable to send a full regiment to reclaim the fortress. Magistrate Solomon and Marshal Marris have hired mercenary champions to enter the stronghold and kill the Blackrock leaders before Lakeshire is overrun.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who owns Stonewatch Keep right now?",a="The Blackrock clan holds Stonewatch Keep under Warlord Gath'Ilzogg and his lieutenant, Tharil'zun. The fortress once belonged to the Alliance and protected Lakeshire before its capture.",al={"who controls stonewatch keep","who lives in stonewatch keep","stonewatch keep enemies"},it="residents"},{q="How did the Blackrock orcs capture the keep?",a="Morganth, a renegade human warlock, allied with the Blackrock clan. His dark magic strengthened the orcs as they stormed Stonewatch and overwhelmed its human defenders.",al={"how did orcs get stonewatch","fall of stonewatch keep","why did stonewatch fall"},it="history"},{q="Why doesn't the Stormwind Army retake Stonewatch Keep?",a="Internal politics and troop shortages across the kingdom have left Redridge largely neglected by Stormwind's army. Lakeshire's leaders must rely on independent adventurers to face the threat.",al={"why no stormwind army","where are the guards","lakeshire army help"},it="threat"},{q="What is Morganth's connection to this fortress?",a="Morganth helped the Blackrock clan capture Stonewatch Keep, then abandoned them after their victory. He went to the nearby Tower of Ilgalar, where he raised his lair and used ensorcelled Shadowhide gnolls to do his bidding.",al={"morganth stonewatch","is morganth inside stonewatch keep"},it="ties"},{q="What is Stonewatch Keep?",a="Stonewatch Keep is a massive stone fortress overlooking northeastern Redridge Mountains. Originally built and garrisoned by the humans of Lakeshire to guard the mountain passes, it once anchored the eastern defenses of the kingdom. Today, it stands as the fortified stronghold of the invading Blackrock orcs, who seized it through dark sorcery and brutal force.",al={"what is stonewatch","stonewatch keep overview","what is this place"},it="place",add="2fd36daf"},{q="Is Stonewatch Keep dangerous?",a="It is one of the most perilous strongholds in Redridge Mountains. Heavily fortified and swarming with disciplined Blackrock orcs, the keep is overseen by Warlord Gath'Ilzogg and his trusted lieutenant, Tharil'zun. Wandering into its courtyards alone is lethal; taking it on requires seasoned adventurers ready for relentless, brutal combat.",al={"how dangerous is stonewatch","is stonewatch keep safe","danger of stonewatch keep"},it="danger",add="9c4dac94"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, Stonewatch Keep recalls Stormwind's strained borders. Its ramparts must be cleared to protect Lakeshire's vulnerable townsfolk.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you can honor the defenders who shed blood at Stonewatch by helping free the keep and avenge the soldiers and captives taken by the Blackrock clan."},kw={"blackrock clan","gath'ilzogg","keeshan","lakeshire","morganth","redridge mountains","stonewatch keep","tharil'zun"},rel={"subzone:stonewatch","subzone:stonewatch-tower","quest:169","quest:19","subzone:tower-of-ilgalar","subzone:lakeshire","npc:marshal-marris","npc:magistrate-solomon"},src={"Stonewatch Keep"}}
E["subzone:stonewatch-tower"] = {t="subzone",n="Stonewatch Tower",z="redridge",s="Blackrock sentinels hold Stonewatch Tower in northeastern Redridge. Once Lakeshire's outpost, it now helps the clan watch the ridges and guard its mountain stronghold.",h="Blackrock sentinels hold Stonewatch Tower in northeastern Redridge.",sec={{t="A Fallen Watchpost",b="Stonewatch Tower rises above Lake Everstill, guarding the high mountain passes. The Kingdom of Stormwind built it as a forward scout for Stonewatch Keep. From its heights, sentries watched the eastern ridges and warned Lakeshire of threats coming from the Burning Steppes. Warlord Gath'Ilzogg's Blackrock orcs swept down from the heights, overcame the human defenders, and seized the stronghold for their war effort. Blackrock sentinels now watch the tower, keeping Alliance scouts from reaching the fortress unnoticed.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Stonewatch Tower?",a="Stonewatch Tower is a human watchtower within the larger Stonewatch complex in northeastern Redridge Mountains. Built to protect the region, it is now held by the Blackrock clan.",al={"stonewatch tower lore","what is this tower","stonewatch lookout"},it="place"},{q="Who controls Stonewatch Tower right now?",a="Blackrock orcs serving Warlord Gath'Ilzogg control Stonewatch Tower. They captured the stronghold from Redridge's human defenders.",al={"who owns stonewatch tower","who is in stonewatch tower","stonewatch tower enemies"},it="residents"},{q="Why is the tower important to the Blackrock orcs?",a="Its height lets the Blackrock clan spot approaching Alliance forces and guard the approach to Stonewatch Keep, their main fortress.",al={"why do orcs want stonewatch tower","strategic importance of stonewatch tower"},it="purpose"},{q="Can Lakeshire reclaim the tower?",a="Lakeshire lacks the soldiers to retake Stonewatch alone. You can help weaken the Blackrock garrison holding the tower and keep.",al={"will lakeshire take it back","lakeshire plans for stonewatch tower"},it="conflict"},{q="What happened at Stonewatch Tower?",a="Originally built by the humans of Lakeshire as part of the greater Stonewatch stronghold, this scout tower once guarded the eastern reaches of Redridge. However, the defenders were overrun when the Blackrock orcs pushed into the region. Under Warlord Gath'Ilzogg's command, the orcs captured both the tower and the adjoining keep, turning Lakeshire's former vantage point against the kingdom.",al={"stonewatch tower history","what happened to stonewatch tower","how did orcs take stonewatch tower"},it="history",add="84e56e26"},{q="Is Stonewatch Tower dangerous?",a="Extremely dangerous. The tower is heavily garrisoned by the Blackrock clan, serving as an entrenched forward watchpost right in the shadow of Stonewatch Keep. Any traveler approaching without heavy reinforcement will quickly find themselves swarmed by seasoned orcish warriors under orders from Gath'Ilzogg.",al={"stonewatch tower danger","how dangerous is stonewatch tower","is stonewatch tower safe"},it="danger",add="7b29287c"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you see how far the Blackrock clan has pushed into Stormwind territory while the kingdom's central army remains absent.",["race:Human"]="As a human from Lakeshire, you know the orcish standards above Stonewatch's towers threaten your people's survival."},kw={"blackrock clan","gath'ilzogg","lakeshire","redridge","scout tower","stonewatch","stonewatch tower"},rel={"subzone:stonewatch","subzone:stonewatch-keep","subzone:lakeshire","topic:blackrock-clan","zone:redridge"},src={"Stonewatch Tower"}}
E["subzone:three-corners"] = {t="subzone",n="Three Corners",z="redridge",s="At Three Corners, roads meet at the western edge of the Redridge Mountains. The routes link Goldshire, Lakeshire, and Darkshire, while Stormwind guards watch for gnolls threatening travelers and supply wagons.",h="At Three Corners, roads meet at the western edge of the Redridge Mountains.",sec={{t="A Crossroads of Three Shires",b="At Three Corners, three roads link the southern settlements of Stormwind. Goldshire lies west in Elwynn Forest, Lakeshire northeast in Redridge, and Darkshire south in Duskwood. Stormwind built Tower Watch at the junction, where guards and scouts try to keep the roads clear. Gnolls from Redridge threaten travelers and supply wagons moving between the regions.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is this place called Three Corners?",a="Three roads lead from the crossroads toward Goldshire in Elwynn Forest, Lakeshire in Redridge, and Darkshire in Duskwood. Together, these are the Three Shires of southern Stormwind.",al={"three corners name meaning","why three corners","three corners history"},it="name"},{q="Who guards the tower at Three Corners?",a="Members of the Stormwind Guard man Tower Watch. The post warns of danger and helps defend against gnolls coming down from the Redridge peaks toward the Elwynn border.",al={"who controls three corners","tower watch guards","who is in the tower"},it="in_charge"},{q="What threats are active around Three Corners?",a="Gnolls from the surrounding hills prowl the roads and ambush travelers and couriers. Guards call on passing adventurers to thin the packs and keep the roads passable.",al={"three corners monsters","dangers at three corners","three corners gnolls"},it="threat"},{q="What is Three Corners?",a="Three Corners is a vital crossroads sitting just inside the southwestern border of the Redridge Mountains. Three highways branch from this central junction toward the three major regional settlements: Goldshire in Elwynn Forest, Lakeshire here in Redridge, and Darkshire down in Duskwood. Guarding the center of this vital intersection is Tower Watch, a fortified scout post manned by the Stormwind Guard.",al={"what is this place","where is three corners","three corners overview"},it="place",add="36588b3d"},{q="Is Three Corners dangerous?",a="While the crossroads itself is shielded by the Stormwind sentries stationed at Tower Watch, the immediate surrounding hills and trails are teeming with peril. Local gnoll packs relentlessly roam the brush and ambush unwary travelers along the roads. Anyone passing through is strongly urged to stay near the garrison's watchtower rather than wandering into the wild brush alone.",al={"is three corners safe","danger at three corners","threats three corners"},it="danger",add="4545d69d"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance travelers leaving Elwynn Forest, Three Corners is the first fortified outpost. Stormwind's hold on its borderlands is stretched thin.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you pass through a junction that links the southern human heartlands. Couriers and traders travel between Elwynn, Duskwood, and Redridge."},kw={"crossroads","darkshire","gnolls","goldshire","lakeshire","redridge","three corners","tower watch"},rel={"zone:redridge","zone:elwynn","zone:duskwood","subzone:lakeshire","subzone:goldshire","subzone:darkshire","topic:stormwind-guard","topic:gnoll"},src={"Three Corners"}}
E["subzone:tower-of-ilgalar"] = {t="subzone",n="Tower of Ilgalar",z="redridge",s="In eastern Redridge, Morganth holds the Tower of Ilgalar and commands the Shadowhide gnolls. The banished sorcerer practices dark magic there, far from Stormwind.",h="In eastern Redridge, Morganth holds the Tower of Ilgalar and commands the Shadowhide gnolls.",sec={{t="A Bastion of Dark Sorcery",b="Morganth holds the Tower of Ilgalar above eastern Redridge. Cast out of Stormwind's Mage Quarter for forbidden magic, the sorcerer retreated to these rugged heights to pursue the dark arts beyond imperial interference. He rules the local Shadowhide gnoll clan, whose members guard the spire's base. Inside, conjured demonic hounds stalk the tower, and shadowy power threatens Lakeshire below.",sp=0},{t="The Rivalry with Azora",b="The Tower of Ilgalar draws comparisons to the Tower of Azora in Elwynn Forest. Who built Ilgalar remains a mystery, and the towers face one another in quiet magical opposition. In Elwynn, the archmage Theocritus watches Ilgalar through enchanted scrying devices such as the Eye of Azora. He monitors Morganth's experiments and seeks to stop the sorcerer's corruption from spreading through the kingdom.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who lives in the Tower of Ilgalar?",a="Morganth lives in the tower, ruling it with summoned demonic darkhounds and the local Shadowhide gnolls. The human sorcerer was exiled from Stormwind City for forbidden dark magic.",al={"who is in tower of ilgalar","tower of ilgalar boss","who controls the tower"},it="residents"},{q="Why did Morganth flee to Redridge?",a="Morganth fled Stormwind after the Mage Quarter cast him out for pursuing the dark arts. He withdrew to Redridge's remote crags to carry out forbidden experiments beyond the scrutiny of the realm's authorities and the Kirin Tor.",al={"why is morganth here","morganth backstory","why was morganth exiled"},it="history"},{q="What is the connection between this tower and the Tower of Azora?",a="The Tower of Ilgalar and the Tower of Azora are magical spires in southern Stormwind, seemingly mirrored in purpose. From Elwynn Forest, Theocritus uses the Eye of Azora to watch Ilgalar's upper sanctum and Morganth's dark rituals.",al={"tower of azora connection","ilgalar and azora","eye of azora redridge"},it="ties"},{q="Why are there gnolls guarding the tower?",a="Morganth used magic to subdue the local Shadowhide gnolls. They guard the tower's outer reaches and keep intruders, scouts, and the Lakeshire militia from climbing the cliffs to his sanctum.",al={"why are gnolls here","shadowhide gnolls tower","gnolls around tower"},it="allies"},{q="What is the Tower of Ilgalar?",a="The Tower of Ilgalar is a mysterious mage tower perched in the eastern heights of the Redridge Mountains. Built high above Lake Everstill, it resembles the Tower of Azora in Elwynn Forest, yet it has become a bastion of forbidden sorcery rather than lawful arcane study.",al={"what is tower of ilgalar","tower of ilgalar lore","redridge mage tower"},it="place",add="d387a688"},{q="Is the Tower of Ilgalar dangerous?",a="It is exceptionally perilous. The tower is ringed by hostile Shadowhide gnolls who obey the sorcerer within, while darkhound familiars patrol its grounds. Ascending the spiral stairs brings you face-to-face with Morganth himself, an exiled warlock wielding devastating dark magic.",al={"is tower of ilgalar dangerous","tower of ilgalar dangers","how dangerous is tower of ilgalar"},it="danger",add="30aed8f6"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, the tower warns of the dangers of forbidden dark magic. Kirin Tor veterans such as Theocritus keep watch.",["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you may find Morganth's summoned darkhounds and shadowy hexes a striking example of rogue spellcraft beyond city covens."},kw={"azora","darkhounds","ilgalar","lakeshire","morganth","redridge","shadowhide","theocritus","tower of ilgalar"},rel={"zone:redridge","npc:theocritus","subzone:tower-of-azora","subzone:mage-quarter","zone:stormwind","topic:gnoll"},src={"Tower of Ilgalar"}}
E["zone:redridge"] = {t="zone",n="Redridge Mountains",z="redridge",s="Redridge Mountains face attacks from Shadowhide gnolls and Blackrock orcs of the Dark Horde. Rushing rivers cut through wooded slopes around Lake Everstill, but Lakeshire must hold the line with help from wandering mercenaries while Stormwind’s forces are tied up by strife at home.",h="Redridge Mountains face attacks from Shadowhide gnolls and Blackrock orcs of the Dark Horde.",sec={{t="A Bastion Under Siege",b="Redridge was once among the kingdom’s most peaceful regions, supplying Stormwind with timber, freshwater fish, and crops. Now Lakeshire stays fortified against aggressive incursions. Stonewatch Keep, once a proud stronghold of the kingdom, has fallen to renegade Blackrock orcs. Their control cuts off roads and threatens to overrun the eastern valleys.",sp=0},{t="The Divided Range",b="These peaks form part of the spine running down the subcontinent of Azeroth. Centuries ago, the range stretched much farther north. Then the Dark Iron clan summoned the Firelord Ragnaros by accident, and the earth tore open to form the fiery crater of Blackrock Mountain. The cataclysm left the northern peaks severed into the ash choked Burning Steppes. Only the southern Redridge valleys remain lush and green, exposed to attacks from the slopes above.",sp=0},{t="Neglected by the Crown",b="Magistrate Solomon and Marshal Marris plead for reinforcements, but Stormwind’s regency council has left Lakeshire to fend for itself. Desperate entreaties to Sentinel Hill and Darkshire bring no help; both settlements are crippled by crises of their own. With no reinforcements in sight, local magistrates hire any capable sellsword willing to brave the Lakeridge Highway, clear the gnoll camps, and push back the danger over Lake Everstill.",sp=0},{t="The Hidden Allegiances",b="Morganth, a rogue warlock, first allied with the Blackrock orcs to seize Stonewatch Keep. He later betrayed them and bound the Shadowhide gnolls to his service from the Tower of Ilgalar. Reports recovered during the Blackrock investigation also reveal an alliance between the orcs and the black dragonflight.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why won't Stormwind send soldiers to help Lakeshire?",a="Lakeshire’s surviving royal soldiers are badly outnumbered after the loss of Stonewatch Keep. Magistrate Solomon has appealed for troops, weapons, food, and supplies, but Stormwind’s forces are stretched thin, and neighboring settlements face troubles of their own. The garrison relies on adventurers to help hold the region.",al={"why no stormwind guards","why is redridge abandoned","where is stormwind army"},it="motive"},{q="Who controls Stonewatch Keep?",a="Blackrock orcs affiliated with the Dark Horde control Stonewatch Keep. From the mountain stronghold, they threaten the eastern valleys and travel along the Lakeridge Highway. Their ties to other local threats emerge during the investigation.",al={"who is in stonewatch","stonewatch enemies","what happened to stonewatch"},it="in_charge"},{q="What threats dwell in Lake Everstill?",a="Hostile murloc tribes infest Lake Everstill and raid nearby docks and ruins. Swimmers also face predatory threshadons beneath the surface, prompting rumors of aquatic monsters in the depths.",al={"lake everstill monsters","redridge lake dangers","everstill murlocs"},it="threat"},{q="Are there any Horde outposts in Redridge?",a="Redridge has no Horde settlements, vendors, or flight paths. Horde travelers passing through are generally en route between the Burning Steppes to the north and the Swamp of Sorrows to the southeast, navigating Alliance held roads and hostile wilderness.",al={"horde towns redridge","is redridge horde or alliance","horde flight path redridge"},it="place"},{q="What is the Three Corners?",a="The Three Corners is a crossroads in southwest Redridge. It joins the Lakeridge Highway to the eastern border of Elwynn Forest and the road into Duskwood, making it a vital transit point often targeted by wandering gnolls and wild beasts.",al={"three corners","three corners crossroads","redridge intersection"},it="place"},{q="Why is the northern path to the Burning Steppes so perilous?",a="The trail north past Render’s Camp climbs straight into the Burning Steppes, a desolate volcanic wasteland ruled by powerful Blackrock orcs, fire elementals, and dragonkin. That sudden rise in danger makes the northern mountain pass one of southern Azeroth’s deadliest climbs.",al={"redridge north road","burning steppes border redridge","redridge pass north"},it="danger"},{q="What is Redridge Mountains?",a="Redridge Mountains is an elevated, picturesque region east of Elwynn Forest and south of the Burning Steppes. Known for its rushing rivers, towering elms, and the shimmering Lake Everstill, it was long considered one of the more peaceful lands in southern Azeroth. Today, its tranquil beauty is shattered by invading Blackrock orcs, violent gnolls, and hostile lake murlocs.",al={"what is redridge","redridge mountains zone","tell me about redridge"},it="place",add="85c0e73f"},{q="Is Redridge part of Stormwind's kingdom?",a="Yes, Redridge is under the protection and domain of the kingdom of Stormwind, though since the Second War its local leaders have largely governed day-to-day affairs independently. Lakeshire's Magistrate Solomon still formally petitions the Stormwind throne for defense, relying on Alliance trade and mutual loyalty even when royal troops are nowhere in sight.",al={"does redridge belong to stormwind","is redridge alliance","is lakeshire part of stormwind"},it="ties",add="5d244582"},{q="Why is there a lake in the middle of Redridge?",a="Lake Everstill naturally gathers the drainage of the surrounding mountain ranges. Its clear, serene waters once sustained Lakeshire with abundant fish and clean water, though lately it has been overrun by vicious tribes of murlocs and stalked by lurking thresher beasts beneath the surface.",al={"why lake everstill","redridge lake origin","what is the lake in redridge"},it="place",add="8563150d"},{q="What happened at Redridge Mountains?",a="Redridge was once a tranquil cradle of human farmsteads until the First War, when Warchief Blackhand and Shadow Council warlocks defeated Sir Anduin Lothar's knights and drove the humans into exile. Reclaimed and rebuilt by the Alliance after the Second War, the region has recently fallen under siege once more after Blackrock orcs pushed down from the mountains and seized Stonewatch Keep.",al={"redridge history","what happened in redridge","redridge first war"},it="history",add="8de34bfa"},{q="Is Redridge Mountains dangerous?",a="Despite its idyllic appearance, Redridge is extraordinarily perilous. Blackrock orcs control the eastern canyons and keep, Shadowhide gnolls raid the woods, and murlocs swarm the lake shores. Even the northern road borders the searing peaks of the Burning Steppes, where monstrous threats far beyond an average patrol linger just beyond the valley passes.",al={"is redridge safe","danger level redridge","how dangerous is redridge"},it="danger",add="bf444872"},{q="Why is everyone in Lakeshire so worried?",a="Lakeshire is in an active state of siege. The Blackrock orcs have captured Stonewatch Keep just across the lake, Shadowhide gnolls press the town from the hills, and murlocs infest the waterways. With the bridge broken and no reinforcements arriving from Stormwind, the townsfolk fear an all-out assault will wipe them out at any moment.",al={"why is lakeshire scared","lakeshire threat","why worry in lakeshire"},it="threat",add="1cc45818"},{q="Is Lakeshire about to fall?",a="Without outside intervention, Lakeshire's position is grim. The local town guard is vastly outnumbered by orc raiders, gnoll packs, and lakeside monsters. Their fortress at Stonewatch was easily overrun, and Lakeshire's defenders have been pushed back to the lake's western edge, barely maintaining a perimeter along the broken bridge.",al={"will lakeshire fall","is lakeshire doomed","can lakeshire survive"},it="danger",add="851f5e81"},{q="Has Stormwind sent any help to Lakeshire?",a="Lakeshire has appealed to Stormwind, Westfall, and Darkshire for help, but the neighboring settlements are consumed by their own crises. General Marcus Jonathan has also been asked for reinforcements. The royal soldiers still defending Lakeshire remain short of troops and supplies after the fall of Stonewatch Keep.",al={"did stormwind help lakeshire","stormwind aid lakeshire","has stormwind sent troops to redridge"},sp=1,it="allies",add="7ced12b0"},{q="Who's in charge around here?",a="Lakeshire is governed by Magistrate Solomon, who oversees civil matters and town affairs from the Lakeshire Town Hall. Military and defense operations fall to Marshal Marris, who directs the local guard and coordinates defensive efforts near the bridge.",al={"who leads redridge","who rules lakeshire","redridge leaders"},it="in_charge",add="3a3ab87f"},{q="Who is Magistrate Solomon?",a="Magistrate Solomon is the elected ruler of Lakeshire and head judge of the Court of Lakeshire. Aging and exhausted, he carries the burden of keeping the town fed, organized, and politically connected to the kingdom while desperately petitioning foreign and regional leaders for military relief.",al={"magistrate solomon","who is solomon","solomon redridge"},it="identity",add="1dd15680"},{q="Does Marshal Marris answer to Magistrate Solomon?",a="Yes. Solomon represents the civil authority and court of the kingdom in Lakeshire, while Marshal Marris commands the Stormwind Guard detachment stationed there. The two work together in close partnership, with Solomon managing diplomatic and municipal survival while Marris handles tactical skirmishes and troop deployments.",al={"does marris report to solomon","marshal marris solomon rank","who outranks who lakeshire"},it="ties",add="0e63cf14"},{q="Who are the Blackrock orcs and why are they in Redridge?",a="The Blackrock clan is a ruthless remnant of the Old Horde based out of Blackrock Mountain to the north. Unlike Thrall's Horde in Kalimdor, these renegades reject all peace with the Alliance. They have descended from the Burning Steppes into Redridge seeking to conquer the region, using Stonewatch Keep as a staging ground to crush Lakeshire.",al={"blackrock orcs redridge","why are orcs in redridge","who are blackrock clan redridge"},it="threat",add="7b7fd7c0"},{q="Where did the Blackrock orcs come from?",a="They marched south across the jagged northern mountain passes directly from the Burning Steppes and Blackrock Spire, their ancient fortress from the Second War. They set up forward outposts like Render's Camp before overwhelming Stonewatch Keep.",al={"where did redridge orcs come from","blackrock orcs origin","where are the orcs coming from"},it="origin",add="114fb915"},{q="Are the Blackrock orcs the same orcs from the wars?",a="Yes. They are hardened veterans and direct descendants of the First and Second War Blackrock clan who refused to surrender or follow Thrall's new shamanistic path. They retain their original bloodthirsty practices and dark magic, holding fast to their original mission to extinguish the human kingdoms.",al={"are blackrock orcs from first war","second war blackrock orcs","are these the same orcs from old wars"},it="history",add="9f02e3ae"},{q="What are the Redridge gnolls? Why are they attacking?",a="The local Shadowhide gnolls are feral, hyena-like humanoids who inhabit the Redridge hills and valleys. While naturally territorial and predatory, their current coordinated violence is driven by dark influences that have unified their scattered packs into an organized army bent on slaughtering human settlements.",al={"redridge gnolls","why do gnolls attack redridge","shadowhide gnolls"},it="threat",add="09fb7c4a"},{q="Are the gnolls working with the orcs?",a="The Shadowhide gnolls serve the rogue warlock Morganth in the Tower of Ilgalar. Their relationship with the Blackrock orcs can be investigated through reports recovered in the region.",al={"gnolls and orcs allied","do gnolls work for blackrock","are orcs and gnolls teaming up"},sp=1,it="allies",add="ba7471d2"},{q="Who is Yowler?",a="Yowler is the leader of the Redridge gnolls. Residing in the hills above Lakeshire, he rallies the pack against the town. Verner Osgood asks adventurers to defeat him and bring back his paw.",al={"who is yowler","yowler gnoll leader","yowler redridge"},it="leader",add="74e139ea"},{q="Why is the Everstill Bridge broken and why does it matter?",a="The Everstill Bridge is heavily damaged. It matters tremendously because it spans the narrow neck of Lake Everstill, serving as Lakeshire's main transportation link to the eastern shore and Stonewatch. Its destruction hinders town trade and defense while complicating any counter-attack against enemy encampments.",al={"everstill bridge broken","why bridge broken lakeshire","broken bridge redridge"},it="purpose",add="b25dfaa0"},{q="Why hasn't Stormwind repaired the Everstill Bridge?",a="Stormwind has sent no funding, supplies, or masons to assist. The responsibility has fallen entirely on local workers led by Foreman Oslow, whose repair efforts are constantly interrupted and sabotaged by murloc raids and supply losses.",al={"why hasn't bridge been repaired","stormwind bridge repair lakeshire","who is repairing the bridge"},it="motive",add="b35f81a4"},{q="Why are there black dragon whelps in Redridge?",a="Black dragon whelps have spilled down through the passes from the Burning Steppes, infesting the Lakeridge Highway and southern canyons. They prowl the rocky ridges scouting territory and preying on passersby, serving as an ominous warning that the brood of Deathwing is active nearby.",al={"dragon whelps in redridge","black dragons redridge","why whelps redridge"},it="threat",add="834d2ea2"},{q="Are the dragons working with the orcs?",a="The growing Blackrock presence and sightings of black dragon whelps alarm Lakeshire. Magistrate Solomon asks travelers to take his concerns to Highlord Bolvar Fordragon. Further investigation reveals the nature of the threat.",al={"are black dragons allied with blackrock","orcs and dragons alliance","do blackrock orcs work with dragons"},sp=1,it="allies",add="ce7dd1a7"},{q="Why is an adventurer doing all the fighting here instead of the guards?",a="Lakeshire's guards are completely pinned down defending the town's perimeter, leaving none to spare for offensive sorties. With requested reinforcements still unavailable, Magistrate Solomon and Marshal Marris have no choice but to hire traveling adventurers to push back the orcs, cull the gnolls, and secure the highway.",al={"why am i doing this redridge","why adventurers redridge","where are the guards redridge"},it="why_me",add="7d7bd3f8"},{q="Where is the Stormwind army?",a="Stormwind's forces are stretched thin. Royal soldiers remain in Lakeshire after their defeat at Stonewatch Keep, but the town's repeated requests for fresh troops and supplies have not brought the reinforcements its defenders need.",al={"where are stormwind soldiers","why no stormwind army","stormwind army location"},it="place",add="839c7682"},{q="How did I end up in Redridge Mountains?",a="You likely followed the roads east from Elwynn Forest through the Three Corners crossroads, or crossed over the river from the dark woods of Duskwood to the southwest. As a fledgling champion aiding the human lands, your travels naturally lead here once the outlying troubles around Stormwind call for sturdier hands. Lakeshire's calls for aid reach across the neighboring territories, drawing traveling adventurers up along the Lakeridge Highway into these embattled heights.",al={"how did i get here","how did i reach redridge","why did i come to redridge"},it="arrival",add="de572e98"},{q="What am I supposed to be doing in Redridge Mountains?",a="Lakeshire is in desperate straits and virtually abandoned by the crown. You are here to answer Magistrate Solomon and Marshal Marris's pleas for defense. The town is hard-pressed by rampaging Shadowhide gnolls along the roads and ferocious Blackrock orcs who have seized Stonewatch Keep. With the royal garrison outnumbered and the Everstill Bridge shattered, you must beat back the gnolls, push back the orc vanguard, and keep this peaceful lakeside haven from collapsing entirely.",al={"what am i doing here","why am i here","what is my goal in redridge","what is my mission here"},it="purpose",add="d1ce2561"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance soldier, you can hone your skills at Lakeshire, a frontline hub facing organized orcs and gnolls.",["faction:Horde"]="The Blackrock orcs entrenched in Redridge belong to the hostile Dark Horde, making them enemies of Thrall’s Horde as well as the humans in Lakeshire.",["profession:Mining"]="You can find copper, tin, and rare silver veins in the rocky crags and valleys around Lake Everstill, especially near the Rethban Caverns.",["profession:Herbalism"]="The temperate mountain slopes support Briarthorn, Bruiseweed, Mageroyal, and Swiftthistle."},kw={"blackrock orcs","lake everstill","lakeshire","magistrate solomon","marshal marris","redridge","redridge mountains","render's valley","shadowhide","stonewatch","stonewatch keep","verner osgood"},rel={"subzone:lakeshire","subzone:lake-everstill","subzone:stonewatch-keep","npc:magistrate-solomon","npc:marshal-marris","zone:burningsteppes","zone:elwynn","zone:duskwood"},m={levels="15-25"},src={"Redridge Mountains (Classic)","Redridge Mountains"}}
